{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play","id":1516734,"title":"A Mage the Awakening Chronicle in Los Angeles (Actual Play)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-29T21:58:39-07:00","id":1516734,"title":"A Mage the Awakening Chronicle in Los Angeles (Actual Play)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hello everybody. Last night my group started to play MtAw and I am so excited to finally get to run this game. I did precovid and while we had fun I didn't think I was doing the game justice back then. I've got to be a player in several games and have spent a lot more time in the community since then, not to mention seeing some actual plays on Youtube so I'm excited this time around as I think the game will be <i>much</i> closer to how I feel mage can be than last time around. Anyway, being the game just started I wanted to find a place to commerate the game and keep track of what is going on in it and this seemed like a good place to do it, so here it is.<br /> <br /> First a little background for anyone reading this that isn't me, the game is taking place in Los Angeles in March 2019. I'm using the LA setting from the 2e core and then of course adding on top of it. I did a little setting information google doc that you can look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gpdl1OKLXQeYfinxttPAu8eZeOeqp8Y6Sfrv92JK9PA/edit?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> if you are interested in that sort of thing. The game itself is biweekly, alternating with one of the players for a VtR game we are also playing set in Manhattan.<br /> <br /> There are five PCs who are not offically in a cabal at the start of the chronicle:</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eye of God - Mastigos Mysterium, at character gen Space 3/Prime 2/Mind 1 Obsession is &quot;Disocver Hallows&quot;</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Giger - Acanthus Mysterium, at character gen Time 3/Fate 2/Matter 1 Obsession is &quot;Hoard Magic&quot;</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Maxwell - Obrimos Mysterium, at character gen Froces 3/Matter 1/Prime 1/Time 1 Obsession is &quot;Maintain Order</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot; </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ragnar - Moros Adamantine Arrow, at character gen Matter 3/Death 2/Forces 1 Obsession is &quot;The Glory of Valhalla&quot;</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Saike - Mastigos Adamantine Arrow, at character gen Space 3/Time 2/Mind 1 Obsession is &quot;The Demon Wind&quot;</span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Editing this on 2/24/2025 to add a link to the new Chronicle I started this week, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551256-trenches-pilgrims-a-promethean-the-created-actual-play#post1551256\">Trenches &amp; Pilgrims</a>, a Promethan the Created Chronicle set in World War One.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter One</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">6/28/2023</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Saike wasn't present for this session&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>\u201cLos Angeles is the second largest city in the United States, second only to New York. LA county is home to 10,000,000 people, a quarter of all of California's population, and that doesn\u2019t speak to the rest of the urban sprawl. Despite so many people living so close to each other it is easy to feel isolated and alone. The people you walk by on the sidewalk are people you\u2019ll likely never see again. No one here knows your name. You are a face in a mass of faces. One young woman is experiencing this more than anyone else ever will. She runs through Little Tokyo, sobbing, bleeding, screaming for help, but no one looks at her. She grasps at a stranger's shirt, begging him to notice her, but he walks away, none the wiser to her presence. She sobs as she turns around, the only person who can see her walking towards her through the crowd, bloody knife in hand, but even he goes unnoticed by the crowd. No one notices the screams of her death, no one notices the man, covered in blood, leave the alley and disappears into the crowd. When her body is finally found, detectives and reporters alike ask how no one could have noticed such a gruesome murder so close to the busy streets of LA, so close to City Hall.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of all the people who feel invisible in LA, perhaps the homeless feel this the most. People go out of their way to pretend not to see they are there, to cross the street to avoid them, to see themselves as better than them. One such homeless man wishes he hadn\u2019t been noticed, hadn\u2019t been picked, stripped naked, cleaned and brought to this room full of chanted, hooded strangers. He wishes he wasn\u2019t the one being forced into the golden sarcophagus they surrounded. He wished he couldn\u2019t hear their prayers as the lid was closed on him.<br /> <br /> <br /> With so many people in this urban sprawl the city never truly sleeps. There are always vehicles on the roads, people walking the streets, going about their business, going to or returning from work, but in the evenings it does slow down. One man rides furiously, on his pedal bike. A moment before he was fine, riding to work for the night shift at the Good Samaritan Hospital, but the delusion had taken over in a moment, a psychotic break forcing him to ride and then stop, opening his arms welcomingly as the semi crashed into him, bringing his final moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> And there is a girl in her apartment, waking from a nightmare, a nightmare where she was a goddess of death, seeing over the underworld, and she begins to write, writing as an unseen, veiled woman, half alive and half dead, watches over her.\u201d</i> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This is the intro to the game I read off to the players&gt;</span></span><br /> <br /> The session began with with the three Mysterium mages recieving a text from Architect, the curator of the local athenaeum. Something strange had happened last night and the Guardians of the Veil found out about it through one of their agents who works in the LA General Medical Center's ER. The Guardians are too short on people to send themselves and reached out to the Mysterium to investigate it. The Guardians didn't give many details so Architect had decided to send these three to cast a wide net of knowledge in the arcana, and he also reached out to the Adamantine Arrow for protection, just in case. Due to this Ragnar recieved a text from the mage who had mentored him when he first awakened, Vulcan, telling him what the Mysterium had requested and letting him know to expect a second Talon. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This is of course Saike, who won't be making it to the hospital in time due to not making it for this session&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Eye of God, being up late the night before, would have slept past the meeting time. When he didn't respond to his text Architect sent a sleepwalker to his appartment to wake him up, he was late to the meeting, but not extremely late as a result. The other three mages who did arrive quickly identified eachother, introduced themselves, and entered the hospital. They knew the name of their contact, Dr. Choi, and the receptionist got him on the phone and sent them to the room he wanted to meet at. When they arrived outside the room they detected some sort of magic, but as Dr. Choi rounded the corner he produced a small metal cylinder with a rod attatched to it with a chain. When he put the rod in the cylinder the magic faded. Dr. Choi introduced himself, told them he had something extremely weird happen in the ER the night before and reached out to the mage he knew, assuming they would want to know about it, he then took them into the hospital room. On the T.V. there was a new report playing. Dr. Choi turned off the T.V. but not before the reporter was able to say, &quot;The authorities are still unsure of the identity of 'The Shadow that Walks', who are they, and what do they want?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> There was a man under a blanket that completely covered him, hooked up to all sorts of machines, one to help him breathe, one showing his <i>extremely</i> slow heart rate, one checking for brain activity, etc. Dr. Choi explained that the man had been hit by a semitruck the night before, all his ribs were broken, his skull was caved in, his internal organs were ruptured, he had internal and external bleeding. When the paramedics arrived one the scene he should have been dead, he should have been dead now, but he was still breathing, his heart still beating, he even had some brain activity, despite most of it having been crushed by the truck. He showed them the man to allow them to look over the damage. Giger used Postcognition to watch the accident himself while the others discussed the identity of the man, Todd Williams, he had an employee badge for the Good Samaritan Hospital in LA with him when the accident happened. Giger watched the man biking to work the previous night. Everything was normal until out of the blue he seemed to start suffering some sort of psychotic break and raced through traffic, weaving in and out despite the danger. This went on for about five minutes before he ran a red light, stopped his bike in the middle of the intersection, and opened his arms, smiling, to be hit by the semitruck. Two times during this scene Giger's peripheral mage sight pinged a supernatural effect, once when the psychotic break started, and once at the moment of impact. He went back to the first ping and say a monter <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I'll provide the art for it below&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> the size of a small dog flying in the air. Throughout the five minute scene it followed through the sky, and was present still at the scene of the accident, at which point it flew off.<br /> <br /> When Giger returned from his Postcognition Eye of God had just arrived. After introducing himself at the door to Dr. Choi as his shadowname the Dr. let him into the room, saying &quot;No one who introduces themself like that isn't supposed to be here I'm guessing.&quot; Eye of God introduced himself to the rest of the mages, recieved a recap of the information they had gotten, and then Giger informed everyone of what he had seen through his magic. The group discussed plans of action, Dr. Choi asked if he should reward the room or if they would be able to get back in, Eye of God snapped some pictures and assured him they would, and they left the hospital, with Dr. Choi taking back out the steel cylinder and putting them ward back up. The mages all got into the limo that Giger had ridden in to the hospital, met his driver/butler Leopold, and were off to the scene of the accident. </span><br /> <br /> Not much happened at the scene other than some spells and mage sight work. Maxwell noticed with his sight that the flow of mana in this area was recovering from some sort of disruption, like the mana had been torn away, removed, somehow. Eye of God knew of a few ways that could happened, either a Prime unmaking spell destroying the mana, something Abyssal happened, or a Lower Depths sucking it down. Giger through up a Fate spell, Serendipity, to figure out the best course of action to finding the &quot;Fly&quot;, to which he got some answers: &quot;Find its nest&quot; and &quot;Find its prey&quot;. Giger also through up his sight and saw strings of destiny wrapped around Eye of God, unsure what the destiny was though, he never informed anyone about this. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;In character Eye of God does not know about his destiny&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> In order to find its nest the the mages decided to return to Todd's hospital room and Eye of God would try to track the &quot;Fly&quot; back to its nest using sympathy. They got back into the limo and Co-Located back. There Eye of God did some <i>big</i> Space magic and ended up releasing some paradox into the spell causing the target of the spell to shift, </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;&quot;One paradox dice isn't gonna happen I'll release it&quot; and then it rolled a 10 and an 8 for two success LMFAO&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> but after a second attempt he managed to jump along Todd's sympathy to find the &quot;Fly&quot;. The group got some magic ready </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Acceleration for Giger, Maxwell cast Gravatic Supremacy on everyone, and Ragnar put up a Soul Armor spell on everyone&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> And they Co-Located again to the location of the fly using a borrowed sympathy from Todd.<br /> <br /> They found themselves in an abaonded warehouse, the &quot;Fly&quot; hiding up on one of the rafters above. The place was filled with animals that were not in great condition. Some mice and rats that were half eaten, still squeaking in pain and draging themselves along and a pigeon with no head, flapping around and running into thing. The &quot;fly&quot; wasn't aggressive towards the mages but they decided they would fight it. Ragnar did some powerful Matter magic in the form of Shrink and Grow, making the entire warehouse the size of a house, which frightened the &quot;Fly&quot; and the battle begun.</span><br /> <br /> The &quot;Fly&quot;<br /> <img width=\"300\" height=\"200\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/736d9401-ae2e-4f9e-91e2-b75d3ac885ad/ddrx3e3-8bcbf7ce-412b-4da8-9efc-209dcfc5ff18.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1221,q_75,strp/brainsect_by_halycon450_ddrx3e3-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..m5kTFxSyQEc1tm7ZstNMAw5Oq6lijqJZMaXMNguaxFc\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/736d9401-ae2e-4f9e-91e2-b75d3ac885ad/ddrx3e3-8bcbf7ce-412b-4da8-9efc-209dcfc5ff18.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1221,q_75,strp/brainsect_by_halycon450_ddrx3e3-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..m5kTFxSyQEc1tm7ZstNMAw5Oq6lijqJZMaXMNguaxFc\" data-thumb-url=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/736d9401-ae2e-4f9e-91e2-b75d3ac885ad/ddrx3e3-8bcbf7ce-412b-4da8-9efc-209dcfc5ff18.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1221,q_75,strp/brainsect_by_halycon450_ddrx3e3-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..m5kTFxSyQEc1tm7ZstNMAw5Oq6lijqJZMaXMNguaxFc\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> And the <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/halycon450/art/Brainsect-832953963\" target=\"_blank\">link</a> to Halycon450's upload of their art","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 05-24-2025, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T11:52:24-07:00","id":1517967,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Holy cow this session blew my mind. As you're about to see Eye of God did something crazy in this one. A note about his character, he has the Destiny 3 merit and took the doom &quot;murdered&quot; but that is now up in the air because of this, which is fun and exciting. Can't wait now to bring the doom into the story and have him see how his actions bring about some crazy consequences!!!!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter Two</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">7/12/2023</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Two men kneeled in meditation together, swords on the floor at their sides. This was Saike and Rasuto Katto. When their meditation had finished and Saike had confirmed that his meditation was focused on his swordsmenship skills Rasuto Katto confirmed this was indeed a good thing to meditate on for a young talon, as his sword would be needed by the Arrow. Then Rasuto Katto checked his phone, seeing the message that the Mysterium had requested the help of two talons and Saike was one of the two to be sent. Saike got the information on the assignment and used a Co-Location spell to arrive at the hospital, a Postcognition spell to learn who he was looking for, and then almost entered the room that Todd Williams was in before Dr. Choi stopped him. After he learned he was with the Arrow, Dr. Choi once again lowered the ward and allowed him to enter.<br /> <br /> From here the battle with the &quot;Fly&quot; was quite easy as the mages outnumbered it. Saike was the only to not use any magic, relying on his sword, Ragnar created a sword using Matter magic and the Shaping spell, and the Mysterium mages all used various attack and control spells to harm the creature and slow it down. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;It is perhaps important to note that Giger released a paradox that slow Ragnar down during this fight, instead of slowing the fly down, this will be important in a moment.&gt; </span>Ragnar also revealed</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">his wyvrn ghost familiar in this fight, calling for it to manifest and attack the fly, which is gladly did. Once defeated though the mages quickly realized that the &quot;Fly&quot; could not be killed, Maxwell even tried to use the sword that Ragnar had shaped to behead it, which did not kill it. So information was to be gathered.<br /> <br /> Ragnar opened his sight and saw a swirl of ash in the center of the room, the source of some active magic that was irritating everyone's peripheral. He scrutinized it and revealed the following information, sharing it with the other mages:</span><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&gt;&gt;&gt; Surface Information</span></span></div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Primary arcanum: Space</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Resonance: The feeling of the end being just out of reach</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Age: Days</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Practice: Fraying</span></span></li> </ol><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&gt;&gt;&gt; Deep Information</span></span></div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The mystery is not related to the Supernal or to the Abyss</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Death, Prime and Space all have information about this mystery</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Death - The other side of this portal is missing the final moment of life, the moment that a life ends, death. Creatures native to this plane cannot die and feed off of the deaths of life forms that can. </span></span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Several things happened at this point, one, Maxwell activated his sight and saw the lingering effect of paradox on Giger, scollding him for it quite hard. While this distraction was happened Eye of God, who saw an open doorway where Ragnar saw the swirl of ash, decided to walk through the door. He was teleported to a place filled with skeletons, their minds still trapped within their corpses. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Of course had he been able to use Life magic or Life sight, he would have also seen that the skeletons were still alive, despite their state of decay.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> In a pool of murky water among the piles of skeletons he saw a massive green creature that slept, dozens of minds trapped within its skin. His Prime sight revealed to him that he was ina place that was lower in reality than the Fallen World, and with the use of Mind magic to recall his studies, he realized it was a Lower Depth. While in this realm a paradox was released by him, despite his attempt to contain it, and he noted an alien intelligence took note of him </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Abyssal Backlash condition.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Upon his return to the Fallen World many questions were asked about what he saw, which he reported. Giger's Fate sight also revealed that the strands of destiny that had been around Eye of God when he first saw them were now twisted and flapping violently, like his trip to this realm had violently altered his destiny in some way. The group decided the best thing to do was the close the portal. Eye of God discovered the key, which was something rotting but alive in the vicinity. The mages gathered up all the animals that were in the warehouse and the &quot;Fly&quot; and put them in a box. Maxwell then took the box to the roof and using his Gravitic Supremacy rote, shot it into space. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;All three of the Mysterium mages are either astrophysics PhDs or work on engineering projects that involve leaving the Earth's atmosphere, so they had a lot of fun calculating out how long he'd have to maintain this spell before the box wouldn't return to the planet.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The portal was still open, so the mages returned to the hospital, which Eye of God's Co-location spell was still maintaining, leaving behind Giger and Saike to see if thee portal closed once Todd was no longer in the pressence of the portal and then to get a ride back with Leopold. The portal did close, so now the mages must decide what to do with Todd and the portal.</span><br /> \u200b</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-13-2025, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T22:42:24-07:00","id":1519315,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Saike's player had to leave the game due to a real life opportunity that I'd be mad if he didn't take, sorry to not get to play with my little brother but happy to see him getting and taking opportunities. Giger's player also had a work thing tonight, so we only had Ragnar, Eye of God, and Maxwell around for this chapter. Thankfully because of how the last chapter ended the cabal was already split up in this way, so it worked out really well. Lots of new characters and potential mysteries were in this chapter, so I've taken way to long to actually write it up, but here you are!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">7/26/2023</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">With the physical threat of the monster dealt with Saike went on his way from the warehouse. Giger left from there with Leopold to deal with his own affairs. Ragnar has a martial arts class to teach, so he and the other mages decided to split up for a few hours. While he taught his students, Maxwell and Eye of God went to <i>Lapis Vivus Templum</i>, the Mysterium headquarters. The entire construct is stories beneath The Getty, it is a ruin from the Time Before made of living, growing stone. The central camber is a massive library filled with flying bookshelves filled with every topic a mage could wish to research. While one might expect the awakened and sleepwalkers to maintain <i>Lapis Vivus Templum</i> it is filled with bound goetia, ghosts, and spirits that have been magically materialized. Shambling corpses also wander around, carrying whatever they have been tasked to move.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"141\" height=\"224\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133936052457975862/28a8f50e5bd55432271f57245a41547b.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133936052457975862/28a8f50e5bd55432271f57245a41547b.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133936052457975862/28a8f50e5bd55432271f57245a41547b.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Together our protaganists looked into the lower depth they had discovered, hoping to find more information on it and on the monster that Eye of God had seen resting in the pool of water. The research took several hours but they eventually discovered a journal that belongs to a mystagogue in the 1980s named Eternal Elm. Eternal Elm never researched this lower depth, but her cabal mate, Second Ending, did. He was a member of the Adamantine Arrow and believed that &quot;The Garden of Eternal Rot&quot; might be a path to eternal life. The entire cabal eventually seperated, and Eternal Elm's journal never explained what happened to her cabal mate or this lower depth.<br /> <br /> Before they left to meet up with Ragnar the same sleepwalker from Eye of God's home that morning approached them, informing them that Architect wished to speak with them on their mission before they left.\u200b She escorted them to his office, where he and Moon's Relfection on Water's Surface, the Hierophant, waited for them. Together they discussed their work so far, assuming that nothing too dangerous was to be reported if the two of them were in the athenaeum doing research. The protagonists gave a report on what they had found, including Eye of God having stepped through the portal into The Garden of Eternal Rot. This <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;obviously&gt;</span> concerned the elder mages. Architect confirmed that the trip had left a stain on Eye of God's pattern, and that in the future they should avoid traveling to any lower depths. Eye of God stated they hadn't completely solved the problem, as the victim of the monster they faced waqs still dying but not dead. The Hierophant tried to impart some wisdom on the young mages, stating that &quot;A Mystery is rarely completely solved.&quot; but did not try to disway them from working to cure the sleep of his condition. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This was mainly my way of letting them know they don't have to chase every mystery in the game to a conclusion, and stated so outright after the session.&gt;</span> Then the elder mages asked how things were going socially, as they had a task that needed a cabal, and they wanted to put the mystagogues together into one, along with Ragnar as protection, to deal with a situation that they had come across due to the work of one of their &quot;Sphinxes&quot;. Maxwell exressed some concern about Giger not controlling his magic. This caused Moon's Reflection on Water's Surface to defend Giger, telling Maxwell that even experienced mages sometimes lose control of their magic, and while it should always be avoided when possible, the Abyss will find ways into the Fallen World through the magic of mages. She affirmed that his concern is valid, and that those mages present should keep an eye on him to be sure he isn't intentionally playing with the powers of the Abyss, but that slip ups do happen.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"118\" height=\"236\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120171925554/2365268e9d3707c54139113c2227c79f.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120171925554/2365268e9d3707c54139113c2227c79f.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120171925554/2365268e9d3707c54139113c2227c79f.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"150\" height=\"229\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120465510430/ba527bafaf0caad4fd60e40ddacd950d.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120465510430/ba527bafaf0caad4fd60e40ddacd950d.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133939120465510430/ba527bafaf0caad4fd60e40ddacd950d.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://instagram.com/ruzurifu?igshid=MmU2YjMzNjRlOQ==\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a link to Ruzurifu's Insta, they are responible for the art I used for Architect</span><br /> <br /> \u200b<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Astrid Hagen is a Dreamer, or at least has the potential to be according to the Sphinx cited earlier, and the fron woman for a viking metal band called &quot;Sea of Wolves&quot;. Architect informed the younger mages as to what a Dreamer is. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;You can learn what a dreamer is in the LA setting from the core book, 2e. or in the setting guide I provided in the first post.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The goal of this new cabal, should the mages accept, would be to confirm her status as a Dreamer, at which point they could claim her as a Dreamer of The Golden Order and investigate further or allow another cabal to make a claim to the information she might be able to provide. The choice was up to them and the meeting wouild end with them not having decided if they would accept this task. </span><br /> <br /> <img width=\"157\" height=\"204\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133940974981230692/Screenshot_2023-07-26_185628.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133940974981230692/Screenshot_2023-07-26_185628.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133940974981230692/Screenshot_2023-07-26_185628.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Her in her stage makeup.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Finally, the elder mages wished to know the plan of action for the portal. Maxwell said he'd prefer it doesn't exist, but until then they would contain it. Architect passed along the information of a Guardian of the Veil named Blood who had done warding work on behalf of the Mysterium before. As they left the office Architect appolgized for sending a sleepwalker to Eye of God's home and gave assurance that he has confidence in their abilities to solve this problem. Maxwell called Blood and set up a meeting for that night.<br /> <br /> Ragnar finished his lesson, mainly focusing on the basics but finding ways to hint at simple Truths into the training. Then the three mages met at the Getty to discuss their next step. With several hours before their meeting with Blood they decided to try to get their hands on the jounral of Second Ending. Ragnar called his old mentor, Vulcan, to ask if she had any information on the missing mage. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Due to a really lucky roll on a chance dice Ragnar knew a little bit about Second Ending already, namely that he is an example the Arrow uses to teach their mages not to let your obsessions consume you.&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">She didn't but knew where the journal could be located. This took the mages to The American Military Museum, which hides a portal to a pocket realm filled with the headquarters of the Adamantine Arrow, a base of operations they call <i>Bibliothecam Animae Famem</i>. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I'm noticing a pattern for how I name places in my game.&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">She helped him find the journal while the others waited, and gave him two pieces of advice, don't let the nerd influence you too much, and keep an eye out for a mage named Valkyrie, another young talon who shared in his symbolism. She thought they might be able to hit it off at the next Talon meeting, and informed him that she carried with her a spear, at all times. Maxwell looked through the journal and found information on The Garden of Eternal Rot. Second Ending had discovered a portal there in Long Beach and even gave the address of the place he had found it. The last entry of the journal had information on a planned treck into that place.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"142\" height=\"289\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133946316318314607/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191434.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133946316318314607/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191434.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133946316318314607/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191434.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span></span><br /> <br /> The meeting with Blood went well for the mages, he called them right on time, teleported to them, investigated the now closed portal, Eye of God Co-Located a portal back to the hospital so he could see what it was like opened, he got information on what they knew, and he agreed to ward the place for them under two conditions. One, they gather a dozen small animals for him to release the spell with. Two, Maxwell call a mage named Madeline. A mage Blood owed a favor too, she had apparently told him that Maxwell would get in contact with Blood at some point, and Blood could return the favor by putting them in contact. The mages agreed, and as he begun working they went to the nearest pet shop to collect a dozen mice and Maxwell called Madeline. He knew very little about her before the call, just that she too was apart of the Mysterium and she was an Acanthus. She told him she knew he had been tasked with finding the soulstone of one of the Rapt <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Player background stuff, the first step on being intiatied into the Atlantean Mystery.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and she and some of her associates would love to help. They agreed to meet later in the week to discuss details of how they could help eachother. After an hour Blood exited the building, the ward finished, offered his assistance in the future if they need it, and left with his mice.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"192\" height=\"192\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133950708304052244/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191525.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133950708304052244/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191525.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1133950708304052244/Screenshot_2023-07-26_191525.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> The final scene of this chapter involved the mages ubering to Long Beach, finding the building Second Ending had talked about in his journal, using Space magic to enter the building, and using even more Space magic to allow them to scry into the room the journal indicated had once had the portal. An older man now lived inside, so Maxwell instead used Time magic to look into the past. There he saw this mage coming and going, many rodents caged and nailed to the walls, dying, but not able to finally die. As he came and went he clearly studied the portal, scrying into it until one day and arrived, collected materials he had left, and entered into the portal. As Maxwell scanned through time in this place he saw thre mortal eventually close, and then fade from existence </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I let him use his Prime sight to notice the way symbols of Death were being affected in the area alter.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and only when the portal was completely gone did the animals eventually die. With this the cabal decided that Todd had his symbol taken from him, and restoring it somehow, or finding a way to permanetly close the portal, would allow him to die. They all returned to their homes for the night to meet again the next day to continue their mission to save </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Kill&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Todd.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-14-2023, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T15:58:00-07:00","id":1520790,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Waited too long and ended up getting an extra session in so this post is a two-for-one, lucky us!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/2/23</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Giger, in his sleeper persona, Ted Turner, attended a sort of party, a high class one, filled with the highest of the high class. Most of those there were incredibley boring but one man, Mark Slim caught his attention. They visted for a bit before Mark told Ted about a historic artifact, a vase from the Warring Kingdoms period of Chinese history. Ted convinced him that his father would have loved to see it, and he got an invitation to set up a time to come visit Mark's mansion and see the vase. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This happened during the day of the last session, so his character could make some progress while the other characters would have been.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <img width=\"175\" height=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136471101778698342/dfcp5ka-4253239e-2704-4cbf-8bdd-48cbe7584976.png?width=517&amp;height=905\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136471101778698342/dfcp5ka-4253239e-2704-4cbf-8bdd-48cbe7584976.png?width=517&amp;height=905\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136471101778698342/dfcp5ka-4253239e-2704-4cbf-8bdd-48cbe7584976.png?width=517&amp;height=905\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> The following day led to a breakfast meeting, hosted by Ragnar in a diner, they discussed their plans going forward. Ragnar had been informed by Vulcan that there would be a talon briefing mission that afternoon that he was expected to attend, so while he did the Mysterium mages took the time to do research in the <i>Lapis Vivus Templum</i>. Giger spent the time catching up, both on information that he had gotten from the day he had missed, and also on his own when it came to The Garden of Eternal Rot. Eye of God spent time researching demons in the Iron Maze, a section of the athenaeum dedicated to the realm of Mastigos. There he found records of <u>The Worms of the Tapestry</u>, an imp that takes the form of a fanged mass of wormed that feed on both the blood and the sympathy of the summoner, and then use that to repair parts of the world that have broken down, specifically, they close portals that exist between the fallen world and Lower Depths, the Abyss, or the Suprunal. </span><br /> <br /> The meeting of the talons was very much like a military meeting, with the higher up, Love is War and Reiksman, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;art pending&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">where all the talons gathered were shown a display of Los Angeles that seemed to shift as the places of interest in the briefing are describing, but Ragnar realized it was actually just the spot of their preception that was changing. Three new threats had been indentified; first, three murders had happened in the past several months in broad daylight but with no witnessess, despite being in crowded areas, like Little Tokyo, near a crowded hiking area, and the on one of the beaches. No ghosts had been left by any of the murder victims, but the Guardians and Arrow are certian the supernatural is involved. Second, a pack of Werewolves has been sighted in the San Gabriel Mountains. Their alligence, and territory, are unknown but they have killed both human and spirit alike, so are the be considered a threat. Finally, The Shadow That Walks, a theif who has been stealing priceless sleeper artifacts, has remained unidenitified by mage society, even with the use of magic. Their sympathy is jumbled in a way that makes the identity hard to track. It is unknown if they are a part of the supernatural world, or if they are aware of it, but they may one day steal something of the mage's world, and there fore they are a threat. Any information gathered on any of these threats is to be reported to the first talons. During the meeting a mage spoke up, asking about the murderers, but no more information was given. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;While Ragnar didn't know who the mage was by name, he does now know what he looks like.&gt;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"120\" height=\"259\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136495758032519198/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136495758032519198/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136495758032519198/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">After the meeting was over Ragnar approached Valkyrie, who was obvious to him due to the golden spear she carried. They discussed their shared symbolism briefly and then voiced interest in finding more information on the Werewolves, they decided they would find a Thyrsus and investigate.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"120\" height=\"179\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136493696100073643/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200006.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136493696100073643/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200006.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1136493696100073643/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200006.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Finally, once the cabal was together again, they returned to Long Beach to investigate the past of the portal with Giger's more advanced study for the Time aracnum. Giger, with the help of some alcohol he had picked up, </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;<i>luckily</i> it was the occupants favorite drink&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> they managed to get some alone time in his living room, in which Giger used his Time magic to send Maxwell back in time further than he had gone before, to see the opening of the portal. They learned the building was decaying at an excellerated rate, too fast to be natural but he wasn't able to detect any magic active in the area until the portal opened, and that there use to be a small hallow here, but it was consumed slowly as the schism was born. This led him back to the <i>Lapis Vivus Templum</i> to do research. </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Maxwell's research led him to the name of a mage that was assumed dead, </span>Clausius. This mage had been spreading entropy throughout Los Angeles in the early 2010s before being captured by the Bellerophon Group and is missing since. He also learned that Madeline was a member, or working towards being a member. He called her and set up a meeting for the next day, where she asked if she could bring a friend. Maxwell was okay with that on the condition that he could also bring friends.\u200b<br /> <br /> The following day Eye of God tried to summon The Worms of the Tapestry but gave up, not wanting to bring the Abyss into the Fallen World. The whole failure took eight hours, right up until the time it was to meet Madeline, and Co-Located to Maxwell while he hid in the bathroom of the Getty for their meeting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/11/2023</span><br /> <br /> The cabal met with Madeline and her friend, Caesar, leader of the Bellerophon Group. He explained to Maxwell that the organization was interested in him because they knew he was linked to the Rapt via the divination preformed to learn about his journy through the Atlantian Mystery, and they wanted to help him gain the soul stone of one of the Rapt in exchange for him giving them information on whatever Rapt he discovered in the process. He agreed and Caesar took them into a lower level of the anthenaeum, a level that a member of the Adamantine Arrow like he should not have had access too, and he took them through a door with no handle into The Hall of Madness. Here there were seven oil paintings hanging on the wall of a hallway, along with a second hall that intersected with it filled with books and items. The cabal was allowed to look over the items and notes here while Madeline watched and Caesar left to take care of his own afairs. The cabal learned of several mages that had been captured throughout the time of the Bellerophon Group here, but Clausius was of the most interest to Maxwell. He discovered he had been cured in 2011, but slipped back into a state of Rapture shortly after and disappeared through the first hallow he had been using to spread his entropy resonance through, during this time he also had managed to shred all his symapthetic links, becoming untracable. Using time magic on his old rod <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;dedicated magical tool&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and a jar filled with mana taken from the hallow he had been corrupting, they managed to track his old sympathetic links back to the hallow, looking past it with Space magic they discovered it was not just a hallow, but a portal to the Shadow. From there they went on to other things.</span><br /> <br /> While Maxwell was doing his research in the Hall of Madness, Giger looked over the paintings, seven of them in total, one of a frozen corpse covered in ice, one of a man in dark robes, a hood covering his face and a large bowl filled with garbage on his back, one of a woman who looked ill from poisoning, one of a man with his arms open and face cast skyward, one of a man with a shovel in a graveyard, one of a man in a temple, and one of a man standing alone in the darkness. The eyes followed Giger as he studied them, even their necks turned to keep an eye on him. He noticed the frames of the paintings had high speech glyphs on them, magic for binding, and Madeline revealed the goetic faults of various Rapt had been trapped in these paintings so that the knowledge they had gained would never be lost.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"123\" height=\"322\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1139734010881388624/Screenshot_2023-08-11_183223.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1139734010881388624/Screenshot_2023-08-11_183223.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1139734010881388624/Screenshot_2023-08-11_183223.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I haven't decided on Caesar's art yet.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Ragnar had arrived late and didn't get to enter the Halls of Madness, but he did meet Caesar on his way out. Caesar talked to him about </span>Reiksman, saying he didn't agree with how he like teaching young talons, but also that he couldn't interfere if he was the one sent to brief them. He did warn Ragnar though that Reiksman wanted the talons to not trust him, so he would give them incomplete or outright false infromation. Not enough that would result in them getting killed, but enough that they would be wise to not trust him.<br /> <br /> Ragnar called Vulcan and got the name of a mage who had supposedly defeated a werewolf in combat, a Thyrsus of the Free Council named Fox, he and Valkyrie decided they would track this mage down to help them with the werewolf pack.<br /> <br /> Finally the mages arrived at the sight of one of the murders Ragnar had learned about in the briefing. Immidiatly Ragnar felt his mage sight warn him of magic, and with Death magic he discovered the ghost of one of the murder victims, Victoria Adams. The ghost seemed stuck in a death loop, running down the alley begging for help, tripping and falling, trying to get up to get away, being stabbed in the gut, extoplasm spraying like blood, falling back onto her back, continueing to be stabbed, and then starting over at the end of the alley. The session ended with him exspanding the ability to see this ghost to the rest of the cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T17:44:54-07:00","id":1522318,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/23/2023</span><br /> <br /> Investigating the death of Victoria Adams, Giger used Postcognition to allow everyone to view the murder. It was only Maxwell and Ragnar that were able to actually watch the murder, as some sort of magic was preventing people from noticing either the killer or Victoria. The murder went exactly as expected based on how the ghost was reacting, the killer chased her down the alley way, as she fell they caught up to her, stabbed her, she collapsed into the wall, and they sat on top of her stabbing until she was long dead. Then something unusal happened, the killer sat on her corpse and sobbed, appologizing over and over. Then they got up and disapeared into the crowd, covered in blood but no one took notice of them. Ragnar also noticed something about the killer, he was certain he had seen the blade before.<br /> <br /> Once they were no longer viewing the past Ragnar pulled ectoplasm out of the ghost and used it to create a wall, breaking her cycle long enough to talk to her. She begged him for help while they tried to get information from her. Mostely it was useless, she had no idea who the attacker was or what he wanted, only that he was making Fate right by killing her and that he was sorry.<br /> <br /> Investigating with mage sight the cabal noticed the sliced threads of Fate lay all over the alley, clearly the nimbus of a mage. Using his Space magic, Eye of God discovered the nimbus was connected to a mage name &quot;Thread-Cutter,&quot; and that Thread-Cutter was connected to someone named <u>The Woman at the End of the Thread</u>. Upon learning that he saw her, looking back at him.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"210\" height=\"208\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141553822368542830/image.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141553822368542830/image.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141553822368542830/image.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> She appeared and Giger immediately knew she was a Fae from the Supurnal. She implored them not to interfere with the work that Thread-Cutter was doing, that he was setting Fate right and this was a good thing, even if people must die. She also took hold of the strands of destiny that whipped invisible around Eye of God, stating &quot;We will see you in the future, this much is certian.&quot; She left, vanishing into Thread-Cutter's nimbus.<br /> <br /> The mage's began doing research, with Maxwell discovering a legacy known as the Thread Cutters who practiced Fate and Death magic, but it was unclear their involvment here, if at all. With the help of Eye of God's Mind magic Ragnar was able to recall where he had seen the blade used to murder Victoria, it was weilding by a mage of the Adamantine Arrow, the one who had spoken up during the Talon meeting.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"145\" height=\"313\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141562795972902962/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141562795972902962/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1141562795972902962/Screenshot_2023-08-02_200817.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Now the question was, how do they find Thread-Cutter, and what do they do with him?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 09-20-2023, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T23:58:10-07:00","id":1522816,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">With two players gone on game night traveling on what was supposed to be a VtR story end we decided to just do a two person session of Mage so everyone could be around for the Vampire game. It was me, Giger's player and Eye of God's player tonight so I decided I'd start introducing some of the plot lines I had in mind for their characters.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/13/23</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eye of God keeps his sleeper life intact as best he can. He works in a manga store, catering to anyone who enjoys that side of Japanese culture. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Eye of God is a reference to a character in Full Metal Alchemist, for those who don't know.&gt;</span> The shift was busy due to an upcoming convention, many people were buying now to avoid lines on that weekend. When he finally got to go on break he found two of his co-workers, Brandon and Jacqueline, excitedly talking about something in the break room. Turns out they had been playing Onrain Senshi, an invite only MMORPG that was a medevil European style setting, but with a Japanese lense over the game. They were both very excited about it, and Brandon offered to send an invite to Eye of God <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Real name Johnny&gt;</span> so that they could start on a secret quest that you only gained access to once 20 people you had invited joined the game. When Eye of God googled the game he noticed in the negative space between the Japanese character i nthe game's title were what appeared to be incomplete High Speech runes. He accepted and started playing right after work. Before he left work a homeless man, Thomas Abrams, stopped by the store to use the bathroom if he was allowed. Eye of God knew he was very polite and kind and didn't have a problem with it, he found the bathroom looking even better than it was before, but Eye of God noticed he was a little more on edge than usual. He questioned him about if anything was the matter and he just told him that he hadn't seen one of his friends in his usual spot lately. He enjoyed the game after playing it for a few hours. He got off for the night but after only a few minutes found himself online again, and played all night long before going in to do another shift. Once his shift was finished, he was back on the game, quickly becoming addicted.<br /> <br /> In Giger's Penthouse where, for the past two weeks, his perphial mage sight has been alerting him constantly to the presence of magic. His apartment now shared a space with an aedes, one that appeared like the inside of a cave, filled with gems, coins, and magical items. His mage sight would onhly settle down while he was asleep, so living in this space weighed on him emotionally. As he was heading off to bed he noticed something moving behind the curtain, he approached and found a red, lizard like humaniod creature that he immediately recognized as a fae. The fae seemed frustereated but impressed that he had been caught, and extended out an arm, offering him his own pearl necklass back as a reward for catching him, and he introduced himself as Kobold. Kobold spoke in riddles, as fae seem to like to, about his, and Giger's, place in the story. Giger asked about his ability to break the story, to which Kobold warned there could be &quot;Great rewards but also great curses.&quot; He then told him being he was caugtht he must return, but one of his siblings would be about. The next morning Giger had Leopold report on anything that was missing. Nothing else from their appartment but Leopold knew of at least three accusations of theft in the building. Thinking they might also be mages, Giger investigating, but finding no nimbuses around their apartments he let the matter rest for now and called Eye of God for an extra set of ...eyes.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"202\" height=\"304\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151693108187242557/Screenshot_2023-09-13_183655.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151693108187242557/Screenshot_2023-09-13_183655.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151693108187242557/Screenshot_2023-09-13_183655.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> \u200bGiger was unable to get Eye of God to drive to him, so he went to his apartment with Leopold to find it in a small state of disrepare, it looks as if Eye of God hadn't cleaned all weekend <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Honestly a big yikes to me describing my own apartment as in a state of disaray LOL&gt;</span> Leopold went to do some cleaning while Giger tried to figure out what was so great about this video game. Eventually he managed to get Eye of God off the game but it only lasted 10 minutes before Giger sensed some magic go off with his periphial mage sight and Eye of God hopped back on the game. Giger looked the game up and noticed the same runes in the negatives space that Eye of God had, but he realized they were not incomplete High Speech but abyssal in nature. Giger, realzing magic was involved her, talked Eye of God into letting him buy a new computer for him, so he could &quot;enjoy the game on the highest end equipment.&quot; Eye of God transfered all of his stuff over to a hard drive and Leopold, to Eye of God's surprise, destroyed the computer at Giger's instruction. Together they drove off to Giger's appartment to investigate the mystery there, and Eye of God felt fine on the trip over, thinking about the game some but it seemed to stop consuming him. In the end though it proved useless, even with his mage sight and adding in Prime he couldn't see anything, while Giger continued to see the cave and its contents. They concluded that this must be an aedes and more research would need to be done.<br /> <br /> Giger then got a phone call from Mark Slim, the man he had met at the party before, who had some meetings cancled and was wondering if he would like to come and see his collection. Sensing that he was with someone he invited him to bring along any friends he may be with as long as they will be respectful of the collection, so Giger and Eye of God found themselves at the estate of Mark Slim. When they entered a sort of library / museum room he had set up they found him watching T.V. An FBI agent spoke about how her team would be working with the LA and California police to investigate the Shadow that Walks. Seeing her on T.V. both mages felt a ping in their periphial mage sight. Opening their senses Giger saw her fate being tied to an unknown person and Eye of God saw she was actually asleep.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"250\" height=\"319\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151708226350481428/25b1e7a7f78dfaaaf3491305bb449841.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151708226350481428/25b1e7a7f78dfaaaf3491305bb449841.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151708226350481428/25b1e7a7f78dfaaaf3491305bb449841.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Together they looked on the collection, the ancient Chinese vase was the first thing they saw, but Mark Slim was excited to show off his entire collection of ancient, priceless relics. While most were mundane in the eyes of the mages, the vase was of interest, strange runes, which they knew to be High Speech, covered it, talking about &quot;The Mandate of Heaven&quot; and its prison. As the conversation and tour continued they noted some sort of spell, &quot;The Holy Communion of the Syzygos Bythos&quot;. Unsure what that was, it was clear that it was at the very least real fallen world occultism. Mark explained his grandson had taken an interest in the occult since he had moved to Los Angeles to live with him, which was a step up from being an anime watching loser he was before hand, but he still didn't care for his interests. A tour of the house followed, and when they returned they found his grandon, Mark Slim III putting something back on the bookshelf, Giger approached and shook his hand, introducing himself and getting a look at the book, a titleless tome bound in brass and leather. Mark III and Eye of God actually hit it off though, talking about some anime they both enjoyed and Eye of God got his email to invite him to Onrain Senshi. Mark Slim didn't seem impressed by this, but aside from the strange occult studies he was getting himself involved in, the mages didn't notice anything strange about Mark III. Eye of god then got a text from Brandon, who was excited about getting &quot;The Final Scroll&quot; in Onrain Senshi, even if it was &quot;bugged&quot; as he put it. What Eye of God and Giger saw when they looked at the picture of the quest item in game was in fact abyssal runes.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151715747899375706/cute-anime-characters-with-glasses-z7r3x9ypj6r9evqw.jpg?width=468&amp;height=905\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151715747899375706/cute-anime-characters-with-glasses-z7r3x9ypj6r9evqw.jpg?width=468&amp;height=905\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1151715747899375706/cute-anime-characters-with-glasses-z7r3x9ypj6r9evqw.jpg?width=468&amp;height=905\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Upon getting his computer set up Eye of God downloaded and played Giger noted how good the game looked, in fact it looked perfect, just like on Eye of God's old computer as well. Eye of God was put to task by Brandon to farm for a rare drop from Ogres in game, a blood stone, that was needed to complete &quot;The Final Spell&quot; while the other players farmed higher level ingrediants for it. Giger was suspiucous of the game so, casting Fate magic to help him find what he was looking for, he set off into the neighborhood. Unfortunately when he cast the Fate spell he overreached and did not contain the resulting paradox <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;again on purpose&gt;</span> and Eye of God was effected by the spell as well, the very first ogre he killed dropped the rare item...what luck.<br /> <br /> Giger found an old gaming laptop and a graphing calculator at an old rumage sale and after some failed haggeling aquired both. He installed the game on both of them to find it ran perfectly on each. At that point Eye of God got a notifcation in game that Mark III had accepted his invite to download the game. Eye of God began digging in the code and found a befouled version of the &quot;Emotional Urging&quot; rote that would be cast whenever someone got up from the game.\u200b</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 09-20-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T18:47:08-07:00","id":1523447,"title":"","content":"Wowzah! After doing our Giger/Eye of God session that was Chapter 7 we had our normally scheduled Chapter 8. The following week when we were supposed to play VtR two players couldn't make it again, so me, Eye of God, and Ragnar did a astral journey one shot with the expectations that the plot that happened would be self contained, but the NPCs might not be, which is Chapter 9. Then, on Friday, our CoC game got cancled because the DM wasn't preped enough to run it, NBD. The DM also happens to be Giger's player, and he asked me if I would be willing to run a one-on-one session, which is Chapter 10.<br /> <br /> Obviously if you are one of my players who happen to be reading over this, don't read Chapter 10.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chapter 8</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/20/2023</span><br /> <br /> While Eye of God and Giger were working on their own mysteries <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Chapter 7&gt;</span> Maxwell was within the Antherneum researching Sag'Suga Isim but not having much luck. All he managed to find from a weekend of research was information from a Thyrsus in the late 1990s talking about humans and spirits that had come in contact with the entropy god. The humans had become souless,. while the spirits had become shadows of themselves, entropy elementals.<br /> <br /> Ragnar traveled North to his mother's home for the weekend, hoping to have a relaxing visit with her. Once he arrived though he discovered he was being followed by the ghost of Victoria Adams. She was no longer in her deathloop, instead just staring off into the distance. Any interaction he forced with her via Death magic resulted in her being confused, unsure of who he was or where she was. The Monday morning he returned home she was waiting in the kitchen, she turned to face him, her face changed, half of it old and rotten and the other half young and beautiful and spoke &quot;Find me, necromancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Giger awoke to the pitter patter of feet in his bedroom and, using his Postcognition spell, saw Kobold sneak out of the air duct and run into his living room. Using more Time magic, he moved himself into the past, the night before, and called the cabal to come help him. Witrh the use of Maxwell's gravity magic, they managed to pin Kobold to the ground in the entry way and interrogate him. To his surprise it wasn't Kobold, but a different creature that also called itself Kobold. This Kobold wanted to steal knowledge, and tore a page out of a book that Giger offered him. The interogation still happened, and they learned that the aedes appeared wherever great greed appeared or was fated to appear, this is where The Dragon would move the hoard. Eventually a deal was struck, Kobold would help Giger to understand the Mystery of the Dragon's Hoard in exchange for the release of the gravity spell. Giger then scrutinzied the aedes and learned the true nature of what was around him. He managed to successfully scrutinzie the aedes, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;managed to get the opacity to zero in four rolls, despitre it being an opacity four mystery, with using mana, the help of Kobold giving him a +1 to the rolls, and getting really lucky with two exceptional successes right off the bat to get the opacity really low really fast&gt;</span> and learned that when the Exarchs acsended they stole a multitude of destinies from huamnity, destinies we should have been able to fulfill but no longer could. They shaped these destinies into artifacts and hid them away within the supurnal. These destinies exist within the Dragon's Hoard. Using Fate Giger identified four destinies within the aedes that he could immidiatly see. The Crown of the Tyrant was a destiny that would have the wearer of the crown unite the world under one throne, one crown, and one fist. The Shield of the People would be wielded by someone who protect the people of the world against an external threat. The Sword of the Godslayer would be wielded by someone who would fell gods, Maxwell took an interest in this destiny. Finally the Pen of Peace would be used to write a philosphy that would bring about 1000 years of world wide pacifism. Still unable to reach any of these items, Giger now was a step closer to them, and Kobold was gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;Surface Information<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Primary arcanum: Fate and Matter</li> <li>Resonance: Greed, the desire to protect what is your and take what belongs to others, The Exarchs</li> <li>Age: The aedes exists outside time</li> <li>Practice: N/A</li> </ol><br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt; Deep Information<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The mystery is related to the Supernal</li> <li>The Dragon\u2019s Hoard contains all of the destinies the Exarchs stole from humanity when they created the lie. Each destiny has been shaped into an artifact and hidden here. An acanthus with Fate 3 and Matter 3 can do a targeted supernal summoning to summon out one of the artifacts, allowing someone to complete a trial involving stealing it from the Dragon\u2019s Hoard, and then gain the artifact, destiny and doom associated with the item.</li> <li>In addition, any Acanthus who has revealed the mystery gains one free reach on any Fate and/or Matter spells cast to protect what is theirs or to take from others.</li> </ol>\u200b<br /> <br /> <img width=\"175\" height=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1154238836881248326/e8fb9f017c918c98f3e2a6b2229df20ec3efb6db.png?ex=651acfef&amp;is=65197e6f&amp;hm=9b93c930e7eaec8899ac11b86ea869f11253cb705d8e6ca4668f94e7f2a77a7e&amp;=&amp;width=712&amp;height=905\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1154238836881248326/e8fb9f017c918c98f3e2a6b2229df20ec3efb6db.png?ex=651acfef&amp;is=65197e6f&amp;hm=9b93c930e7eaec8899ac11b86ea869f11253cb705d8e6ca4668f94e7f2a77a7e&amp;=&amp;width=712&amp;height=905\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1154238836881248326/e8fb9f017c918c98f3e2a6b2229df20ec3efb6db.png?ex=651acfef&amp;is=65197e6f&amp;hm=9b93c930e7eaec8899ac11b86ea869f11253cb705d8e6ca4668f94e7f2a77a7e&amp;=&amp;width=712&amp;height=905\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> The final scene had the cabal back at the murder scene of Victoria Adams, Giger pearing into the past, this time wtinessing the murder himself, and then watching to see where her body was taken, The Los Angeles County Department of Medical Examiner-Corner. The cabal went there, Ragnar used Matter magic to make his licence appear to be that of someone related to Victoria, and they entered the building to see Victoria's body. When they did her ghost stared at the body, confused as to why she was dead, even asking Ragnar to explain why to her. He admitted he didn't know. At that point the body of Victoria grabbed Ragnar, the face changed again to be like she was in his kitchen that morning and said &quot;Find ME, necromancer,&quot; and the chapter ended.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;XP was spent after this chapter. Giger increased his Prime to 1, and then moved a dot of Matter into Prime, being he hadn't used Matter magic at all I allowed this, so he now has Prime 2. Maxwell increased his Gnosis to 2, and Eye of God increased his Mind to 2.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chapter 9</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/27/2023</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God and Ragnar found themselves in an old medieval city that was about to be under seige. They found themselves on the side of the defends, who appeared to be vikings, and Eye of God recgonized they were at the Battle of York. Strange, humanoid figured were in the sky but to far away from him to notice. Neither of them were sure why they were there. They engaged in battle until Eye of God remembered they were looking for a battle standard with the rune of the Adamantine Arrow on it. Using his Space magic he found it and then recalled he and Ragnar were to find a way to Valhalla. Seeing the figures in the sky he realzied they were valkyrie. They also heared the voice of Vulcan, from the time they were awake, encourging them to fight till the end. They did, and the valkyrie took them to Valhalla.<br /> <br /> In Valhalla they remembered what they were doing in the Temenos. The Adamantine Arrow had gained intel that a goetia somehow linked to Tremere Liches had been placed in the realm of Valhalla in the Temenos, and the mages had been sent in to find and bind it, the battle standard Eye of God had found changing here to that of a chain. After interacting with some of the local goetia they learned of a stranger in the realm who had gone to talk to Odin. Figuring this might be their target they went to investigate and then stalk the stranger, who they had scene get permission from Odin to &quot;Find and deal with the intruder on his behalf.&quot; Eventually the stranger noticed Eye of God following him and turned to confront him. It turned out this was a fellow mage, named Midas, who had been sent here to preform some magic on the same goetia they were looking for, on behalf of the Minisitry of Mammon. The three of them agreed to work together, but Eye of God and Ragnar kept their shadownames secret. Eventually the search took them to the edge of the realm, where the valkyrie looked down to Earth, and into a cave, where Eye of God found a place where the goetia had been feeding. He dominated the goetia and allowed Midas to preform his magic on the entity. Midas announced he gained nothing, and when Eye of God offered to look at his sympathetic connections to find for Midas who had brought the goetia here, Midas informed him it wouldn't work. Eye of God is not currently a strong enough Mind mage to seek out all information within the minds of others, only surface information. but made a deal with Midas to pass along any information he found once he could, and Midas offered an IOU, not wanting to accept a gift, but agree to a transaction and Midas gave them the name of one of his servants, Mr. Garcia, at the Hilton, who could put them in contact in the waking world. Ragnar then useed the chain to bind the goetia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img width=\"250\" height=\"367\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1156782652880326666/9d2b80bb5893d65cd8f07d10b86f0667.png?ex=651ad68c&amp;is=6519850c&amp;hm=b10af4c626e7c5b0fc52cc9b574a1e653dddd9594eaedf9cc2c2ef2faf1a6795&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1156782652880326666/9d2b80bb5893d65cd8f07d10b86f0667.png?ex=651ad68c&amp;is=6519850c&amp;hm=b10af4c626e7c5b0fc52cc9b574a1e653dddd9594eaedf9cc2c2ef2faf1a6795&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1156782652880326666/9d2b80bb5893d65cd8f07d10b86f0667.png?ex=651ad68c&amp;is=6519850c&amp;hm=b10af4c626e7c5b0fc52cc9b574a1e653dddd9594eaedf9cc2c2ef2faf1a6795&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Midas in the Astral&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Upon waking Ragnar could feel the influence of the goetia in his mind, but Reiksman summoned the goetia out of his mind and bound it. He told both mages they were now owed a favor by the Adamantine Arrow and Eye of God cashed it in right away, saying he wanted access to the goetia in the future once he could dive into its mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chapter 10</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/29/2023</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Shadow That Walks is a thief who has gained notoriety first in Southern California, and eventually all of North America, for his crimes. He has stolen from the ultra wealthy countless times and leaves behind his mark, a red cloth with a dagger pinning it to the wall. California has failed to identified any leads and has had to bring in the FBI in order to help catch this criminal. Even the Adamantine Arrow and Gaurdians of the Veil have taken notice, althought none of the locations of the awakened have been targeted yet. A secret no one else knows about The Shadow That Walks is that he awakaned to the path of the Acanthus, and took the shadowname Giger.<br /> <br /> Tonight The Shadow That Walks would rob Mark Slim. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Frankly, from a narrative standpoint, not too much happened.&gt;</span> He produced a lot of Fate magic to set him up for success, too much, and ended up gaining two paradox conditions. Then he broke in, tied up a gaurd, had a bat fly in his face, which freaked him out as a strange omen, and then had Leopold enter the house as he disabled the cameras and window alarms to the library. While he waited for Leopold he studied the book that Mark Slim III had been interested in. It seemed to be some sort of bestiary, with many monsters in it. Strange equations in High Speech were scattered throughout the book, one involving Prime and another arcana, the rest he couldn't make sense of but with Prime sight he realized they were rotes. The book was bound in bronze and made of some strange parchment, not papper, that was different colors when he looked at it with his Prime sight. Split into three sections, \u201c<i>Pleromaic Outcasts</i>\u201d was black-green and described strange, alien worlds. \u201c<i>Saklastic Archons</i>\u201d was a brick red color and was a bulk of the bestiary, and \u201c<i>Ptahilistic Unquiet</i>\u201d continued the bestiary but was a grey-green color. He returned it after memorizing some of the symbols from the third part of the book and one of the realms from the first part <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Being under the effect of Accelerate he was under no time restrictions.&gt;</span> When Leopold arrived they stole the vase they had seen on his last visit with the High Speech, but left the book. As they were leaving a minivan pulled up and the FBI agent assigned to The Shadow That Walks case stepped out, Mark Slim was furious she was there, but she explained that she had analyzed The Shadow That Walk's patterns and she was certain Mark Slim was the next target. He refused to listen though and sent her away. Throughout this event Giger noticed that there was active magic on the FBI agent. He left, Leopold had already escaped the grounds, and Giger swung through the city <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;He has a grabblings hook swing thingy&gt;</span> before returning home. He dropped all his magic, but the weight of so many spells <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;5 spells with gnosis one and no sanctum&gt; </span>exhausted him, and he wasn't able to use his Time magic to view the past. He placed the vase in a secret room in his penthouse and slept. The next morning his cast Postcognition to view the past, and with his mage sight he saw the fate of him, the FBI agent, and Mark Slim all bind together, and his Prime sight revealed no supurnal magic on the FBI agent.</div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-05-2023, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T16:53:29-07:00","id":1524055,"title":"","content":"So a reminder because that last post had three Chapters included in it, this happens directly Chapter 8, and chapter 10 happened at an undecided time, but has also been a thing. Ragnar showed up at the end of this session, he was busy with family. so the very first scene described here happenedat the end of the session and is basically a wrap up of the last scene of Chapter 8, then everything else happens after that in chroniclogical order.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chapter 11</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">10/4/23</span><br /> <br /> The corpse looked up at Ragnar and repeated itself, &quot;Find ME, necromancer.&quot; With his Death sight active Ragnar was able to see a second face behind that of the corpse, controling it, forcing it to move to its designs, the same face he had seen in the ghost of Victoria Adams that morning. The actual ghost of Victoria was no longer inspecting her own body, wondering why she had died, now she cowered in the corner of the morgue, and the wyvern familiar howled in fear. The face looked up at Ragnar for a moment longer before vanishing, the corpse slumping back over before the mage. Unsure of what to do he turned to Giger and together they decided they would find a way to send Ragnar back one month to the murder of Victoria Adams. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I am unclear if this is still the plan though, as it turns out my entire player group didn't catch that this was a second ghost controling the corpse, not Victoria herself, so we will see if they decide to move forward with that plan anyway.&gt;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"196\" height=\"272\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159337846772072490/Screenshot_2023-09-27_181403.png?ex=6539e302&amp;is=65276e02&amp;hm=a67c8f3ad5fd03742830b0da7e9cddba80098cf31c69160a0d6da3a42a633f44&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159337846772072490/Screenshot_2023-09-27_181403.png?ex=6539e302&amp;is=65276e02&amp;hm=a67c8f3ad5fd03742830b0da7e9cddba80098cf31c69160a0d6da3a42a633f44&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159337846772072490/Screenshot_2023-09-27_181403.png?ex=6539e302&amp;is=65276e02&amp;hm=a67c8f3ad5fd03742830b0da7e9cddba80098cf31c69160a0d6da3a42a633f44&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Ragnar left to be on his own for a bit to think on what had happened, </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;because the players wasn't yet around and the last scene didn't happen until the end of the session&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and Eye of God went into work to draw mana from the hallow there. Giger, also in desperate need of mana, convinced Maxwell to let him come to his sanctum and draw mana from the hallow he had there. By the time they were done Giger recieved a phone call from Mark Slim, enraged, he told him to come immidiately to his estate. When asked why he reported he had been robbed by The Shadow That Walks. Eye of God recieved an email from Mark Slim III stating the same, telling him his grandfather was furious, and asking for assistance. Together the three mystagogues found themselves in the mans estate again. At first the police were unwilling to let them pass but Mark Sr. forced them to let them through, just not into the crime scene, the actual library / display room they had been in before. It was clear to Eye of God's Mind sight that Mark was furious, pacing back and forward, sputting things about how the city had fallen, crime was rappant, and the authorities were complicant in their inaction, &quot;Something needs to be done.&quot; Giger asked what he wanted to do and Mark replied, &quot;I want to find The Shadow That Walks and ring his neck.&quot; Mark III also was experiencing very strong emotions, the black aura Eye of God saw confirmed it was fear, but he hid his emotions better than his grandfather. Eye of God also noticed the detective, Special Agent Olivia Miller, was once again asleep, a man standing next to her in a trenchcoat, and wavey brown hair. Despite her being asleep she stood, smoking a cigarette as she ordered the police around. Finally she turned and looked at the bag of sand with a red cloth pinned to it by a dagger and said, &quot;The Shadow has a partner, there is no other possible way they could have removed the vase without triggering the alarm here.&quot; When one of the detectives said it was an interesting theory she retorted, &quot;It isn't a theory.&quot; Giger also looked through his mage sight and noticed Mark Slim and Olivia Miller were becoming linked by Fate. One last thing that Eye of God noted was that there was a small fold in the mental pattern of Mark Slim III, and upon scrutinizing it discovered it was a small abyssal influence in his mind, allowing <i>something</i> to influence him in subtle ways he wouldn't notice. </span><br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;Surface Information<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Primary arcanum: Mind</li> <li>Resonance: influence</li> <li>Age: weeks</li> <li>Practice: Ruling</li> </ol><br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt; Deep Information<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The mystery is related to the Abyss</li> <li>The small pocket is a link to another mind that allows the other mind to influence Mark Slim III in subtle ways, much to subtle for him to notice a second mind in affecting him.</li> </ol>Finally, the Marks were called in to report any other items they were missing. Mark Slim began checking over all the other artifacts, while Mark Slim III beelined for the bookshelves and disapeared from the view of the mages waiting in the hall. Eye of God and Giger, recalling that Mark Slim III had been making some notes that involved a potential spell they decided to use this opportunity to sneak away and investigate his bedroom. Giger stayed in case they came out, but once Maxwell and Eye of God were in the room and saw the disaray of the place, Maxwell swapped places with Giger. Inside they found papers strewn across the floor, piles of paper on desks with his computer, and papers pinned to the walls with links of red strongs connecting some. Most of it seemed benign but they found several papers that detailed incomplete, imprecise in ways that would allow them not to function, summoning circles, complete with failed but recognizable High Speech runes. They returned and told Maxwell of this, who preformed a simple Prime spell on both Marks to discover if they were Sleeperwalkers, Mark Slim III is, certianly not ever trained by an order, but he still might be stumbling upon High Speech and some sort of magic on his own. Eventually the Marks returned, the elder still enraged but more composed, and the younger no longer expereincing the fear that he had been before. As the cabal was leaving Mark Slim III pulled Eye of God aside and told him he needed his help, and if he trusted the others them as well, and he would call him once he had what he needed to show them, to which the mage of course agreed.<br /> <br /> Once in Gigers limo he showed them a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gjw6GxwTbDHCCKFFp8UulZ5YZRDbMlq_imD8k-rPX4I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">note </a>he had recieved that morning from an unknown sender, they discussed what this could mean but went no further than that before Maxwell insisted they take a detour. He had decided it was time to enter the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The cabal called Ragnar, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;whose player had shown up at this point&gt;</span> informed him of their plan, and went to the hallow they had discovered while investigating Clausius. Eye of God opened a portal to the room where Todd was and were surprised to see two men standing in the room with him, and they were equally as shocked to see 4 men standing under a freeway. One man cleared his throat and asked if he may come through. He introduced himself as the mage Heinrich, who had heared about Todd from his Guardian friend, assumably the masked man that waiting still in the room, and had gotten permission from the Hierarch to take him to his sanctum where he could study his condition and also keep him safe from any sleeper that might stumble through the Guardian's ward. He used some Forces magic to hide the portal and assured the cabal that he wouldn't be moving Todd until that evening so they would have plently of time to explore the Shadow and return, and then gave Maxwell his contact informatin. &quot;This is still your mystery, I'm just also investigating the medical ramifcations of this now,&quot; he assured. He stepped back though the portal and the cabal entered the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"170\" height=\"246\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159320972361465886/c9c998072773c4ef82c7ca5efeaabea3.png?ex=6539d34a&amp;is=65275e4a&amp;hm=b6b2f9e55a7fc16bd2bd373139a38b7691e8ab301d178d6ea0986f59735415ae&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159320972361465886/c9c998072773c4ef82c7ca5efeaabea3.png?ex=6539d34a&amp;is=65275e4a&amp;hm=b6b2f9e55a7fc16bd2bd373139a38b7691e8ab301d178d6ea0986f59735415ae&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1159320972361465886/c9c998072773c4ef82c7ca5efeaabea3.png?ex=6539d34a&amp;is=65275e4a&amp;hm=b6b2f9e55a7fc16bd2bd373139a38b7691e8ab301d178d6ea0986f59735415ae&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Once through Giger observed the stands of Fate moving in and out of the portal and found one that would lead them closer to Clausius. They followed it through the Shadow, sneaking their way except for Eye of God, who was caught by a spirit of a traffic light that refused to turn green for him until he paid in essence. Maxwell had a creative thought and simply used Forces to make the red light seem green, and Eye of God passed, not before the spirit assured him he'd get to the bottom of this trickery. Finally the strands of Fate lked them to a building that was in a state of decay, nearly collapsing in on itself. Maxwell noted with his Forces sight that all types of forces were being expelled from the building. Ragnar noted with his Death sight that something else was happening as well. Inside the building the found a shadow that was just barely 3D playing o nthe floor, supurnal magic radiating from it. Maxwell used Prime magic to note the practice, unraveling, and that both Forces and Death were used in the spell. The nimbus they all felt with their mage sights caused them to become completely aware of the inevitable end of all things, the heat death of the universe. Maxwell decided he would not let this spell stand, but he also knew he couldn't end the spell on his own. The three <span style=\"color:#000000\">mystagogues</span>\u200b worked together to cast a powerful dispel magic spell led by Eye of God, and succedded. They decided not to wait around to see if the caster of the spell would come looking, and returned to the physical world. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;While this isn't super important they all decided they were dealing with a Master of Death and/or Forces.&gt;</span>\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:00:42-07:00","id":1524067,"title":"","content":"In the 2nd edition do all mages have an obession flaw? I noted it in your first post and was curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:07:20-07:00","id":1524070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1524067#post1524067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the 2nd edition do all mages have an obession flaw? I noted it in your first post and was curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions are a default mechanic for Mage now, basically extra Aspirations. You start with one and get more as you go up in Gnosis, which is good because you use them to earn Arcane Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:08:43-07:00","id":1524071,"title":"","content":"Arcane Beats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:10:05-07:00","id":1524073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1524071#post1524071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane Beats?</div> </div> </div> </div>5 Beats make 1 XP, which I think is standard across CofD. 5 Arcane Beats make 1 Arcane XP, which can be spent on most of the same things as normal XP but has a few things that can <i>only</i> be bought with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:56:30-07:00","id":1524075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1524073#post1524073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5 Beats make 1 XP, which I think is standard across CofD. 5 Arcane Beats make 1 Arcane XP, which can be spent on most of the same things as normal XP but has a few things that can <i>only</i> be bought with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Cauthon said, and you can also mix your normal XP with AXP for things like more arcana and gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T19:27:44-07:00","id":1524079,"title":"","content":"Ragnar finally spent XP, went up to Gnosis 2 and paid for an enhanced item, a ring with &quot;Kinetic Blow&quot; on it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Chapter 12</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">10/13/2023</span><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFind me, Necromancer\u201d The instruction echoes across Los Angeles. One at a time the dead speak the command, the presence commanding them jumps from specter to specter as she tries desperately to communicate her need. The echo reaches into the underworld, as hoards of ghosts howl out the plea \u201cFind me, Necromancer\u201d. The words echo down a hall, red with blood. In the center of the hall grows a tree of coagulated blood. From the bough of the tree hands a man, the noose and the tree the same. The warning reaches the ears of the hanging man, \u201cFind me, Necromancer\u201d and those words cause his eyes to stir and his mouth to smile. Finally, his time has come. </i><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Some fun foreshadowing I hit my players with at the start of this session.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Upon their return from the Shadow each member of the cabal had recieved voice messages. The mystagogues each had a voicemail from Architect asking them to meet him at 10 AM the next morning as something relating to one of their missions had come up. Ragnar had an automated voicemail informing him that all Moros were to meet in Architect's sanctum at 1:30 PM the following day for a path meeting. Eye of God had a second voicemail from Mark Slim III, saying he wanted to meet and to call him. They agreed to meet right away at a cafe near by.<br /> <br /> At the cafe Mark was suspicous of the other mages, especially Ragnar, who he had never met before, but he was convinced by Eye of God he could trust them and so he produced a book out of his backpack. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Instead of repeating it all here, a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1F5z3hnl73Lp02Q6XxWEMgA7MlJV3VbfmgHsgB26_9DE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">handout </a>that was made for the will be provided with all the informaiton they learned on the book.&gt; </span>Eye of God worked through the book, letting the other mages know they book discussed Abyssal cosmologies to which Mark inquired about. The cabal decided it would be best to further discuss with at Eye of God's appartment and they all returned there with Mark.<br /> <br /> Once there Eye of God decided he would play more Onrain Senshi. He encouraged the others to continue looking at the book and learned that Brandon was sure they were closing in on the final component for the spell, ten more hours and they would be the first ones in the world to cast the spell and see this secret part of the end game. Giger used Fate magic to make sure Eye of God would find what he wanted within an hour and began reading more on the book, finally Ragnar took the book and looked over the last section. Maxwell cast &quot;Pierce Deception&quot; and questioned Mark about the book, learning that he didn't know where exactly his grandfather had gotten it and he really wasn't sure what was special about the book, just that it was. HE was caught in a lie however when Maxwell asked if he thought his grandfather would do anything about the robbery, Mark replied that he doubted it but Maxwell caught the lie and saw Mark Slim fighting The Shadow That Walks. Giger agreed to talk with Mark the next day and the cabal tried to convince Mark III that the book was just some old biestiary from some crazy monks. He seemed disapointed and left. During all of this Eye of God had found the final item they needed and the players had gone to a location in game to cast the spell. It was clear to Eye of God that it was a real summoning spell they were preforming, but he reasoned that it was in game and therefore not going to work. Just as the spell finished everyone felt a powerful ping to the peripheral mage sights and the game crashed. Eye of God called Brandon, who did not pick up but then returned his call, very upset that the game had crashed and servers were down, he'd check in status of their world first in the morning and ended the call with &quot;Goodnight Jared.&quot; <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Not Eye of God's actual name, which is Johnny.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The cabal dispersed at this time to prepare for their meetings the next morning. </span>All but Maxwell felt a strange desire to write, Ragnar wrote on a blog and the others wrote in their journals that night.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Eye of God was complicant in summoning an Abyssal entity into the fallen world and had to roll a single dice for a wisdom check, which he failed. He gained the </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">megalomanical condition.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> The mystagogues arrived at Architect's office in the athenaeum and he asked how the investigation was going with Todd, letting them know he had heared about Heinrich taking his body to his sanctum but that it was still technically their mystery, at least for now. then Architect revealed the real reason he had asked them to meet with him, something had happened with Astrid, the potential dreamer they were asked to investigate and he asked if they had made any headway with her. Eye of God became frusterated at this point, saying he had been doing all the work and that is why no progress had been made and that this meeting was a waste of his time. Architect was shocked and allowed him to leave, asking Maxwell and Giger if he had always been like that. Maxwell reported he hadn't noticed if he was or wasn't and Giger remained silent. They continued the meeting with a video from a camera phone of a live preformance by Astrid's band &quot;Sea of Wolves&quot; in a bar. All of them felt a ping to their mage sight and then she locked up, opened her arms and looked to the sky and then death metal screamsed &quot;FIND ME NECROMANCER&quot;, and the magic vanished and she continued the concert like normal. With the use of Death magic they saw a ghost appear next to her, making the same motion and moving her mouth with Astrid, before vanishing. Architect stated it was likely not the fact that Astrid was a dreamer but instead a medium, and that he wanted to cabal to investigate this further, becoming the top priority for the cabal as far as hte work they had been given by the order, and that after this was resolved fi things weren't going well anymore as a cabal they could end their duty together. Maxwell got the video and information on where the concert was emailed to him and went to Ragnar, showing him the video. Ragnar was able to confim it was the same ghost he had seen puppeting Victoria's corpse in the morgue.<br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The meeting of the Moros involved every Moros in The Golden Order attended. I don't plan to drop pictures for every member that was mentioned during it, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gVx7e30wcz3HGmBOu8wBYFM89CgX20PhotYCC09sCXA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a link to the handout I gave to Ragnar at the end of it so you can see the art work for all the characters if you'd like too.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar approached the sanctum but before entering Vulcan stopped him, congratulated him on the work he has been doing and produced a gift for him, a leather bag. Inside he found a ring which she proudly told him to put on. As soon as he did he felt his mage sight go off and his body become different, like energy moved through it differently. He reported it felt good and she retorted saying she'd high five him but he might break her hand if he did, and to not hit anything he doesn't want to break while wearing that ring. The sanctum of Architect forced ghosts to manifest, Ragnar saw that most Moros here had a familiar with them, and his wyvrn coiled around him protectively as they talked. Victoria Adams was also there, standing among the dead. The meeting was about the fact that ghosts throughout Los Angeles all repeating the phrase, &quot;Find me, Necromancer.&quot; Crypt reported that ghosts in the underworld were howling this out still while the ghosts topside were not. The ghosts in the underwold had gathered in masses together. As they discussed how to investigate it Obeye insisted they leave it along, that the spirits of the dead should be left alone but noone agreed. Ragnar announced that a corpse became possesed by a ghost and grabbed him and said the phrase that way and that the ghost of Victoria Adams had become attatched to him after he broke the loop and spoke to her. Crypt found this curious, he had done that as well but she didn't bind to him. In the end the Moros decided that Architect would lead ghost summonings in the athenaeum, Crypt would keep an eye on the Underworld and call on Vulcan and Ragnar, both who had volunteered to help, if anything below should need his attention. Obeye refused to help in any way with this and left, cursing in her native language. The rest of the mages would investigate on their own and gain help from their cabal and they would meet together agian in a week. Ragnar noted Obeye still outside the sanctum when he left, cursing still.<br /> <br /> Giger called Mark Slim and went to visit. He found him letting off steam by attacking a punching bag, with good form. It turns out he use to practice boxing, he was professionally trained but never fought. He spared with Giger, who had trained a very small amount himself, and beat him but took it easy on him, letting him keep pace with him but not letting him win. They then discussed the incompetence of the police and how they are likely taking money to not solve this case. Giger told Mark he was going to try to look into the Special Agent, as he thought she might be involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 07-02-2025, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:44:23-07:00","id":1524646,"title":"","content":"Sorry mods, I'm sure the Chapter 12 post is getting annoying but I fixed all the little editing issues I had with it, so this will be the last time.","signature":"","edited":