a-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></b><br /> <br /> Love is War: <br /> <br /> \u200b<img width=\"250\" height=\"183\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1168265407426211980/wallhaven-83rlo2.png?ex=655122f2&amp;is=653eadf2&amp;hm=1a243635748896493af6a811d5b3839f290c2da79a47cc7f0c13f9786fd78a18&amp;=&amp;width=960&amp;height=540\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1168265407426211980/wallhaven-83rlo2.png?ex=655122f2&amp;is=653eadf2&amp;hm=1a243635748896493af6a811d5b3839f290c2da79a47cc7f0c13f9786fd78a18&amp;=&amp;width=960&amp;height=540\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1168265407426211980/wallhaven-83rlo2.png?ex=655122f2&amp;is=653eadf2&amp;hm=1a243635748896493af6a811d5b3839f290c2da79a47cc7f0c13f9786fd78a18&amp;=&amp;width=960&amp;height=540\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-29-2023, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:44:45-07:00","id":1524702,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 13</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">10/27/2023</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God rode his bike back from the athenaeum to his appartment after ditching the meeting with his cabal and Architect. One the bikeride home someone stepped out onto the street in front of him, he managed to dodge them and he turned to ask what their problem was but thet didn't seem to realize he was there. As he rode away he heard a car horn behind him, he turned to see the figure standing in front of the car, just looking at the driver. He decided to play the hero and returned to guide the stranger off of the street. He discovered they were a women, and despite any attempts to get her to speak with him he couldn't, instead he decided to look into her mind for answers. He learned, shockingly, that she lacked into compsure when he tried to peer into her thoughts, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Composure stat is 0&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and trying to find answers to things like how long was she in this state, what was her name, etc. revealed that she had no ability to comprehend these sorts of questions. Mage sight revealed that she had zero sympathetic links, and that her mind was flat, one-dimensional even, like a newborn. A mind existed, but there was nothing there to give it depth yet. Prime sight revealed to him that the symbols of multiple people seemed to be on this women, making her up. More Mind magic did reveal flashes of images, when asked about a home he saw a large, looming brick building, a sign on the front but she wasn't able to understand the words of it, so neither was he. An important person revealed a man in a lab coat, and he was also able to see the city as a looming mass of buildings, faceless people, and metal boxes, which he recognized to be cars. As he took her hand to guide to back to his apartment to do further Mind magics to try to figure out what was going on, he realized that her right hand was missing, this fact hidden by the hoodie.<br /> <br /> Back at his apartment he sat her down with a pen and paper and used Psychic Domination to instruct her to draw, she did, as while she did and for several seconds afterwards Eye of God felt the pressence of magic in his peripheral sight, as the woman seemed to collapse backwards and begin dreaming, when the dream ended she awoke with a &quot;Fuck&quot; and then looked around hte apartment, unsure of where she was. Eye of God explaimed that she was finally speaking and she looked confused at him, asking who he was. he gave her his sleeper name &quot;Johnny&quot; and asked for hers, which she told him she didn't think she had one. He explained the state he found her in and told her he brought her back to his apartment. He tried to convince her he was a mind reader and that he ahd read her mind, but she didn't seem to beleive her. She caught her own scent and asked to shower, he let her, and she started to take off her hoodie and realized she was missing one hand, she didn't seemed shocked by this, but also didn't seem to know about it.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"218\" height=\"218\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167636953894764635/Screenshot_2023-10-21_210615.png?ex=654ed9a7&amp;is=653c64a7&amp;hm=323342b334b024f05f682a5d33b5e4330062e610e0173788e9cc3cca09835120&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167636953894764635/Screenshot_2023-10-21_210615.png?ex=654ed9a7&amp;is=653c64a7&amp;hm=323342b334b024f05f682a5d33b5e4330062e610e0173788e9cc3cca09835120&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167636953894764635/Screenshot_2023-10-21_210615.png?ex=654ed9a7&amp;is=653c64a7&amp;hm=323342b334b024f05f682a5d33b5e4330062e610e0173788e9cc3cca09835120&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Here is the symbol she drew. You nerds will know what it is, my players don't, but she revleaed she thinks it represents her role in the world somehow. EoG was afraid it might be a symbol of the Eye but doesn't recall ever seeing this symbol used to represent the Exarch.&gt;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"250\" height=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167642943839010867/latest.png?ex=654edf3b&amp;is=653c6a3b&amp;hm=6f4587f1a4d304085847e60ed6cefcf4dcdc1b885f6555f0c60fb1d05b3cfb8f&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167642943839010867/latest.png?ex=654edf3b&amp;is=653c6a3b&amp;hm=6f4587f1a4d304085847e60ed6cefcf4dcdc1b885f6555f0c60fb1d05b3cfb8f&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167642943839010867/latest.png?ex=654edf3b&amp;is=653c6a3b&amp;hm=6f4587f1a4d304085847e60ed6cefcf4dcdc1b885f6555f0c60fb1d05b3cfb8f&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Eye of God then organzined with Maxwell and Giger to summon <i>The Worms of the Tapestry,</i> an imp that consumes blood and sympathy and uses what they take to restore the fallen world. They summoned this demon in the warehouse where they found the portal to the lower depths and closed the portal, finally putting Todd to rest, as was confirmed by Heinrich. The entire ordeal took 12 hours to complete the summoning and another hour for the worms to do their work. Eye of God used the &quot;Borrow Threads&quot; spell to trick the worms, giving them a duplicated sympathy of his to Giger.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"259\" height=\"194\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167651947822723092/download_1.png?ex=654ee79e&amp;is=653c729e&amp;hm=96ca2f03473bf5d3761eb4ae9562206961186d3cc3322e737f6a252da1912a91&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167651947822723092/download_1.png?ex=654ee79e&amp;is=653c729e&amp;hm=96ca2f03473bf5d3761eb4ae9562206961186d3cc3322e737f6a252da1912a91&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167651947822723092/download_1.png?ex=654ee79e&amp;is=653c729e&amp;hm=96ca2f03473bf5d3761eb4ae9562206961186d3cc3322e737f6a252da1912a91&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The Worms of the Tapestry, the demon they summoned.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> That evening Giger and Eye of God both noticed strange writing in the journals from the other night, not their hand writing and they did not recall every having that information before. Also, while asleep, Giger dreampt of a shadowy figure on top of his apartment building with him, screaming &quot;WHY? WHY? WHY?&quot; over and over again until Giger woke up.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"379\" height=\"251\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167654456863772782/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=654ee9f4&amp;is=653c74f4&amp;hm=a93a79f7b70a80f6109a93b8766841c696cdfb64ccd7eb5ca4636ef346d890bd&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167654456863772782/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=654ee9f4&amp;is=653c74f4&amp;hm=a93a79f7b70a80f6109a93b8766841c696cdfb64ccd7eb5ca4636ef346d890bd&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167654456863772782/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=654ee9f4&amp;is=653c74f4&amp;hm=a93a79f7b70a80f6109a93b8766841c696cdfb64ccd7eb5ca4636ef346d890bd&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The writing they found in their journals.&gt;<br /> &lt;that writing but without a weird font&gt;</span> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Upon the completion of the consumption of the daimon the true transformation of the Oneriose can begin. The blood spilled by the death of the daimon is mixed with the blood of the Crimson Truth. This profane mixture spreads throughout the Onerise to be consumed by the goetia living within the realm. Consumption of the astral blood causes the Goetia to begin to undergo&quot;<br /> <br /> The following morning Eye of God treated himself to a meat stick from his fridge and went to watch some Attack on Titan. His new guest was sitting in a shirt he had lent her, as her clothes were still filthy, and was able to see that her right arm, which he thought was just missing her hand, was gone up until the mid bicept. He didn't care too much though and watched aniume, refusing to answer any of her questions about it until later, when he took her to his place of work so he could regain mana. It was here that he spent more time discussing anime and manga with her, especially his favorite, Full Metal Alchemist. She seemed excited about this series.<br /> <br /> While preping for taxes with Leopold Giger felt magic in his apartment and turned to find an arm sticking out of space, the person who it was attactched too calling out for some help. He took hold and pulled a woman through. This woman was bleeding from some sort of bite on her leg, that she claimed was raptors, and had a bone in her other hand. Apparently she had been running from these raptors when she saw the tear that led to Giger's apartment and she slipped through, lamenting the lose of her pack and her gun. Giger interrogated her some and discovered she was part of the Mysterium in Los Angeles like him, that her shadowname was Starlet, and that she was part of a group of mages who explored the fractures of the fallen world. Giger was interested and asked how he could join. Starlet was unimpressed with him and offered to take him on an easy run in the future as an &quot;I owe you for popping into your home like this&quot; but with a clever use of Time magic, restoring her wounded leg to how it was before she was bit, he earned a little respect, and she said she'd take him on a more interesting run in the future. He showed off a little more but casting some Fate magic on her, and having her dial a random number, it was his. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\"><img width=\"340\" height=\"425\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167662544782106684/DzHvoQLWoAAHCD2.png?ex=654ef17c&amp;is=653c7c7c&amp;hm=010fb518d92a9d8238cbe4f45662aa82ad8caa86e1507f8eebf1db17a2ff96fc&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167662544782106684/DzHvoQLWoAAHCD2.png?ex=654ef17c&amp;is=653c7c7c&amp;hm=010fb518d92a9d8238cbe4f45662aa82ad8caa86e1507f8eebf1db17a2ff96fc&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1167662544782106684/DzHvoQLWoAAHCD2.png?ex=654ef17c&amp;is=653c7c7c&amp;hm=010fb518d92a9d8238cbe4f45662aa82ad8caa86e1507f8eebf1db17a2ff96fc&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> &lt;Starlet&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar was busy tonight, only showing up in time for the final scene of the session.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Finally the cabal went to investigate the bar the Sea of Wolves had preformed at when Astrid channeled the ghost and creamed &quot;FIND ME NECROMANCER&quot;. Before leaving Eye of God told his guest that she couldn't come, but he noticed her trying to follow him out of the apartment, surrounded by some sort of magical effect. He told her to go back inside. Maxwell visited with the bartender and then the owner of the bar, and recieved an email that he had been using to talk with them when setting up their preformance at the bar. While this was happened Ragnar visited with a ghost at the bar, whose face altered to the same ghost that had been possesing other ghosts and repeated the instructions, &quot;Find me Necromancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 14</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/1/2023</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Maxwell is gone for this session, traveling IRL.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;The first scene of this session we didn't RP. Eye of God wanted to get rid of his hubris condition so he used at work in front of Brandon and Jacqueline, ending his Megalomaniacal condition but gaining the Rampant condition, which he thren ended by portaling home, leaving him with 5 widsom by the end of this and anew obsession, to gain wisdom. This happened during the evening shift after meeting at the bar from the last chapter and he found his guest watching Attack on Titan, trying to catch up to him so they could watch together without her having to ask questions.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The cabal disperssed for the day whioe Maxwell tried to reach out to the Sea of Wolves. Giger had another dream that evening with the sme shadowy entity screaming &quot;WHY?&quot; at him, this time though it was a red streak near its shoulders. He recognized it to be The Shadow That Walks from the media.<br /> <br /> Ragnar awoke early, as he always does, and after his routine of meditation he traveled to the headquarters of the Adamantine Arrow, </span><i>Bibliothecam Animae Famem</i>, to try and gain information on the mage Thread-Cutter, who he believed was responsible for the murder of Victoria Adams and the other women who had died in public but unseen by the crowds of people. There he found Reiksman, looking over a map of the LA area. HE sensed magic was being done so he stood to wait, but Reiksman called him forward, obviously, without ever turning to notice he was there. Ragnar asked about Thread-Cutter, but his superior told him they did not keep detailed information on all of their Talons so it could not fall into enemy hands. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Reiksman read Ragnar's mind at this point to find out why he wanted to find Thread-Cutter.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ragnar was pointed to a Mystagogue named Darkened Winds, who was apart of the same cabal as Thread-Cutter until just several months ago, when the third member disappeared.<br /> <br /> Ragnar hosted a breakfast at Denny's for the cabal, where everyone met Eye of God's guest. It was here that Eye of God decided on a name to give her, being she couldn't remember her's and was certain she didn't have one, Jessie. Eye of God explained to her that sometimes friends get together in the morning for breakfast and coffee and she was thrilled to partake, ordering the same thing as Eye of God </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">It should be noted at this point that when Eye of God woke up this morning he found her watching anime and eating a meatstick.&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ragnar explained over breakfast about Darkened Winds, both Gier and Eye of God know this mage, he is the mage who oversaw their intiation into the Mysterium and gave them direction on their first steps into the Atlantean Mystery </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Maxwell too&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">. They went to </span>Lapis Vivus Templum to find him. Ragnar waiting in the lecture hall area of the athenaeum, the only place non Mysterium mages are allowed, while Jessie explored The Getty above. Eye of God knew that Darkened Winds travels North to San Fransico and South to San Deigo often, but was lucky enough to find out that he was in the Clockwork Room of the athenaeum. Together, he and Giger walked down a long wallway, where they could hear the stone of the athenaeum contracting and relaxing, as if it were breathing. They found a silver door at the end of the hall with a book infront of it. The door had no handle but Giger instructed Eye of God to write what he wanted to find in the book &quot;Darkened Winds&quot; and they could hear the sound of bookshelves being dragged along the floor for a minute before the door opened. Inside they found the bookshelves had arranged themselves into a path. They followed the path directly the Darkened Winds who discussed his failure and how he isn't surprised they sough him out over a potential murder case. He gave them the address where Thread-Cutter use to live and then asked them how they quests for the Atlantean Mystery were going before letting them leave. The entire time they were in this room they knew precisely how much time had passed due to the ticking sound in the room.<br /> <br /> Before leaving the Getty the mages found Jessie investigating a model of the Pyramids. She is certain she's seen the real ones before, and on the drive to Thread-Cutter's apartment \u200bshe used Eye of God's phone to research Egypt more.<br /> <br /> Finally, the cabal arrived at the aparment, a run down place in West Hollywood. They used Space magic to get inside the building and then the apartment and found the place filled with notes, like one would expect in a mages home. Giger realized they were in an Arcadian Demense and a pair of dog tags seemed important to his mage sight. Ragnar's mage sight showed a chest freezer in the corner of the kitchen as covered in piles of volcanic ash, and when he opened it he found a corpse. He recognized the corpse to be the missing mage Sarah Hilsburry, a Thearch and he guessed the cabalmate that had gone missing that broke up the cabal Thread-Cutter was a part of. Eye of God could not see the corpse but Giger managed to dispell the magic hiding it from him. With three spells cast in the apartment the cabal decided Giger would hide their nimbuses with his magic when they left, they then went into the bedroom to find the fae they had met before. She taunted them, insited that even if she couldn't harm them Thread-Cutter would once he had finished with the fourth, revleaed that Eye of God had a destiny attatched to him, and refered to Jessie as someone who had &quot;found a loophole.&quot; Ragnar managed to get pictures of Sarah Hilsburry's corpse and stole the dog tags hanging on the bokshelf before Eye of God created a portal for them to erscape through. \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-04-2023, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T13:58:07-07:00","id":1525030,"title":"","content":"Opps! I don't wanna get the above post pinged as potential spam but I forgot to add art for Darkened Winds, so here it is!<br /> <img width=\"145\" height=\"257\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1169469000363823134/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=655583e1&amp;is=65430ee1&amp;hm=d1cffdc11b7a2b38a7d264d8a530b46e97e9cc28cd18345c3ab11014684adbb5&amp;=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1169469000363823134/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=655583e1&amp;is=65430ee1&amp;hm=d1cffdc11b7a2b38a7d264d8a530b46e97e9cc28cd18345c3ab11014684adbb5&amp;=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/910681466311159818/1169469000363823134/Screenshot_2023-10-27_191121.png?ex=655583e1&amp;is=65430ee1&amp;hm=d1cffdc11b7a2b38a7d264d8a530b46e97e9cc28cd18345c3ab11014684adbb5&amp;=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T10:33:03-08:00","id":1525078,"title":"","content":"Where do you get such good artwork?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T17:02:35-08:00","id":1525138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1525078#post1525078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you get such good artwork?</div> </div> </div> </div>primarily google, but im also in some discord servers where other people find and share art so that does help. And i've also used some AI art generators when I really need a very specific look for a character, like the GotV Blood<br /> I really need to start citing artists more<br /> <br /> Edit: As things have been going on since I posted this years ago, I know longer use AI for any characters. Support real artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-21-2025, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T10:11:55-08:00","id":1525314,"title":"","content":"Thanks maybe I should use those formats to try to work out what my main character looks like in VTM or this series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T18:19:17-08:00","id":1525575,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 15</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/15/2023</span><br /> <br /> The cabal went to a nearby coffee spot to discuss what the next play was. While they waited for Maxwell to arrive Ragnar scrutinized the pair of dogtags, labled &quot;Galent Rodriguez, Navy Seal&quot; and discovered they were a soulstone belonging to a Rapt mage. Once Maxwell arrived both he and Eye of God used unveiling and knowing spells to learn that Thread-Cutter was a Gnosis 3 mage with Fate as his highest arcanum, and that he had two vices, impatient and wrathful, the obsessions &quot;Understanding his dharmachakra&quot; and &quot;Broken Oaths&quot;, and a strange virtue; &quot;Enforce the endings that the fated avoided&quot;. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;In my setting all subtle arcana can be used on a soulstone to gain information on them related to the relevant arcana.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The cabal discussed and cast spells, planned to use his vices and the virtue, which they identified as his fault, against him by using Fate veiling magic to make it look like Giger had somehow escaped a Fated end and then slashing his tired, provoking him into a battle. Giger did just that while Maxwell went invisible. On top of Thread-Cutter's apartment Ragnar saw a gthost, which fired and Giger and despite the ghost shield Ragnar had already cast, the bullet struck Giger, wounding him, though he could see no wound. The battle started between Ragnar's wyvern familiar and the ghost while the corpse of Sarah Hilsburry shambled into the alley way, acting as a shield for Thread-Cutter. Giger tried to send the corpse back in time but released a paradox that set him back in time instead, to the coffee shop, where he never left as the rest of the cabal did to keep planning. He attempted to call Starlet for more help but she didn't want to help them break into another mages sanctum while she didn't know either mage. He ended the spell, exiting a taxi as he returned to the present to join the fight, because of this time shift Eye of God was the one to slice the tire and be shot by Thread-Cutter. Despite this strange start and the preperations the Rapt had made, the mages over powered him. Even the support magic coming from the Fae woman wasn't enough and with a gun shot from Maxwell </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar had aquired a gun for him to use for the battle via Order Status&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and blue fire from the materialized wyvern ghost they managed to defeat Thread-Cutter without killing him. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Also I need to give credit to Eye of God, who opened a portal for Maxwell to fire through and rolled two exceptional successes on his Warp praxis for big damage.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> However the gunshot and the dragon drew attention, so they took Thread-Cutter into Giger's limo and escaped.<br /> <br /> Once there while they were trying to decide what to do with him, Victoria Adams materialized and attempted to use Threade-Cutter's own knife against him. With magic they prevented her from killing him and took him to the Adamantine Arrow, turning him over the Caeser, who let them know they would have to testify at his murder trial after they filled him in on what they knew about him. The cabal agreed. </span>\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T18:20:12-08:00","id":1525576,"title":"","content":"Maxwell increased his Gnosis to 3 and Giger increased his to 2 after this session was over, so we'll see what new obsession Maxwell selects <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T08:41:48-08:00","id":1526404,"title":"","content":"Tonights Session will include my players meeting the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1noCyi4YXrP_c6_TFNjE_a8ix5O9OtEZ68AuHUCbRu4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Council of the Golden Order</a> so there is a handout for it. They'll also learn about the Lex for the first time, so <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LCWd_O6q7TP4AeteJ-omaEvurXo0vLXiQxdWY2r27Mk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here is a handout on the Silver Laws</a> for my setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T16:00:44-08:00","id":1529526,"title":"","content":"Maxwell ended up not making it to the trial session so we did a filler, before the trial session. Ragnar didn't make it to the next session but it seemed at the time that Ragnar wouldn't be able to play with us anymore, so we went ahead and did the trial. Thankfully he is still gonna be around it seems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 16</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">12/6/23</span><br /> <br /> Giger had a nightmare where The Shadow That Walks screamed &quot;WHY?&quot; at him over and over on a rooftop. The next morning on the news The Shadow That Walks had left their calling card behind at a jewlery store that had been robbed. Not far away from there two men at been beaten nearly to death in an alleyway. Giger spoke with Mark Slim at his mansion and Mark Slim revealed he wanted to bring justice to the streets of Los Angeles. He also stated that there was no way The Shadow That Walks robbed that jewerly store, it wasn't high profile or rich enough for him. Giger noted bloodied and brused knuckles on Mark's hand before leaving. On his way out Giger tried to push the idea that the FBI agent in charge of the investigation was likely the Shadow That Walks, a personal theory of his, and that they needed a cop to help bring her down. Mark didn't trust any police, but would accept a true officer was wanted to clean up the police force in LA.<br /> <br /> Eye of God worked a shift at the manga store, where he discovered his friend Brandon had been storing his own snot in the breakroom as he was sick today. Eye of God obviously found this kind of gross which shocked Brandon, &quot;This is what you and I have done forever for when we wanna go home?&quot;. There is now a rift between the two of them because Eye of God reported this to his manager, who threw out the bag of snot and sent him home.<br /> <br /> Ragnar decided to investigate Astrid to find out if she was a medium, taking Giger and Eye of God with him. She didn't react to the pressence of the ghosts that followed Ragnar, nor most of the spells that were cast by the mages. Only after a spell from Giger that provoked the abyss by paradox did she react, vomiting and running to the bathroom, where she held up for a while. When she finally returned she passed the mages at the table, Giger having a paradox condition on him, and she retreated once again to the bathroom to vomit. The cabal decided to leave her alone. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;No the cabal has not noticed the paradox and abyssal condition being the important factor here, this specificity is for your benefit.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 17</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">1/3/24</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eye of God spent some time trying to find out what was going on with Brandon. His Mind magic wasn't strong enough to penetrate the depths of his mind yet, but it did get a response from something inside his mind. He also noticed some of Brandon's thoughts were clearly not his, but they were somehow still his. He needs more Mind magic to investigate this further he decided. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;He really wants Mind 3.&gt;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The Trial happened, it was mainly a narration with the PCs giving some testimony when asked. Thread-Cutter was found guilty and sentenced to death, which brought tears to Partriarch's eyes. The Interfector refused to kill the mage &quot;Killing a mage is too great a sin even for a Guardian to commit&quot; and vanished to complete the &quot;Rite of the Black Crystal.&quot; and would return in two weeks to fulfill his job as Interfector. Everyone would have to attend that was currently present. The cabal was found guilty of invading another mages sanctum and have to do some community service for the Golden Order in order to repay this, they got a job from the Guardian of the Veil councilor to investigate a strange anomoly, a building that no one had exited for the past two weeks. People came in, no one left.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Giger made a call to the police station to speak with detective Gordon W. James, the detective assisated the FBI lead and tried to sow doubt in his mind. He is unsure of how that went.<br /> <br /> Finally the cabal arrived at the edge of the a ward made by the mage Blood around the appartment building that no one was leaving...</span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;and that will continue in chapter 18.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T17:06:50-08:00","id":1532265,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 18 &amp; Chapter 19</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">1/12/24 &amp; 1/26/24</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Honestly, these chapters were so linked and a failure that I'll just post them as one. Honestly, I don't even feel like narrating this one. They found out via Time magic that Mark Slim III was in the apartment, and also saw all the people entering but not leaving. The whole place had been altered by a scelesti unleashing a really powerful paradox in the place while trying to kill a cabal of Banishers. I used &quot;The Twisting Maze&quot; from Intruders, Encounters with the Abyss 206-211 and eventually had to just give them the answer because they fumbled around for 2 sessions without me really communicating properly how to deal with the problem. They did end up finding one of the Banishers, Bianca von Veritas, and the scelesti. Maxwell Reversed Gravity and sent the Scelesti off into the abyss before they used the answer I gave them to save the place. They discovered an old stone obelisk which Giger realized was the Obelisk of Names. I'll give you more on that in the future. Bianca von Veritas is now in guardian custody with the rest of her cabal being dead. The cabal of banishers had killed a cabal of mysterium mages severl years ago and stole the obelisk to use as bait. The cabal did not decide what to do with Mark Slim III, that's for the next session. Gonna have to spend more time as a ST figuring out how I wanna use and communicate the abyss for sure, because that was the biggest problem as to why this failed I think.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2024, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T18:56:21-08:00","id":1532268,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you could try impossible synesthesia:<br /> <br /> &quot;As you form the Imago, your hands sting with the flavor of a routine delivery route &quot; - taking bashing damage from containing Paradox in the area. It also is a small nudge in the right direction, since anyone who does delivery in the area will have a very clear idea of how the area is supposed to connect and may help provide a bonus (or teamwork) to walk the correct path.<br /> <br /> &quot;You smell the sound of copper&quot; - Generic example.<br /> <br /> Lastly did your players try to analyze the area with Focused Mage Sight ? You could place the fact its an Abyssal Invader as surface information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T21:24:20-08:00","id":1532273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1532268#post1532268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly did your players try to analyze the area with Focused Mage Sight ? You could place the fact its an Abyssal Invader as surface information.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did, and they figured out it was abyssal pretty quickly, it was the fixing of it that was what I couldn't figure out how to communicate without just telling them straight out. It was a failed attempt at my first <i>ever</i> time using an abyssal manifestation so I'm not super demoralized but it was a failure for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T17:40:23-07:00","id":1533025,"title":"","content":"Had two players call out this week, and it ended up being a really fun session for everyone involved anyway!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 20</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">3/8/2024</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God and Giger took Mark Slim III to a cafe to discuss what had happened to him and the book he carried. Together they decided to tell Mark about magic, knowing he was a sleepwalker. They told him the book had magic in it, and that they would train him once he had rested. To prove magic was real, Eye of God opened a portal to his home, and they all stepped through. Mark Slimm III went to get himself some food, as he hadn't eaten in over a week after being trapped in the Abyssal maze, and there he and his grandfather, Mark Slim, began fighting in the hallway. The elder was worreid about the younger going missing for so lonmg, while the younger was concerned with the bruises on his grandfather's face. The mages snuck out, deciding not to get involved.<br /> <br /> Eye of God went to the athenaeum and did research on how sleepwalkers tended to be trained and begun working on a set of lessons for Mark Slim III. He then spent the rest of the day with Jessie, the homeless woman he was allowing to stay with him. She had become quite enraptured by both anime, seeming to want to impress him with her knowledge of it, and also ancient Egypt, insisting even that she looks like some of the pharaohs she was learning about. Unconvinced, but willing to investigate, Eye of God aquired a DNA testing kit, which he helped her do and sent in on her behalf.<br /> <br /> Giger recontacted Detective Gordan James to try to convince him that Special Agent Olivia Miller was The Shadow That Walks. While Detect James didn't seem completely convinced, he was willing to talk. Giger suggested they meet at the docks in warehouse 12 the next night, and went to investigate it before hand, wanting to scout the layout before meeting anyone there. It was quite easy for him to infultrat the docks, espically with the help of Fate magic to increase his luck, he quickly made his way to the meeting spot and begun investigating. He was in the rafters above the warehouse when he noted a shadowy figure walking along the rafters across from him, making their way to the side of the building he was on. He went to hide, and when he looked back to see if he had been spotted, the figure was gone. Instead they were now above him, and a battle ensued with...Batman? The person he was facing looked like Batman, spoke like Batman, and fought like Batman. Giger attempted throughout the fight to remove the cowl he was wearing but a force resisted him, not allowing him to learn the identity of the man behind the mask. He ended up need to use his grappling hook he carried with him to try and get the Batman out into the air to drop him, while making sure he himself wouldn't crash into the ground. The Batman glided down, reducing the fall but it still hurt him. At this point Giger had taken a beating and used Time magic to slow the Batman down to get a look at him. Even with the Batman slowed so much he was unable to move, <i>something </i> was still striking him. He did manage to remove the mask to see Mark Slim behind it. This, obviously, was a shock to the mage, who once again used Time magic to take himself back to the moment he was about to leave Leopold and enter the docks. Too Leopolds surprise he was now bloody and beaten and said, &quot;On second thought old friend, let's drive home tonight.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2024, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T11:21:43-07:00","id":1533454,"title":"","content":"Ragnar's player hasn't been here in a while as you can tell, we did show up late for this session and just kinda vibe as he got himself back into the swing of the story, so while he is present he didn't actively do much.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 21</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">3/22/2024</span><br /> <br /> This chapter begins where the last ended, with Giger, now in his home, dewling on what had happened. Before retiring for the night he had the sudden urge to write, anything, he just needed to write. He ended up writing about his childhood on the computer, putting together a memoir. The next morning when he read over it he found something he had added that he didn't remember, it read, &quot;The intruder appears as a crimson hawk, made of coagulated blood, that resides within the Oneiros, hunting the Daimon from on high. It has one goal and one goal alone, to alter the mind of its victim by altering their ability for growth by consuming the Daimon&quot;. Watching a recording of himself from the night before, he did indeed type that section, but he did not remember doing it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This technically happened the the same day the Eye of God and Giger had their session in Chapter 22, but Maxwell out of the blue decided he wanted to go through the first Atlantean Mystery this chapter, so we did it here with this scene. This was done in a private channel while the others chilled.&gt;</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Maxwell had earned the right to understand the Mysteriorum Arche when he had offered the soulstone of Thread-Cutter to the Mysterium, and now was finally to undergo the ritual. Darkened Winds, who had initiated all three of the Mysterium mages into the order and given them instruction on how to be worthy of the First Atlantean Mystery. Maxwell was instructed to preform the ritual in Prime sight, was given a drink with some sort of hallucinogen in it, and a knife. Then a bull was brought in, which also seemed to be drugged. Maxwell was instructed to slit the throat of the bull and abosrb its mana. Once he had he was instructed to release the mana back into the world, not spending it on a spell or other magic, just watch it be free. He still isn't sure how much time passed as he watched the mana meticulously prod its way through the ritual chamber. Watching it systematically explore he had a strange feeling that became a revelation about the Supernal, magic was alive. He felt a tender kiss placed on his forehead by Darkened Winds as he welcomed him into the deeper parts of the order. He wasn't sure when, but at some point Maxwell had started crying. Maxwell was allowed to read a page from a thick tome that Darkened Winds provided. This page was about the arcanum of Forces and how it was teh perfect example to demonstrate the Truth of Living Magic. Friction and momentum animate the world, gravity draws things in (and repulses things) and energies move from location to location, all evidence of how magic is living. Maxwell then asked if this meant the universe itself was alive, to which Darkened Winds replied, &quot;Yes, you see it as heat moves through the world and I see it with every second that passes.&quot; Maxwell was then given a new task, to prove he would be ready for the next step of his initiation into the mysteries, &quot;Retrieve the Heart of Entropy.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The next morning the cabal met at Giger's apartment, it was time to tap into the Dragon's Hoard and steal from it the God-Killer Sword. Leopold was there of course to assist in small ways, and Eye of God brought his new sleepwalker apprentice as well to assist, Mark Slim III. The summoning lasted for eight hours, with all mages being on the brink of collapsing, before the ritual failed. The room became dark for a moment and floating in the center of the circle was a darkness, pure black with a streak of red splitting it near the top. It seemed at once to be trying to condence itself into a shape and exspand outward until it was nothing once again, it was clear that the Abyss had managed to slip into the summoning circle meant for the Supurnal summoning they had been doing. It took on a humaniod shape, with the red streak being where the neck would be, and vanished, its laugh echoing through the room. Maxwell convinced Giger to return to the past to stop them, but when he rearrived that morning he could still see the Abyssal mark on all of them. Maxwell left immidiatlywhen Giger told him what happened, calling both Blood and Dante to have them keep their eyes open.<br /> <br /> With the ritual no longer happened Eye of God returned home with Mark Slim III to begin training him. When they arrived however Mark looked shocked and disgusted at seeing Eye of Godd's house guest Jessie, going pale when he looked at her. When asked why he said she looked like a corpse freshly pulled from a river. Shocked, but also excited, Eye of God told Mark this must be his inate gift as a sleepwalker, and asked Jessie. She confirmed that she saw herself like that in the mirror and assumed Eye of God did as well. They also slaimed she had makeup on that reminded them of what pharaohs would wear. Eye of God looked into her memory to find out if perhaps she was a resurrected queen of Egypt, but wasn't able to find any informaiton on that. He also looked into her memory for the idea of cars, looking for memories she had of them to see if she would remember cars being much older models but this too did not play out. They decided they would investigate together later and Eye of God began messing with Mark's relationship to Space, allowing him to slowly experience magic while safe in his apartment.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Giger had a meeting to attend with Detective Gordon James. Before however he went to the home of Mark Slim to set a fire, hoping to distract him from his potential night's work. It didn't work, he didn't set the fire, but he did manage to convice Mark Slim that there was a string of arsons in Koreatown. When he made it to the meeting he noticed with his Fate sight that fate here had been sliced apart, the normally silver strings now crimson,he recognized it was the abyss. He also saw someone leaning up against a wall. Unsure if it was who he was here to meet, he cast a spell so that he would encounter a potential ally soon and waited. To his surprise, within the hour Special Agent Olivia Miller arrived, calling in that an officer was down and running to the body leaning on the wall, which Giger had assumed was a mannequin set as a trap for him. The agent called to the mannequin, calling it Detective James, which convicned Giger to return to the past, right as he entered the meeting location. He crawled down to see for himself and it was indeed the man he was here to meet, sliced open and gutted, pinned to the wall with knives, and above him written in blood, &quot;4U&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2024, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T17:28:44-07:00","id":1533671,"title":"","content":"Here are two handouts I gave my players this week <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v9XhuX2YxRGiAxgybzDaeofBLFe_ewdKc1B50s5Zq_k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> one if for Maxwel, information he was given by the GotV on Clausius after helping them with the apartment building that was being sucked into the Abyss<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XOck10Sj-ExYbjDQuObM6bGedNzVmfbUxgQNnLumEj8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> one is a letter Giger found in his mail when he returned from the future after the failed supurnal summoning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T07:42:30-07:00","id":1533698,"title":"","content":"Based on the report from the GotV, I am going to make a guess:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Clausius is imposing the symbolism of the heat death of the universe on the Shadow. Since even spirits cannot survive long before being permanently frozen, their deeply ingrained instincts force them to do anything to survive. So they consume the only kind of Resonance that can exist in those areas: Clausius' own Nimbus. This turns them into Magath who then promote his goal. The reason they don't have his Nimbus on them is because <b>they already digested it.</b><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T12:34:24-07:00","id":1533759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1533698#post1533698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the report from the GotV, I am going to make a guess</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Exciting that someone is making predicitions about my game!<br /> I obviously won't say if you are right or wrong but I will say that Clausius's nimbus is the sudden pressence of the fact that the universe will end being pushed into your concious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T09:34:40-07:00","id":1533892,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 22</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/05/2024</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Giger watched as someone looked over the stone obelisk he had brought back to the Mysterium from the apartment complex &lt;Chapters 20 &amp; 21&gt; before Darkened Winds arrived to guide him through the First Atlantean Mystery, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;See Maxwell's expereince in the spoiler in the last chapter for details.&gt;</span> When it came time for Giger to read from the tome it was opened to a page on Time. He read that Time was the ultimate expression of the Truth the Mysterium teaches, that magic is alive, as Time allows magic to anchor itself in the fallen world. Giger asked a similar question to Maxwell, &quot;is the universe alive?&quot; While Maxwell was thrilled by the answer t othis question being &quot;yes&quot; Giger say it a hippy bullshit, and asked if what they were doing was even ethical, controling a force that was alive. In the end though he did ask what he could do to expereince the next level of the Mysystery, and Darkened Winds told him he must &quot;Bring to the Mysterium the Identity of 'G'&quot;.<br /> <br /> That evening Giger met with Starlet to see if he could handle the work that the Reality Stalkers do. They met at the National History Museum, anmd he was told to bring gear for hiking, food and water, and water-proof boots. She took him around the side to a tar pit, and handed him a fossilized tooth, letting him know that if they get seperated near their exit portal, the one that brought her into his appartment all that time ago, this would be the key, and to keep it on him. She also informed him that the place they were going was full of predators, and gave him a gun that he knew was enchanted in some way. She produced what looked like a rib, and a portal opened before them. Giger was able to spot a Mangrove Tree forrest beyond and stepped through into a swamp. Starlet followed right behind and they stood there while Giger got his bearings. It was hot and humid here, with strange fish swimming between his legs. He looked with Prime sight and could see that all the plants here, and the fish, gave off magic, almost like they would look if they were giving off heat. He also saw a huge source of magic coming from beyond the tree line above, almost like a sunset. They agreed that if they had time, they would check on that. Starlet was mainly interested in testing Giger and retrieving a pack she had lost last time she was here. Together they waded through the knee high swamp water.<br /> <br /> As they crept through the swamp Giger noted something sticking out of the deeper pools of water, and pointing it out to Starlet had her go pale with fear and duck behind a tree. She told Giger that she doesn't think it had seen them yet, and that it was likely a sleeping Spinosaurus. This had Giger excited, but Starlet wanted to completely avoid it. Giger recalled his first meeting with her when she came crashing into his apartment through a portal, her leg torn up by something, and he started to wonder what kind of dinosaur she had faced last time she was here. He convinced her to sneak away and that he would follow, but instead, using Time shielding on his phone, and then a Hung Spell with Shifting Sands in it, he approeached the Spinosaurus. He managed to sit on its back and get a picture of himself riding it before being launched into the water. He was about to end his Hung Spell, allowing him to travel back to the moment he and Starlet first saw the sleeping animal, but instead he decided to try and record some &quot;actions shots&quot; of the beast. This resulted in him being bit by the creature, and losing his left leg <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Player request to lose a limb here&gt;</span> and finally releasing the spell. The water around Starlet began to pool with blood as he truend, left leg missing, and he went even further back in time, to before going on this run with her. Leopold patched him up, and Giger saved the picture and video to his computer before releasing the shielding spell on his phone and casting another time spell to temporarily return his leg to him.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Originally this was meant to be a solo session for Giger's player to get to do this run, but it was as he was preparing to go back into the run with Starlet, armed with his new knowledge, that Ragnar's player popped into the discord to see what was up, and the timing was perfect enough to bring Ragnar into the store.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Before leaving to meet with Starlet, Giger called his cabal mate Ragnar, saying he was working on something and could use some muscle, and Ragnar agreed to help out. Starlet wasn't too happy to see a third mage there when she had only invited Giger, but Giger assured her he had done some Time magic to determine that having a member of the Arrow with them would be safest, so she agreed. From this point on everything happened exactly as Giger had first expereinced, but he led them away from the Spinosaurus much earlier.<br /> <br /> Together, the three mages traveled through the swamp until eventually they got out of it, into a field filled with holes several feet in diameter. While they were trying to figure out what made them, a creature flew over head, and this was the first time Ragnar knew what was happening in this world, a prehistoric type of place. They saw other dinosaurs but never had any interactions with them as they worked their way to a forrest edge, where they made camp for the night. Ragnar's familiair spent the night on guard duty, and Ragnar heared it calling out to the dinosaurs of the night. The next morning they made their way into the forrest, Starlet leading them to where her pack was at with magic, and Ragnar's familiar keeping an eye ahead of them, returning and guiding them away from any potential threats. Eventually, the group came across the corpse of a dinosaur, a small, turkey sized one. Ragnar was able to determine it had only died two days ago due to infection, but it looked as if it had been rotting for weeks. Regardless, both he and Giger took pictures with it, and even convinced Starlet to get in one picture. She instructed them not to share those pictures with sleepers, because all of the lifeforms here would trigger quintessence. Eventually they found her pack, which she took a map out of, which seemed to be a map of this land with &quot;X&quot;s over it, she added a new one and wrote &quot;To Giger's appartment,&quot; on it. They then went to the portal to leave.<br /> <br /> Before leaving though, Giger suggested that they try to trap an animal to sacrifice, reasoning that they animals here are filled with magic and must then restore more mana. They tried, luring a velociraptor into their trap, but they weren't able to do it in in time before the rest of its pack showed up. They all fled through the portal. Starlet let them keep the fossils she had given them, explaining that a fossil of an extinct animal would let them access the portal that brought them back to Giger's place, and the bone of an extinct animal would let them get into that world from the tar pit. While she was telling Giger she'd be willing to take her on another run in the future he asked if they could discuss the details over dinner sometime, and she agreed.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2024, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T13:46:13-07:00","id":1534158,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 23</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/12/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I felt like I failed to communicate with Giger that the scene of the murder from Chapter 23 was covered in Abyssal taint, so I communicated that and let him continue the scene from there.&gt;</span> Giger decided to wait for Special Agent Olivia Miller to appear on the scene again and try to speak to her. When she finally did arrive, he surrendered immediately but to no avail, she refused to listen to a word he said, handcuffing him and going to Detective James's body, so Giger once again sent himself back in time, this time looking over the body to see if he could gain any information on who might have killed him. The brutality of the murder and also the fact that the normally silver strings of Fate had become crimson led Giger to believe that the Abyssal intrusion from the attempted summoning was involved. He alerted his cabal after leaving the area.<br /> <br /> Eye of God went to his job and absorbed all the stored up mana from the hallow there. His friend Brandon was working, but avoided him for the little time Eye of God was there before he left to meet with his cabal, and Eye of God was not interested in approaching.<br /> <br /> The next day Giger was unavalible <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This is when Chapter 24 would have happened&gt;</span> but the rest of the cabal went to the harbor to investigate the potential intrusion. Ragnar used Matter magic to shape some copper into a fake badge, and Maxwell used it to talk his way into the harbor, which had a heavy police pressence. The three amges made their way to the warehouse that the body was in, Maxwell could see Abyssal energy everywhere due to his Prime sight, and upon enterering the warehouse, Ragnar turned on his sight as well, seeing a ghost standing near the body. All three mages noticed a fourth mage, dressed as a detective, near the body as well. He noted their pressence and continued about his work. Ragnar spoke with the ghost for a bit, who was indeed Gordan James's ghost, but it was unable to give much useful information, having not seen the attack. At this point the other mage approached and asked if they had any useful information. Maxwell agreed to share what they found, but away from the scene, the four set up a meeting for the next day outside the Getty. Before leaving Maxwell looked into the past of the corpse, he was able to see a figure in complete black with red scarf around their neck appear behind Detective James before vanishing, appearing behind him again when he was starting his car, stabbing him through the seat. The past cuts out for a split second, and then the body is already mutalated and pinned to the wall, the figure gone.<br /> <br /> Both Ragnar and Maxwell went to their respective order's libraries to research the Abyss before their meeting the following day. Both gained insight into the fact that the Abyss is unpredictable. An intrusion might look like the desired spell effect, it might be similar to the caster's obsessions, it might be anything and everything. Trying to see a pattern in the Abyss is impossible. However, Maxwell <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;who rolled an exceptional seuccess&gt;</span> Learned of an attempt to catagorize the Abyss in the form of a grimoire known as The Ialdabaoth Codex, in Abyssal bestiary that supposedly drives those who study it insane or simply results in their death, then vanishing from history to repear again. Maxwell recognized the description of the book given, it was the same book that Mark Slim III carried with him in his bag. Maxwell, at this point, also began to suspect that The Shadow That Walks was this abyssal intrusion that had snuck in during the summoning, and once it had existed it had always existed.<br /> <br /> The next day while getting ready to meet with the mage they had met at the murder scene, Eye of God discovered the DNA test results had arrived. Inside was a letter of condolences, wishing them the best for the lost of their loved one who's DNA they had sent in, he hid this note and showed the DNA results to Jessie. She is mainly Irish, with equal parts English and Scottish, and then a smattering of Norther Europe and Scandinavia, nothing suggesting Egyption heritage. This frusterated her.<br /> <br /> The meeting in front of the Getty with the mage, who introduced himself as &quot;Detective&quot; went well. Giger arrived in a wheelchair. Detective informed the cabal of several things, including that the time in which Detective James had been mutilated had been cut out of time by the Abyss and a warning about Special Agent Miller being a dreamer. He warned them not to let on at all that they were mages should they interact with her, as her astral partner was giving her powerful abilities of induction. In return they told him about the ghost and the little information that they gained.<br /> <br /> Once Detective left the cabal spoke with Mark Slim III about the book he had. He was glad to show it to them, and Maxwell let everyone know what he had learned about it. Mark assured them he felt fine, but it was clear he was not sleeping. Eye of God was also able to determine that the boy was dealing with a certain level of psychosis related to being obsessed with the book. Using Mind magic on Mark, Eye of God ensured he would sleep tonight, resting well. Maxwell did a quick look through the book to determine if anything in it looked like what he had seen by looking into the past, but found nothing. While he was reading, Ragnar recognized part of what he was reading, he had blogged once and some of the text had appeared in that blog, straight from the book. He asked Mark if he could keep the book for a bit, and Mark excitedly agreed, to everyone's shock. The cabal, unsure what to do with it, decided to store it at Maxwell's sanctum while they decided on a better plan.<br /> <br /> As they left, Maxwell asked Giger about the wheelchair. Giger invited Maxwell to come on a ride in the limo with him andf told him about how he lost his leg, complete with the video.<br /> <br /> That evening Giger found himself writing in his memior again, and this time the text included, &quot;The final result of this transformation is one of senseless, indiscriminate violence. The mind of the victim is filled with blood, and their life reflects this. The only way to save this person is ending their life before the Crimson Truth infects their very soul.&quot; <br /> <br /> Lastly, Eye of God portaled into Mark Slim III's room, found him sleeping, and cast an indefinite length &quot;Memory Hole&quot; spell to make sure Mark would forget about the book, and stole all his notes on it, hoping this would keep him safe from the books influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-18-2024, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T08:48:49-07:00","id":1534596,"title":"","content":"Maxwel is now at Forces 4, and Ragnar is now at Matter 4. Exciting times for the mages. Because Ragnar was gone for so long at the start of the year he's been sorta out of it, so we agreed to do a solo session to sorta get him back into the swing of things, both mechanically and story wise, but it ended up being two solo sessions, so here we go.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">JUST A NOTE!</span> I'm put a trigger warning in here for the first session, its not too bad but ya'l deserve to have a heads up.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mention of suicide, in the second paragraph of Chapter 24.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Both of these chapters happened during the same time period as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1532265#post1532265\">Chapters 18 &amp; 19</a> and explain Ragnar's absence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 24</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/15/2024</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">While the rest of the cabal were assisting the Guardians of the Veil with an Abyssal intrusion, Ragnar was sent to investigate three graveyards on behalf of the Adamantine Arrow. Each graveyard had a local well established ghost go missing from it over the two weeks. He was sent to find out why. He started in the Old Felows Cemetery, where a ghost known as Old Man Benjamin had been missing. Old Man Benjamin was a community man while alive, always helping those around him, and he was the same in death, helping the ghosts of the graveyard acclimate to their new state of existence. There were several ghosts still in this graveyard, and while casting Death spells to allow him to talk to the ghosts, the Supernal breached his soul, granting further insights into the ghosts he spoke too. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;He got an exceptional success on his spell to allow him to speak with the ghosts, so I gave him a condition that raises the rank of ghosts while he interacted with them to 2, so all the ghosts he spoke to gained a little bit of awareness to help him on his investigation.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> All of the ghosts her spoke fondly of Old Man Benjamin, and a few saw him leaving the graveyard, followed closely by a giant dog. Ragnar found, with the use of unveiling magic, that there were infact giant paw prints leaving the cemetery, they looked bloodied. </span><br /> <br /> He walked over to the Evergreen Cemetery where a ghost known as the Weeping Widdow mourned the lost of her new husband. He died in an accident in the first month of their new marriage, and the ghost was formed twenty years ago from the heartbreak of the widow. He used his unveiling magic here as well to look for the tracks, and found them all over the graveyard, pacing and prowling, espically in front of one ghost who simply stood at his grave, unmoving. The ghost only had half a head, and it became clear to Ragnar that the ghost had taken his own life and now stood over its own grave. As Ragnar approeached and the ghost became aware, it seemed angry with Ragnar, but still anseered his questions. Here Ragnar learned that it wasn't a dog but a wolf with red, glowing eyes. It had prowled the graveyard, selecting its prey. It spent a lot of time pacing in front of this ghost, and the ghost was certain it was trying to decide to take him or not, but it turned and took the widow instead, swallowing her in one bite. As Ragnar left, the ghost told him to stay away, it didn't like remembering. <br /> <br /> Finally Ragnar went to the World War I meusum and entered the hidden portal in the back to the Adamantine Arrow headquarters, went to the forges and spoke with Vulcan, telling her of the missing ghosts and the wolf that was taking them. He got a short lecture on ghosts while she took a water break from forging a chest piece, and tehn he went to the library, filling cabnits filled with informatino on different topics, where he spent the rest of the day in research on the Underworld.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Inbetween these two sessions I wrote up a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OcLCa5umps77Dnfq7LaNfaSMCvnYeFBdVJX7KxBGlQk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">handout</a> on information that Ragnar learned on the Underworld with his research.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 25</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/22/2024</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar went home for the evening after his research into ghosts and the Underworld had finished to rest. He woke early i nthe morning, sensing more magic than usual in his apartment <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;He has a familiar that is always pinging his mage sight, and also the ghost of Victoria Adams is hanging around him also.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and he also felt an anxious hostility coming from his familiar. With his mage sight active he was able to see a wolf sat beneath his window, glowing red eyes and the size of a horse, its eyes moving from Ragnar to Victoria Adams. Using his Eyes of the Dead attainment he spoke with the ghost while sliding his magic ring in his finger. expecting a fight. He asked the ghost why it was here and it let out what sounded like a mix of a growl and a laugh. It revealed it was here to take ghosts back to the Underworld, where they belong. Ragnar asked why, being the Underworld would eventually drain the ghosts of their essence, to which the wolf responded that it did not care what their fate was, only that they returned to the Underworld and his mistresses realm, where they belong. That set of a red flag for Ragnar as what he assumed was a ghost had also been encouraging him to find her vessal in Astird, the medium they had been told to investigate by the Mysterium. The wolf confirmed that this was teh same entity, and Ragnar asked how to find her. The wolf said if he gives up Victoria Adams, he will tell him, but Ragnar refused and a battle started in his apartment. <br /> <br /> The battle was short, with the wolf focusing on Ragnar and Victoria Adams. It did eventually manage to swallow Victoria, but with a powerful </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;and lucky&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Death spell Ragnar was able to force the ghost to vomit her back up. Ragnar, with the help of his Wyvern familiar, were able to then overpower and destroy the ghost, but not before taking a horrible bite from the ghost to his leg, almost sending him into unconsciousness. With the destruction of the ghost, boith Old Man Benjamin and The Weeping Widow poured out of its corpus. Both of them, and Victoria Adams, were locked in a dormant state. Ragnar went to wash himself while calling the Adamantine Arrow headquarters, where a ghost picked up and directed his call to the First Talon on duty. He informed them of what happened and within an hour another mage had arrived. He was scared on his face by many battles, but still excuded an aura of hope around him. He looked over Ragnar once and told him to wait in the car so he could recieve medical attention. The mage came down to the car a few minutes latter, the ghosts now bound up in bottles. <br /> <br /> At the Headquarters the mage helped Ragnar to the infirmary, where ghosts and spirits of health looked him over and then retrieved a mage dressed as a docotor, who preformed a small healing spell on Ragnar, not enough to fully heal his wounds, but enough to keep him from bleeding out, saying it was good to gain scars from battle and to let the body heal itself naturally when possible. The doctor mage gave the name &quot;Hacksaw&quot; before returning to his desk to work. The mage that had come to Ragnar's apparment told him they would find out what they could from the ghosts and then return them to their graveyards, at which point Victoria Adams would be returned to him, the amge seemed frusterated that Ragnar has destroyed the ghost instead of binding it, and when Ragnar asked how he did the mage said &quot;B+&quot;. Love is War then came in for a debriefing with Ragnar, told him he did fantastic work but his job wasn't over. They now knew what had taken the two ghosts, </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#999999\">The third ghost was confirmed killed.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> but not who it was working for, or why it wanted them, or where it was going to take them. Ragnar agreed, he had work to do before the ghost reformed in the Underworld and came again.</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T21:48:52-07:00","id":1535189,"title":"","content":"Eye of God's player is out of the country traveling during these two chapters, so we decided to distract ourselves by reexploring the dinosaur realm for fun. Ragnar also decided during this time that his new obsession for reaching Gnosis 3 would be &quot;Protect my cabal&quot;, so we'll see what sort of trouble that gets him into. Ragnar also had asked if he could gain Life 1 in place of Forces 1, which up to this point he hadn't used, so I let him make that change, so Ragnar is now a Life mage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 26</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/26/24</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This takes place after chapter 23.&gt;</span><br /> Maxwell and Giger invited Ragnar to ride in the limbo with them where Giger filled him in on the experience he had in the swamp before he had called in Ragnar for help. Together, the three of them agreed to return to that realm together to investigate more. First though, Giger had a meeting with the Hierophant, Moon's Reflection on Ocean's Surface, to restore his leg via guanxi. He met her, and two others, by a river in the mountains. Over the course of an hour she restored his leg, using Life magic to regenerate it as he lay in the river, allowing the water to flow over him and become his leg. His leg was as good as new, with a slight scar where the leg had been regenerated mid thigh, he promised to pay her back in the future. She of course, was happy to help.<br /> <br /> So then together the three mages stepped again through the portal, into the realm filled with dinosaurs. Maxwell used his Forces arcana to levitate himself aove the water of the swamp, and to mute the sounds they would make while traveling. Ragnar walked on the surface of the swamp water, and Giger used Fate magic in order to help them along their travel. Due to their surpresed sound and the luck Giger gave them they were able to pass through the swamp and the plains that followed to the edge of the forest quite easily, stopping only briefly for Maxwell to boop the nose of a brontosaurus. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Gave him an abeat for this, obviously.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">They campped for the night, and the next morning Ragnar boosted all of the senses of the cabal before traveling through the forest.<br /> <br /> While traveling towards the mountain range through the forest they came across an interesting sight, a wall of wood placed over some rocks, making a small shelter. Inside they found some stone that had been turned into bowls, and the remenants of a camp fire. Ragnar, due to his Life magic, was able to pick of an old scent and the cabal followed it deeper into the woods, leading towards the mountains they were already traveling towards. The scent led them to a cabin built against the side of the mountain. Ragnar's Life sight revealed that there was a semicircle around the cabin, which seemed to be keeping microorganisms away from the hut. Inside they found it to be a living space, a basket of fruit with magic coming off of it, and a desk with writing materials and journals. Ragnar looked into the journals to find scientific talk on evolution in one, and in a second talk of the potential evolution of mythical creatures, including a wyvern. Maxwell, looking over his shoulder as he read, noticed some signature markings of the Mysterium. And invetigating the fruit with the magic on it with his Prime sight, Maxwell realized there was a shielding spell on it, to keep bacteria off of it, preventing decomposition, and gaining the nimbus of the mage who had cast the spell, the sense of life trying to adapt to survive.</span><br /> <br /> After Ragnar had stuffed all seven journals in his pack, the cabal decdied to travel up a path into the mountains that was near the cabin.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 27</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/04/2024</span><br /> <br /> Maxwell levitated above the others as they hikied the mountain path up. From his vantage point he noted a dead dinosaur, an ankylosaurus that had been left on its back, its cuts ripped open. By looking back in time Giger was able to see that it was part of a herd traveling down the very path they were traveling up, and a bear sized predator leaped from a ledge, flipped it on its back and killed it before pursuing the rest of the fleeing herd. The dinosasur was not one Giger recognized. The attack happened just a day ago, but the corpse they had found seemed decayed well past just a single day. Suspicous, they continued to travel up the path, where Ragnar and Giger noted a crevasse in the mountain wall leading into a cave. Maxwell and Giger entered the cave while Ragnar stood watch outside it. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar's player had not yet shown up at this point.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Inside they found an old campfire, and a boulder that gave off magic. By looking back in time, Giger was able to see an old man where the rock once was, staring into the fire, deep in thought, before casting a spell and becoming the boulder. They prepared themselves, expecting an ambush, and Giger used Time magic to revert the rock to and earlier state, clashing with the spell the mage had cast on himself, and managed to convert him back into his human form. The mage was very upset, asking why they would inturupt his important research. They went back and forth for a bit before finally managing to calm him down while dicussing the dinosaur Giger had seen attack the ankylosaurus herd. The mage proudly admitted he knew of this dinosaur, &quot;Bessy&quot; he called it. It was an animal he had evolved from a T-Rex, the top of the food chain. They also learned he had been in this world for nearly four decades research evolution and that the cabin they had found was his. Asking where they were, he gave them a lecture on emanation realms, this one being The Lands Primordial, and how these sorts of realms fit into the cosmology of the universe, and how this one in particular was one filled with the Life arcanum. He also revealed to them the existence of the paragons, Supernal entities that existed within emanation realms. Finally, Giger asked what research he was doing in this cave, to which he responded, &quot;I am learning what it means to be a mountain.&quot; Giger asked if he could also learn what it was like to be a mountain, and the man agreed, turning him into a boulder for one hour. Maxwell tried to send him rolling back down the mountain, but the mage ended his spell so Giger wouldn't &quot;Break apart&quot;. After this, the mage asked Giger to release his magic so he could continue his research. Giger did, and the cabal continued up the mountain.<br /> <br /> After hours of hiking the mountain became too steep to simply walk up it, Ragnar and Giger took to climbing up the side of it, Maxwell, floated along next to them. The climb took an hour, and the two were aching at the top of it. While they rested they were able to see another forest on the other side of the mountain, and past that a great ocean that seemed filthy. Their mage sights revealed that the magical glow Giger had seen with his Prime sight his first visit here was coming from that ocean, which was like a sun giving off light to both Prime and Life sight. The cabal decided to hike down this side of the mountain, but stopped at the sound of flaping wings. A creature that looked like a humaniod Pterodactulus flew down to them, and with their mage sight still active they could tell this was a supernal beign. Awkwardly, Giger said hi to it, and it cocked its head in confusion at the talking monkeies. The paragon, Lykos, spoke in highspeech to them, and told them that monkies were not allowed near the ocean. Through the conversation they learned that monkies came from the ocean and then left and broke things because they are too curious, so monkies aren't allowed near the ocean anymore. Giger tried using magic and cleaver word play to get past it, but it refused to let them go until they had gotten rid of their curiosity, using Life magic to turn them into snails and returning them to the edge of the cliff. Eventually Maxwell left to get the mage, who was still a boulder. Lykos noticed the boulder and recognized it as &quot;Old Monkey,&quot; and pet it softly before Maxwell sent the boulder rolling down the mountain. Lykos used more life magic to turn the old mage into a snail and brought him back. In highsppeech the old man greeting Lykos and said it was good to see him, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;In highspeech, so the players knew he was telling the truth.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and then asked how he had gotten up there. Finally, Ragnar decided to simply use his Matter magic to make a hole and descend through it towards the ocean. Lykos followed them from above, but eventually the old man, who had transformed into a fox in the tunnel, veiled them for far enough that they escaped Lykos.<br /> <br /> Finally, near the ocean, the man started lecturing the cabal on anthropology and paleontology and how much he had learned about evolution from existing in this place for so long. When asked by Maxwell why he had been a fox in the tunnel instead of human he replied, &quot;Simply because sometimes we must experience life as a fox, young Maxwell.&quot; As the mages finally made it to the ocean they could feel an immense heat coming off of it, and the old man warned them not to touch it, as it would mutate them in a likely fatal way. Giger tested this by throwing a beetle into the water. It came out a few moments later, now the size of a large dog, and indeed it was mutated, dying shortly after leaving the ocean. The mage explained that this was the ocean all life sprung from, at least metaphorically. A small pack of T-Rex left the ocean at this point, and the mage explaimed, &quot;There you have! You've witness abiogenesis with your own eyes!&quot; Finally the man introduced himself as Darwin, from the consillium in London. At this point Ragnar's familiar was excitedly hoping around Darwin, trying to get his attention. Ragnar allowed it to manifest, to which Darwin explained, &quot;Bessy!?&quot;. As it turns out, he had spent time in this realm creating wyverns, Bessy as the first to give birth to new wyverns, but they didn't have a very long lifespan and went extinct. Giger, finally appeased, decided it was time to leave. Darwin turned all the mages into </span>Pterodactulus and they flew off to the portal that would return them to Giger's home. Before leaving, Ragnar returned the journals he had stolen. &quot;Americans, thinking everything belongs to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;And that was it, two fun, silly sessions while Eye of God was traveling IRL. Each of the mages here left with an arcane condition from being so close to this primoridal ocean that will allow them to cast one Life spell at one dot higher than they can currently cast, so 1 for Maxwell/Giger, and 2 for Ragnar. Was a fun time, back to abyssal intrusions next time.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 05-06-2024, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T18:55:42-07:00","id":1536023,"title":"","content":"Short session, being we spent a lot of time visiting with Eye of God's player about his trip and catching him up on everything that had happened in our lives while he was away.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chpater 28</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/10/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This chapter started out with a set of dreams or encounters that happened to the player at night.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Giger<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Giger awoke in his apartment due to his mage sight being triggered to find a masked mage in his bedroom, magic coming off of him. Before Giger could ask any questions the intruder asked for his shdaowname and order, Giger confirmed he was Giger of the Mysterium and tried to ask who the intruder was, but he refused to answer, &quot;This is your inquisition, Giger.&quot; The mage asked Giger about the intrusion he brought into the world <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;which happened in an erased future&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">and if he was doing everything he could do to correct this mistake, which Giger believed, and reported, that he was. Finally, as the mage was leaving, Giger asked why he cared and if he was doing anything about the intrusion, to which he responded, &quot;This entire town is filled with rot, don't be part of that decay,&quot; and left. Giger followed the mage to the elevator, where he went invisible, and Giger tried to stop him but the mage commanded he sleep, and he did, waking up back in his bed wher eLeopold had taken him after he found him sleeping in the hallway. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I don't remember for certain when it happened, but the mage had commanded Giger to do something and he did before this last moment as well, I think it was to state his shadowname and order, but I don't recall for sure.&gt;</span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <br /> Maxwell<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Maxwell drempt he was walking along the campus on U of C in the Winter. While he was surrounded by students he noticed a young man in the crowd, who likewise noticed him and approached. As he neared, Maxwell realized the man was his father when he was Maxwell's age. His father shook his hand and addressed him by his shadowname, asking how long it had been since they last spoke, and Maxwell admitted it was too long. His father disagreed, telling him he knew he was busy his their grand mission of ordering the universe. They spoke a bit about it and then his father asked if he was still planning on weilding the sword against the entropy god associated with </div></div> </div> </div></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Clausius. Maxwell said he wanted too, but first needed to clean up the problem from the last attempt. His father nodded in agreement and then asked if he still thought the sword was the best idea, &quot;Would you use it to kill Lykos?&quot; Maxwell said no, so long as Lykos didn't start destroying order or increasing disorder, to which his father replied, &quot;Do you think the sword will care about that?&quot; Maxwell found that question interesting, but before they could continue the line of thought the campus started shaking. His father sighed and started to walk away saying, &quot;He's at it again.&quot; Maxwell asked if this was his own problem he was dealing with, too which his father said, &quot;Maxwell, he's <i>both</i> our problem.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Don't know why its formatted this way, to be split into two spoilers.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ragnar's dream took him to the edge of a sea, the rocky shore covered in snow. A man called out to him by his shadowname seeming to be annoyed to see him. As it turned out, Ragnar had had this dream before, but he never remembered it upon waking. The man was dressed in a black robe with a long, gray beard and his left eye was missing. The stranger told Ragnar he had been waiting for him for one thousand years, and wanted to make him into the perfect warrior. Ragnar was interested in this, and asked how. The man told him he needed to come to him, but in order to do that he needed a key, motioning to his missing eye. One Thousand years ago another mage called himself Ragnar, and took the mans eye to use. When he died and went to the Underworld, he took the eye with him. Ragnar would have to venture into the Underworld to find him and reclaim the eye. Ragnar, finally, asked for the mans name, which was &quot;Langbar\u00f0r.&quot; Then he rode off on a six-legged horse.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;During the two days the cabal was on their adventure while Eye of God's player was away IRL, Eye of God spent the time teaching Mark Slim III, who has become incredibly distracted by something. This wasn't played out, just agreed upon that this is what he was doing.&gt;</span><br /> The cabal spent some time regaining mana at their respective hallows, while Ragnar taught a martial arts class at his dojo. Then they all gathered in Giger's apartment to fill Eye of God in on the trip to the emenation realm, and to decide what the next steps were. They wanted to hide away the grimoire, but Ragnar still wanted to look over it before they did. Then they talked about what to do about the abyssal intrustion. They called up the mage known as Detective, asking to speak again and work together to come up with a plan. He arrived a few hours later. During that time they mages attempted to recall what he looked like, even using Mind magic to attempt to recall his face, but they couldn't, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Maxwell also took advantage of the Perfect Recall spell cast on him to recall his last conversation with his father, which was a hug and a &quot;I'm so rpoud&quot; conversation with him before Maxwell left for LA.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> When Detective did arive, they confronted him about their inability to recall his face, accusing him of casting a spell on them, but he corrected them, the spell was cast on himself, to make up for the fact that he couldn't wear a mask like the other Guardians of the Veil. This calmed the cabal down some and, together with him they discussed everything they knew about The Shadow That Walks. After some time, Detective produced a shard of glass with some blood on it from the jewelry store that had supposedly been robbed incase Eye of God would want to do sympathetic magic to find the culprit, which he did not. <br /> <br /> Together the cabal and Detective came to the conclusion that there must be three Shadows That Walk. The first, and original, that Detective revealed he knew via magic that he would eventually strike at the awakened community, although when, where and why he did not know. Then a copy cat that had robbed the jewelry store, and then the abyssal intrsusion. Giger cast Fate magic on everyone, and they prepared to leave to the streets to &quot;run into&quot; the copycat. <br /> <br /> Before they could go though there was a crash in Giger's bedroom. A massive green kobold was there, asking where the food was. He had been sent by the Dragon, who knew that an abyssal had entered the world near the aedes it resided in, and it did not like that they were trying to steal from its hoard. Kobold warned them not to do it again, and they said they wouldn't. Giger left some food out for the Kobold to &quot;steal&quot; and they left on their way to find The Shadow That Walk's copy cat.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;A note, in DMs with Giger's player I found out that Giger felt something needed to be done to through Detective off his trail, as it was clear that Detective was obsessed with The Shadow That Walks. He doesn't want to kill him or anything, but he does want to distract him or otherwise lead him astray.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T20:16:05-07:00","id":1536730,"title":"","content":"Maxwell missed Chapter 29, and then Ragnar missed chapter 30. Sad days but we still played. Everyone is Gnosis 3 by the end of this post now, with Giger and Eye of God still deciding on their new obsessions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 29</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/24/24</span><br /> <br /> With Maxwell returning to the athenaeum to continue researching the abyss, the rest of the cabal and detective set off to encounter the second Shadow That Walks. They wandered the streets of Los Angeles for nearly a hour under the effects of Giger's Fate magic before overhearing a conversation between an off duty cook and an estranged woman in an allyway. Listening in, they heard the woman trying to get rid of some &quot;stuff&quot; that she isn't supposed to have. Guessing the Fate spell led them to this, Giger and Detective stepped in. The woman ran when Detective flashed his badge, and Eye of God took the bag, filled with jewelry, from the cook, who wanted nothing to do with this and went back inside. Giger, Detective, and Ragnar chased after the woman, and with some bad luck applied to her through for of Giger's Fate magic, they managed to catch her as her heel broke. They swore that she had no clue with the jewelry came from, and after looking back in time, and in response to sensing the supernatural in the past and sending both Ragnar and Eye of God's senses to the past, the cabal realized that a goetia that represented The Shadow That Walks had possessed the woman and used her body to rob the jewelry store. Off the cabal went to the Wiltern's top floor, where a Synese existed for The Golden Order to use.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish to dream dreams of gold&quot; was the passcode to both get a keycard to the room, and then enter through the Synese into the Temenos. Once there, Ragnar was seperated from the others, blown away to a realm he recognized as Alkahest. He followed the line of goetia to a throne inside a citadel and watched as concept after concept was thrown from it. Eventually he too tried to sit on it, but he was thrown off as well.<br /> <br /> Giger and Eye of God found themselves outside the Wiltern once again, only this time in the Temenos. The astral reflection of Los Angeles was filled with a strong police force, clearly keeping an eye out for someone, gaurding banks, museums and the like. Eventually Giger and Eye of God tried to enter a museum to get a sense of what they were gaurding in there. The police interrogated them a bit to find out what their buisness was before letting them through. Inside they found that every piece of art had a police officer next to it. Eventually curosity over took Giger and he reached out, with his foot, to touch a painting. The cop tackled him without hesitation, proclaiming &quot;We finally got him boys!&quot; as they cuffed him and took him away, while Eye of God stood shaking his head.<br /> <br /> At the police station Giger was questioned by the police, who assumed he was The Shadow That Walks there to steal art. He played along and eventually posted his own bail once he had convinced them he wasn't a criminal. However as he left he noticed he was being followed by an undercover cop. Finally, when he caught back up to Eye of God, and Ragnar used a subway tunnel from Alkahest to Metropolis, the cabal was together again. Before they could begin looking for the goetia that they had come here to seek out, the giant from Ragnar's dreams appeared in the crowd. She had sensed him, and came to speak. She told him she could sense the mark of Langbar\u00f0r on him, and asked if he knew that Langbar\u00f0r was the one who cast her out of her home before sealing the door closed with her here. Of course, Ragnar did not know this, and the giant asked Ragnar if he would help her to get home. Ragnar agreed, but asked why she had been cast out, an answer the giant did not have. He then asked how he could hlep her get home, and she told him he needed a key, the same key Langbar\u00f0r had told him to find, somewhere in the Underworld. Ragnar agreed to find it and then asked how to find her, she presented him with a familiar looking hound <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;the same ghost that had attacked him during his solo session in Chapter 25&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> but he realized that this was not the same creature, but an astral reflection of it. She told Ragnar that this hound would lead him to her, either in this realm, or the realm below. Ragnar accepted the hound and it entered his Oneiros. She told him to find her in either place, and that she'd be waiting for him, before turning to leave. Finally, Ragnar asked her name, to which she responded &quot;Hel&quot;. Finally she turned away and walked through the crowd, as the masses of people avoided her.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;An important note, here, Eye of God could see with his mage sight that she was a goetia, and Ragnar could see with his mage sight that she was a Ghost. This hasn't been discussed and I don't think its clicked for the players yet.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Lastely, away from the cabal Detective was at home heading to the shower and the abyssal intrusion that is The Shadow That Walks appeared in his apartment.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 30</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/31/24</span><br /> <br /> Maxwell met up with the cabal just as Hel was departing and was brought up to speed on what had happened, and Ragnar told the cabal he was going to go back to the waking world to look into where he could find the ghost of the warrior mage also called Ragnar. Together the remaining three decided theey would use Giger as bait to trap the Shadow that Walks goetia and interrogate it. By finding a place in the realm of wealth inequality and hiring a goetia of fashion to pose as art, and then throwing a party they managed to successfully lure the goetia in. Trapping it with four different spells before it could retreat, they began questioning it. It gave up no useful information, whispering to Giger &quot;We could have done so much together,&quot; before Giger decided to bring up an earlier verison of the goetia, at Maxwell's suggestion, so that instead of being all of humanity's thoughts on the Shadow That Walks they would meet the earliest version of it, when only a few people knew about it, hoping that the information it could give to them would be more useful. As Giger cast the spell, drawing forth an earlier version of the Gotia, a wall of blue light appeared around the goetia, and a man was suddenly leaning against the wall of the room they were in.<br /> <br /> The mage seemed quite annoyed by their pressence, and stated, &quot;I don't know any of you,&quot; before dispelling all the spells they had used to keep the goetia bound. The conversation went back and forth, with Eye of God trying to read his mind but failing to overcome his resistance, and Maxwell trying to learn about his abilities with Prime magic, but failing to cast the spell. The mage told them that The Shadow That Walks is his personal pet project, and he didn't want them getting involved with disrupting that. After a little bit, the mage offered his shadow name, Gyges, and told them that he would fill them in on what he was doing with the Shadow That Walks, but they had to swear a binding vow to help him bring it about. Giger and Eye of God wanted too, Maxwell did not without more information, which Gyges refused to give, telling Maxwell that it was bigger than he thought, but that the Shadow That Walks was not an abyssal intrusion <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;something Maxwell's players had been suspicious of in the meta text of the game was that the Shadow That Walks was always the abyssal instrusion that had been summoned, and it being a Time intrusion just existed before it had been summoned.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">In the end, Giger and Eye of God swore the vow, stepping through a doorway into a astral realm that seemed like a jungle and learning from Gyges that he had discovered an abyssal artifact that was capable of destroying supernal laws of magic, causing a break down in the way mages could use the Supernal. He had taken it from the scelesti that had used it but was unable to recover any of the destroyed laws, so he wanted to groom the Shadow That Walks into the perfect thief, &quot;After all, who better to steal from the Abyss than a master thief, isn't that right Giger?&quot; </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;this was meant to tip Giger off, which worked <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">. He then told the two to keep Maxwell distracted while he continued to work on the Shadow That Walks, and that he would call for them when the time was right. He informed them it shouldn't be hard to keep Maxwell distracted, as something was about to happen he'd be interested in. He then put his hand on Eye of God's shoulder and told him, &quot;I'm sorry, I wish you'd be around to see the end result.&quot; This, obviously, caught both mages off guard, and they asked what he meant. He got annoyed again, and told Giger to do his job as an Acanthus and look into the destiny Eye of God had. &lt;</span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Giger has known about his destiny since chapter 1, but never looked at it with focused mage sight or Fate magic to learn about it, so they have no clue what's going on with that.&gt;</span> Finally, they all stepped back through and the chapter ended.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I don't remember when in this exchange it happened, but Gyges cast a spell on the goetia to compel it to answer all their questions, as long as it wouldn't expose the identity of the Shadow That Walks to them until he's ready for that.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 06-08-2024, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T21:06:01-07:00","id":1538191,"title":"","content":"We hadn't played in a while so we spent most of this session catching up over the past month, so not a lot happened.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 31</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">6/31/24</span><br /> <br /> With nothing left to ask the goetia or Gyges, the cabal woke up from the Astral Realms. Giger went straight to see Mark Slim, who was staring angry at the T.V. he had. While they were away in the Temenos there had been another murder, who was killed is unclear at that point to the media, but the killing was in West Hollywood. Giger alerted the rest of the cabal to this and they met there. Giger spent the time waiting for Ragnar and Maxwell to show up using Fate magic to guess things about the cops standing guard at the perimeter in order to try to convince them he was a psychic. Eventually, the drop of a date, shocked on of the officers enough to call for Special Agent Olivia Miller to come back to talk to him. Eventually Maxwell arived and used his gift from the primordial ocean Darwin showed them to cast a Life spell, allowing him to speak to birds, to find out if they knew anything. The birds were shocked to meet a human that could speak with them, but sadly knew very little, just that the person everyone is interested in fell loudly in the building, but the birds didn't see it. Eventually Special Agent Miller arrived, and after speaking with Giger, who was trying to put on a show to impress on her he was &quot;gifted&quot; she arrested him, telling him that he had information that the public didn't have and this was classic psychopath behavior, asserting himself into the investiation under the guise of help. She took him back to the station to interigate, and told the officers there to bring the rest of the cabal. Eye of God talked them out of it, and Maxwell sent the bird after the police car, promising him bread if it brought information back to Ragnar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T22:21:41-07:00","id":1539975,"title":"","content":"One of the things I really love about running a game in Los Angeles is the fact I'm so close to basically everywhere that I use in the game. Up above in Chapter 26, Giger had his leg restored by laying in a river in the mountains North of Los Angeles. Well, just under a month ago I was on the trail again that I had in mind when I ran that scene and hiked down to the area where Giger would have laid in the water to have his leg restored to him, enjoy this picture of that pool.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"500\" height=\"667\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/910681466311159818/1262092106781167616/rn_image_picker_lib_temp_e7b2da94-2388-411a-a9de-db84d7ce525b.jpg?ex=66b3a8de&amp;is=66b2575e&amp;hm=1e866891cc36a8b95f1c448e49be8bd723e19b72fe0807faecfc3cdc45ca82c6&amp;\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/910681466311159818/1262092106781167616/rn_image_picker_lib_temp_e7b2da94-2388-411a-a9de-db84d7ce525b.jpg?ex=66b3a8de&amp;is=66b2575e&amp;hm=1e866891cc36a8b95f1c448e49be8bd723e19b72fe0807faecfc3cdc45ca82c6&amp;\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/910681466311159818/1262092106781167616/rn_image_picker_lib_temp_e7b2da94-2388-411a-a9de-db84d7ce525b.jpg?ex=66b3a8de&amp;is=66b2575e&amp;hm=1e866891cc36a8b95f1c448e49be8bd723e19b72fe0807faecfc3cdc45ca82c6&amp;\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> It is really pretty up there, especially in Spring. The trail is called &quot;Rubio Caynon Trail&quot; and if you are ever in the area, I highly recomend hiking up to at least the first of the two waterfalls.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 32</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">7/26/24</span><br /> <br /> With the cabal split up due to Giger being arrested, they had to decide what to do on their own. Giger found himself being forced to wait in an interrogation room for an hour alone before Special Agent Olivia Miller finally came to speak with him, two police officers following her in with boxes full of paper work. Her and Giger had a bit of a back and forth, her insisting to know what his involvement in the murders were, and he insisting that he is just something of an amature detective. Finally she pointedly asked why someone as rich as Ted, his sleeper name, needed to steal in kill, to which he finally decided to ask for his lawyer. Learned Hand, a mage from the Silver Ladder who assists the members of the Golden Order, arrived. He spoke with Giger privately about his involvement in the case, assuming that chasing The Shadow That Walks was an obsession of his, and then encouraged him to be much more discreate going forward due to how high profile this case is. He then assured him that this would be easy to get out of this time being they have no real evidence on Ted. Giger, remembering that his Fate spells implied that Agent Miller may be a potential ally to him, asked Learned Hand to attempt to smooth things over and get him in her good graces. When she returned Learned Hand managed to get his release, but any attempts to repaire any damage Giger had done was half assed and led to nothing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the rest of the cabal investigated the best they could. It mainly amounted to Ragnar entering a nearby building and attempting to summon the ghost of the victim, but nothing answered his call. He followed this spell up by casting a Life spell to boost his hearing and managed to listen in well enough that he discovered the apartment number of the muder, 204. They decided they would return that evening once things had settled down and Giger had returned to them. In the meantime, Maxwell had promised bread with seeds to the birds for helping him, so he fulfilled that. The bird that came seemed very frantic, not eating the bread and hopping around on the park bench Maxwell was on. Finally, Ragnar, used Life magic to understand the bird and heard it freaking out because Maxwell could no longer speak to it, insisting that &quot;they&quot; must have already gotten to him. Ragnar told the bird to calm down and that Maxwell couldn't talk to him but he could, to which the bird freaked out, having met two talking humans in one day.<br /> <br /> While they waited for Giger and for evening, Maxwell let Ragnar use his hallow to regain mana, and Eye of God returned to his apartment, where he found Jessie looking very worried as Mark Slim III paced back and forth, rambling. Eye of God managed to calm him down and find out what was wrong, apparently for the last few days Mark has been trying to remember something important. Something that he knows he shouldn't have forgotten, but that he cannot remember and it has been driving him crazy. Eye of God managed to convince him that it was all in his head, he hadn't forgotten anything and was just adjusting to the fact that magic was real and that he had experienced a few spells that changed the way he saw things. Mark seemed convinced by this, but it left Eye of God worried. He reasoned to himself that his Memory Hole spell must have hidden the memory but not actually stopped the obsessive thoughts and behaviors about it that the grimoire was causing. When the cabal decided to meet back up he brought both Mark and Jessie with them.<br /> <br /> The six of them found a single cop car outside the apartment keeping an eye on who was going in and out. With Mind magic, Eye of God made the officers inside think he was Special Agent Olivia Miller and that they were going to go look over the crime scene again. The officers gave them an apartment key and they headed off to 204. Inside, all of the mages felt magic, and activated their mage sight to see a swirling, crimson, liquid-esque portal was in the lviing room. Ragnar also saw what looked to be a Valkyrie hovering over Eye of God, but could not get its attention. Before they could act too much on this, they heard someone moving in the pathroom, and flash of red cloth in the doorway. As they approached, expecting to see the Shadow That Walks, they instead found Blood standing in the doorway. He too, was here investigating the murder. Maxwell filled Blood in on the fact that this was the abyssal intrusion he had called him about a week ago, and brought Blood up to speed on what they had learned. As they spoke, a crimson sphere came out of the bathroom and landing gently in Blood's hand. He lowered his head to cover his face with his hood and lowered his mask, eating the blood-sphere. Then he revealed who the victim was, the mage Detective, Blood's apprentice. He showed them into the bathroom, where the bathtub was covered in blood with the words &quot;PLEASE HELP ME&quot; written in blood on the wall above it. Giger looked into the past where he saw the abyssal manifestation appear, limping and moving slowly as if it were in great pain, before attacking detective from behind and killing him. As soon as Detective was dead time broke down, and Giger saw the end result of Detective's mutilation as the manifestation walked, no long limping in pain, out of the bathroom and vanished from the apartment. While this was happening, Blood created and consumed another sphere of the blood from the bathtub and ate it so Maxwell caved and asked what he was doing. Blood said simply that he was keeping Detective close to him, even after death. Then, once Giger's sensing had returned to the present, Blood used a spell on the blood to watch the death scene. Has the manifestation sliced up Detectives body it screamed, &quot;FOR YOU! I'M DOING THIS FOR YOU! PLEASE HELP ME!&quot;<br /> <br /> Lots of talk happened after this as the cabal, along with Blood, discussed what could be going on here. They came to the following conclusions about the manifestation;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The manifestation thought it was helping someone who was not present and that reality was hurting it in some way, simply by existing.</li> <li>The manifestation was a combination of something important to Giger and whatever they were trying to summon</li> <li>The important thing to Giger must have been his connection to Mark Slim, who he was helping with his attempts to catch the Shadow That Walks. It was also revealed to Mark Slim III here that truth behind the damage he was seeing on his grandfather, that he had been attacking criminals at night in order to gather inforation on who The Shadow That Walks could be.</li> <li>The summoning was over a sword that was meant to kill gods, and this had somehow been twisted by the abyss when the manifestation entered the world. Their best guess is that the manifestation is now killing figures of authroity</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;They are actually so close to what is going on here it was a lot of fun, going to take action in the next chapter.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T21:20:51-07:00","id":1540689,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately Giger's player has had some things comer up in life that is going to take his attention for a while, so he is going to not be involved in gaming with us while he focuses on other things. Because of this we decided as a group to put the Shadow That Walks stuff on hold and move on to other things, and we can return to it when Giger's player is back. And on top of that, Maxwell's player couldn't make this session, and we ended up starting late, so Chapter 33 is a short an uneventful one.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 33</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/10/2024</span></span><br /> <br /> A week passes with no new activity or insights about the abyssal manifestation the cabal had been dealing with. With the use of divinations the cabal discovered they would not be getting any new leads for quite a while, so they decided to redirect their efforts elsewhere for the time being. Giger announced he would be taking leave for a while to investigate his own matter in order to progress in the Atlantean Mystery <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;which is gonna get retconned most likely because of the IRL issues.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> but before leaving offered any spells he could cast for the party. Eye of God asked for information on his destiny and learned both what the destiny was and also what his doom would be. His destiny is to stand among the heros of legend, while he doom is to be murdered.</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God now is a disciple of the Mind arcanum and so he decided to draw on the deal he had made with the Adamatine Arrow and look deep into the goetia he and Ragnar had retrieved from the astral realm of Valhalla. He was granted access with Ragnar and looked into the source of the goetia. What he saw was an older woman with the Roman numeral III on her right hand, and a corpse. Eye of God was able to sense that the goetia had come from the corpse and represented the mans desire to consume souls. The room they were in seemed to be some sort of business executive's office overlooking Los Angeles. An older man with the Roman numeral V on his collar bone barged into the room to argue with the woman about not following the council's decisions and announced that she had lived for three-hundred years without the council. They had a back and forth before the old man left, the woman threatening to leave whatever council they talked about. She then threw the goetia into the astral and told it &quot;Cause some chaos.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eye of God and Ragnar contacted the Seer of the Throne Midas and told him they had the information. They went to see him and found him in a skyscraper, but the floor he was on was completely blacked out from the outside world. Greek style columns flanked both sides with statues of gold that looked earily like real people were about. Midas sat on a throne but decended to shake Eye of God's hand. He wore an orangish-yellow metallic glove, with an empty cup on the top and an overflowing cup on the palm. Eye of God quickly copied a memory from Midas as they shook hands <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;He had rolled an exceptional success on his earlier roll with the goetia, so I had given him an arcane condition that allowed him to copy a memory from one person he touched that would not provoke PMS.&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and learned that a fourth faction of Seers were moving into the LA area and trying to take power from the current three ministires, the Praetorian Ministry being the new one. Well, Eye of God gave him information he had gained from the goetia as promised, and Midas seemed troubled by this information, as if he knew were these two mages were, but when Eye of God asked if he knew who they were, he asked if that was the information trade they were making. Eye of God said no and instead asked for any information on Exarchal artifacts in Los Angeles. Midas told him he'd have it to him by the end of the week.<br /> <br /> The end of the week arrived and he received a text from Midas with three artifacts; The General's Axe which was held by a pylon of the new ministry coming in, Unitiy's Crown, which was held by one of the oldest Hegemonic mages in Los Angeles, and The Mask of Eyes, which was controled by a mage named Star Maker, who apparently was losing status with the Phemian Minisitry. Eye of God decided he wanted to steal The Mask of Eyes from Star Maker.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T20:28:44-07:00","id":1541378,"title":"","content":"I'm exhausted so here is a summary of what happened;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 34</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/23/2024</span><br /> <br /> Maxwell spoke with Giger about where he would meet Clausius, with his Divination magic Giger saw that he would confront him in a place called \u201cThe Weave of Entropy\u201d. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This would have been before Giger left to handle his own things, but Maxwell's player wasn't around for Chapter 33.&gt;</span> Maxwell did some research on this place and discovered that spirits were being transformed by shells of themselves within that place, becoming entropy elementals. Sadly that is all he learned, so he reached out to Dante, who also didn't know anything himself but knew of another mage in the Technocracy named Boltzmann who had a reputation for studying entropy and agreed to try and put the two of them in contact with each other.<br /> <br /> Eye of God managed to track down some stars who were \u201cup and coming\u201d in Hollywood who were affected by magic, and by tracking them down he discovered that they were all affected by magic with the same nimbus, the flashing of cameras. They all were being isolated from those around by Space magic, unable to connect with anyone. Eye of God followed them for a few days while performing magic on the sympathy that was connected to the magic until he finally tracked down Starmaker\u2019s sanctum.<br /> <br /> The place was covered in magic that seemed to be designed to help with surveillance and protection. The sanctum itself was situated on the top floor of a house that was being rented out, and with the use of Maxwell's Forces magic to make them invisible, his Prime magic to disable the traps, Ragnar\u2019s Matter magic to transform doors into one way mirrors, and Eye of God\u2019s Space magic to slip through the space between the doorframes and the door, they managed to get into the sanctum.<br /> <br /> Once inside they felt the presence of magic on the wall where several High Speech runes were drawn, and Eye of God, with Space magic and active mage sight, saw a creature that looked like Starmaker lurking in the back of the hall. He dispelled the magic in the runes which was some form of Mind magic, and the creature was pulled back into it. It was at this point that Starmaker himself started challenging the cabal verbally, accusing them of being sent by the Tetrarch to kill him. A one sided battle ensued where the cabal quickly overpowered the Seer, despite Starmaker being invisible, and prevented him from escaping. As he was preparing a final, last ditch effort spell to survive, Eye of God convinced him to surrender, promising that the Adamantine Arrow would protect him, and Ragnar agreed.<br /> <br /> Starmaker appeared from his invisibility and gave Eye of God a key from around his neck so he could access a side room in the apartment safely. Inside he found a shelf of books, pictures of all of the people that had been isolated by Starmaker's magic, and the prize he had come from, the Mask of Eyes. He took it and put it on, and immediately started seeing things from around the world, every few seconds his vision would shift to another place, until he took the mask off feeling discombobulated. During this, Ragnar phoned the headquarters of the Adamantine Arrow to alert them of his prisoner of war and was instructed to take him to an address in Anaheim. Together the four mages went there to find Hava Ntry, the Adamantine Dragon <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Adamant Sage&gt;</span> waiting for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-06-2024, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T16:36:23-07:00","id":1543600,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 35</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/14/2024</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar explained what had happened with Starmaker to Have Ntry, why they were there, how they found him, etc. She agreed that the promise Ragnar made that the Arrow would protect him should be honored. However she also did not trust him. Love is War arrived and cast a spell enforcing an oath on Starmaker, that he would not use his magic to harm or affect anyone guarding him and that he would comply with the orders of the Arrow while he was their prisoner, and that Ragnar would protect him and enforce those rules on him as well. Both mages swore the oath.<br /> <br /> The next day was the execution of Thread-Cutter. The entire council was there, along with members of the Bellerophon Group there, who the cabal sat with. Thread-Cutter himself was still there locked in time, Patriarch seemed to be trying to keep himself composed, while the Silver Ladder councilor Erinyes seemed pleased, even excited, about the pending execution. Before however, Caesar told the cabal to look at Thread-Cutter\u2019s connection to the Supernal, using Prime or Death magic, the cabal saw him as a mage, someone with an awakened soul in Ragnar\u2019s case, while Eye of God and Maxwell saw his connection to Arcadia. Then, the execution began.<br /> <br /> At Thread-Cutter's trial The Interfecter had refused to execute him, saying that the sin of slaying a fellow mage was too great for even a guardian to commit, and invoked the Rite of the Black Book before teleporting away. Today he had a black book in his hand, and as he invoked its magic it drew a black light from him, which turned into words in the book. When it was finished, which took only a few minutes, Caesar instructed the cabal to look again at Thread-Cutter, and found he was no longer a mage but a sleepwalker, who The Interfecter had no problem executing with a single sweep of the sword he was wielding. He turned to the Golden Council and declared their judgment and sentence had been passed, and returned to their station in the corner of the chamber to clean their sword. Patriarch clearly started sobbing silently in his throne after this, while Erinyes jumped out of her seat in excitement at the beheading.<br /> <br /> Starmaker was present for the entire ordeal and looked absolutely horrified by what had just transpired before him. And now it was his turn to stand trial. Again, Diamond\u2019s advocate represented him, but this was much more of an interrogation by the councilors and less of an actual trial, especially after Hava Ntry declared he was under the protection of Ragnar and the entire Adamantine Arrow as a prisoner of war. Undying Light insisted on a more thorough interrogation in the near future in order to gain any intelligence that might prove useful to the Guardians when it came to their work against the Seers of the Throne, and it was agreed that Ragnar would be present for that. Through the trial it was demonstrated that Starmaker felt absolutely no regret for how he was using and isolating sleepers for his own arms and the aims of his ministry. Undying Light set up a time for the next morning to have a Guardian with Mind magic interrogate Starmaker with Ragnar present.<br /> <br /> Maxwell received a phone call later that day from Boltzmann, agreeing to meet at his sanctum the next day.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Eye of God Spoiler&gt;</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Eye of God is a member of a secret group of censors that operate within The Golden Order, so he knew how there was a visual, but mundane, illusion that his a crack in the wall of the Athenaeum that took him to a secret chamber that served as the Censorium. He placed the artifact there with the assistance of another censor who went by \u201cA\u201d and cataloged everything he knew about it, as well as how he found and censored it. The Censorium itself was a large dome filled with strange, magic items. Some things Eye of God noticed were a large, golden sword, a large, black ax with a hollowed out circle in its balde, several bookshelves, filled with books and scrolls, that had chains dangling from the top and secured at the bottom, and many strange items that were likely soulstones. In a side room where he did the documentation work and filed it away was also a large time, filled with information on items the censors, modern and past, want to censor from the area but have not been able to yet. Eye of God layer underwent the first Atlantean Mystery that evening, which was the same as the other members of his cabal, except he read about Pandemonium and the Demons that reside in that realm when he read from the book at the end, and how like living beings adapt to the world around them and improve, the Demons force mages to improve in a certain direction so that all of magic might improve. He was then given his next task: &quot;You'll be ready to experience the next part of the mystery once you have revealed the secret of the Ley Line Vortex to the Caucus\u201d</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 36</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/20/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar was not present for this chapter. Eye of God is now an adept of Space&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Together, Eye of God and Maxwell traveled to Anaheim to meet Boltzmann. They found a building that looks like it once belonged to a university campus, and inside they found it was a mix between a library and a laboratory, with many equations written all over them that Maxwell recognized as various important and famous equations from physics, but different, more was going on with them. It didn't take Maxwell long to realize that they weren't just physics, but magic, a mixture of the mundane science and the Supernal, although he wasn't quite sure what he was looking at. Several things were revealed from visiting with Boltzmann. In no specific order;<ul><li>Boltzmann and Clausius knew each other before Clausius became Rapt.</li> <li>Boltzmann was aware of Maxwell from before his awakening and has read his dissertation work, believing he would awaken based on what he had read.</li> <li>Boltzmann is working to understand entropy, not stop it, and revealed his Forces/Prime/Death sight to both mages to help Maxwell understand that Entropy is just as much a part of order as gravity or friction is.</li> <li>Boltzmann had planned to recruit Maxwell to the Free Council and the Technocracy but the Mysterium got to him first.</li> <li>People and spirits that enter the Weave of Entropy return different. Clausius became Rapt, non-mage humans come out as empty shells of themselves, and spirits are transformed into entropy elementals.</li> <li>Sag\u2019suga Isim is not a spirit, despite it existing in the Shadow. Instead it is some sort of monstrous creature that is part spiritual and part flesh. Boltzmann has only ever heard of one other entity like this, something that slept under Paris until the end of WWI. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;A reference to a WWI WtF game I ran but never finished.&gt;</span></li> <li>An old woman from San Francisco faced Sag\u2019suga Isim with a group of others, only she survived.</li> </ul>Boltzmann provided a card he had of the woman, named Moon's Tears, and script underneath that the cabal did not recognize, so the cabal left to the Athenaeum to try and find out what the script was. They were unable to find anything, so they went instead to find Architect, who was speaking with an ancient and ugly man. While they didn't catch any part of the conversation, it was clearly very serious in tone. They interrupted and Architect pointed them to a section of the Athenaeum that had the records of The Celestial War, from when two types of werewolves had an open war between their factions in the 1990s, where they found a cipher written by Moon's Reflection on Ocean's Surface to translate the First Tongue into English. With that and some time they realized the script on the card was an address in the small town of Littlerock. Off they went to find her.<br /> <br /> They found an old home on the edge of town, some sort of magic existed around it that they did not recognize with their sights, and the fence around it had threats in the First Tongue. The old woman, covered in tattoos, did not want to let them in, so Eye of God used Break Boundaries to step through the crack between the door and the frame, and they entered her home, wher she immediately started to take on the form of a human wolf hybrid, but Eye of God explained they were after Sag\u2019Suga Isim, and that was enough for them to get her story. Apparently her pack of werewolves had faced the creature the year before, but it destroyed them before they even realized they were inside it. Whatever it is, they were able to walk into an incredible darkness, and that is what the creature is, an enveloping darkness. Or at least, that's the form it took when her and her pack tried hunting it. Maxwell told her he had a sword that might be able to turn the tide, Moon's Tears wasn't convinced a sword would have any effect on it, but told them that if they were going to hunt it, she wanted revenge for her pack, and they agreed. She doesn't use phones, so the mages plan to teleport to her when the hunt begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T17:59:15-07:00","id":1544244,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 37</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">10/11/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar was not present for this chapter, and after discussing with Maxwell and Eye of God\u2019s players, we decided not to try and involve an Acanthus in summoning the God-Slayer sword because they didn't want to expose the Aedes to a mage outside of their cabal, so the story from Chapter 36 is again on pause, because Maxwell wants the sword before going forward here so we are waiting on Giger to return.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God decided it was time to help Jessie figure out who she was, where she came from, and what had happened to her memory. Firstly he further investigated what they had learned from her Ancestry.com results, specifically, looking at her family tree on there, and finding a small list of cousins in the LA area on her mother's side that were predominantly Irish. After that he decided to look further into the memories she had, recalling specifically that she had a memory of a building. He used his Mind magic to transfer the image of the building from her memory to Maxwell, and then Maxwell used his Forces magic to cause a computer to create that image which they then reverse searched on Google Images to find that the building was the old Teaching Hospital at UCLA. Eye of God then used his Space magic to copy the sympathetic link Jessie has to the hospital and opened a portal to it. He told Jessie to stay behind and wait while he and Maxwell investigated it and they stepped through the portal.<br /> <br /> They found themselves outside the hospital but inside a gated part of it. The gate was locked, and when they approached the actual door of the building they found a padlock that was left unlocked. Once inside, Eye of God noted tracks in the dust. Maxwell redirected all of the Light in the building to where they were so they could check the place out without having to explore it and noticed, in the basement, two rooms that seemed to be in use, even though no one should be accessing the old building. They saw a surgical bed, surgical tools, and desk with notes on alchemy, and a part of the floor that had been dug up to reveal the sewer system. In the room next to it was a freezer that was padlocked and hooked up to a generator.<br /> <br /> Eye of God quickly looked over the rest of the notes on alchemy, not actually spending any time trying to read it to understand them, just making sure his eyes had seen every word so that he could use Mind magic later to recall what he saw. Then, he used his Space magic to unlock the padlock around the chain it was securing and opened the freezer. Inside, he and Maxwell found several body parts, mainly legs and arms, but also a jar filled with eyes and tongues. A bit shocked, they decided to find any right arms that could have been Jessie's, and then Maxwell used his Time magic to view the past of each arm until he found out which one belonged to her. It only took him two attempts to find the correct arm. Each time he saw a person, a woman both times, strapped to the surgical bed, unconscious, being sawed apart by a man completely covered to protect him from the gore of his work. Jessie's mutilation happened two weeks ago, which lined up roughly with when Eye of God found her and also as far back as her memories go.<br /> <br /> Together the mages left the basement via another portal made by Eye of God and went back to his apartment, where he asked Jessie not to look and hid her arm in his own freezer. He told her what they found and asked if she wanted her arm reattached. She admitted she didn't know and asked if she should. Eye of God said that having two arms has its perks and also pointed out that she might be right handed, so she might find things much easier with her right arm reattached. She agreed to give it a try if he thought it was a good idea.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;We ended the session there, a lot earlier than usual, because both players wanted to launch right into reattaching her arm and I needed to do some prep work before that happened, so we agreed to just game instead so I could do some research and get ready for this.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-19-2024, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T12:47:09-07:00","id":1544808,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 38</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">10/18/2024</span><br /> <br /> The conversation between the mages and Jessie continued, with Jessie feeling nervous about the idea of reattaching her missing limb, but she decided to trust Eye of God's judgment and consented to trying. Together Eye of God and Maxwell went to the Athenaeum to request the help of a Life mage. They found Architect, Darkened Winds, and the same elderly mage from before. Architect heard out their request and sent Eye of God to the part of the temple that had records in spirits to find a mage named Shadow\u2019s Muse, while he sent Maxwell to find a mage named Uriel.<br /> <br /> Shadow\u2019s Muse was reading from some sort of scroll when Eye of God found her, and he recognized her as \u201cM\u201d, another censor. Uriel was reading from a Bible in a small side room of the temple, the room was filled with books, scrolls, Stone tablets, and other records. Maxwell looked at a stone slab that seemed to be instructions on how to deal with Abyssal manifestations but didn't spend too long in the room, leaving with Uriel, but not before peaking at the part of the Bible she was reading, Revelations. The two mages were instructed to assist Eye of God and Maxwell with reattaching the arm of a sleepwalker as an act of Guanxi. Neither mage seemed overly concerned when they heard what they were being asked to do and consented to helping immediately.<br /> <br /> When the four mages arrived back at Eye of God's apartment they found Jessie watching Fullmetal Alchemist. As they prepared to reattach her arm Jessie asked if the main characters of the anime reminded him of them, but couldn't figure out how to elaborate on what she felt, so he wasn't really able to answer that question. Uriel spent some time sewing the severed arm back on the Jessie, while Shadow\u2019s Muse cast a spell to reduce the pain while that was happening, and then cast the spell she was asked to cast, allowing the natural healing properties of the body to work where they normally wouldn't, allowing the body to reattach the arm over a period of time. The four mages spoke for a moment about the logistics of the spell and how long it would likely take for the arm to be fully restored before leaving. On her way out Uriel gave Maxwell a look up and down, giving the impression she knew about him and was sizing him up for something.<br /> <br /> The three spoke for a bit, trying to decide what their next step should be now that Jessie's arm was slowly healing. Maxwell decided to step out and call his father, telling him he was planning on visiting home tomorrow. At first he was worried that something had happened, but once Maxwell assured him everything was okay he was excited to see his son and quipped that he was looking forward to the home cooked food Maxwell's mother would be making. Maxwell started discussing with Eye of God about helping him get through airport security the next morning when both of them felt something happening as Jessie grimaced and cried out in pain. Both of them could see with their mage sights that something was changing about her arm. Eye of God sprung into action, opening a portal to the Getty and running down to find Shadow\u2019s Muse, calling out that something was happening and they took off together back to the portal and leaped through.<br /> <br /> In the apartment a battle ensued as the reattached arm broke and fused the bones in the forearm and hand into a bone blade to fight back the mages, while the spot that was connected to Jessie began chewing. At first all three mages used magic to try to destroy the arm, with Jessie failing to do any real damage while striking at it in a panic, but eventually Eye of God began using his Mind magic to recall the notes he had skimmed over in the hospital and magic to help enhance his own mind so he could make better sense of them. While he did gain information the amount of paradox his body had to withstand was staggering, and he almost began dealing real damage to his body. He ended up getting the faintest sensation of stepping back through that portal to The Garden of Eternal Rot <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;See Chapter 2&gt;</span> but pushed it away as he realized what needed to be done. By this time Maxwell and Shadow's Muse had managed to use magic to blast the arm out of the stitches, so it was flailing itself around on the ground, the part of it that was connected to Jessie like a lamprey\u2019s mouth. All three mages realized that their magic was targeting the arm as if it was a separate creature from Jessie, damaging the arm but not her.<br /> <br /> Eye of God gained two different insights from the alchemist's work. Firstly, the ritual the alchemist was performing is one of fallen magic and seems to date back to Egypt from the time of the Pharos, drawing on the mythology of Osiris. A body must be cut into 14 pieces, and then put back together with one of these pieces missing, submerged in flowing water, but beyond this it is unclear what was done, but he knows it only worked after a fever dream the alchemist had, and it only worked once, on Jessie. The second thing he learned was of a source of power the alchemist called Azoth, with two different forms, like Yin-Yang or the two sides of a coin, Pyros and Flux. Creatures of flux were attracted to creatures of Pyros and would try to consume that pyros. Using his Prime magic, and assisted by Maxwell, he tried to draw out the flux from the arm but couldn't, so instead Shadow's Muse bound the arm in iron and took it to the Athenaeum to censor it, agreeing with Eye of God not to write up any details on how it was found until they were there together so he could be as vague as possible about Jessie.<br /> <br /> Both mages then went to their hallows, Maxwell drawing the mana out with magic and Eye of God meditating, trying to avoid Brandon who was there working, and trying to keep Jessie calm, for she refused to leave his side.<br /> <br /> Once back at his apartment she went into a panic attack, saying she trusted him and it backfired, that she didn't understand what had happened to herz she didn't understand why her capture has done what he did, didn't know why she had such strange memories, and didn't know how she was supposed to defend herself. Eye of God could sense something was happening with his mage sight, and saw that there was a core part of Jessie that was trying to change into something else as she struggled with what had happened. She begged him to start taking her with him in adventures so she could learn to defend them both, or so that she could learn about what she was. He didn't want to because of how bad she was at fighting, so she asked him to put her in contact with Ragnar so she could learn. At that moment something changed in Jessie, that part that Eye of God saw was trying to change, changed, taking a new shape and with it, Jessie changed, becoming more aggressive and standing taller before him. He challenged her to stroke him, trying to make a point. With the help of his Space armor attainment she missed, but it was clear to him that she would have broken his nose without it. He let her text Ragnar, and she deleted the text. He reminded her he could just read her mind and get the answer to which she responded, \u201cMaybe the fact that I deleted it should be enough for you to know that you shouldn't.\u201d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T14:53:44-08:00","id":1545266,"title":"","content":"This was supposed to be a Halloween session but nothing I did inspired me to want to run one, so we ended up just having a normal session. Happily though, Giger\u2019s player has returned, so while Ragnar is still MIA dealing with the workload of the season, our Acanthus is finally back. His return made the session a little chaotic but we live for that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 39</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/2/2024</span><br /> <br /> This chapter started with Eye of God the morning after the battle with Jessie's arm. As he left his bedroom he found her not in the couch she was usually relaxing on, but instead next to it doing sit-ups. He wasn't able to not notice how tired she had become literally overnight, whatever had happened to her had not only changed her personality but had altered her body somehow. Eye of God offered her a second chance at striking him, and still with his Space armor she missed, this time leaving a hole in the drywall. She seemed proud of that and left for a run.<br /> <br /> Giger and Maxwell worked on getting mana from their hallows, but Eye of God had a strange experience while at his. Brandin, his coworker and friend, came up to him while he was reading the manga that the hallow stores the mana in, to ask if he needed help checking out. Brandon has no clue who Eye of God was, clearly disturbed by the familiarity that the mage had for him, and was even more disturbed when Eye of God asked about him collecting snot. When he returned from work he told Jessie that Ragnar invited her to his dojo to train and she left immediately.<br /> <br /> Giger went to spend time with Mark Slim. It was clear that he still wasn't sleeping over the past week, still obsessing, still insisting that The Shadow That Walks was still out there, insisting that The Shadow That Walks is pathological in his theft and murder. Giger, wanting to help calm him down, ended up taking him to 71 Above, a restaurant and bar, where they both drank together until Mark finally seemed relaxed. Once back, Mark Slim III seemed relieved and helped Giger get him to bed before asking if he had talked to Eye of God recently. Clearly there was something more there but Giger couldn't pick up on it.<br /> <br /> Once back at his apartment Giger texted the others that he had spent the last week studying and believes he discovered a way to deal with The Shadow That Walks Abyssal and to meet at his apartment, but not to bring Uriel <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Maxwell had brought Uriel but once the God-Killer Sword was mentioned she started asking questions and Giger rewound time to avoid her being there.&gt;</span> Eye of God brought Mark Slim III with him as his apprentice. Here, he asked to cast a spell on Eye of God, rewritten some of his history where he \u201cgave it his all\u201d while trying to summon the sword but the summoning still failed, so Giger finally decided to accept the inevitable. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;For months now Giger would give Eye of God crap OOC about not spending a point of willpower during that summoning to give him the extra dice he needed, causing them to fail by one success. Finally that feud is over it seems, was a funny reuniting scene.&gt;</span> The cabal decided it was time to attempt the summoning again, and as they prepared they heard police sirens in the distance.<br /> <br /> The summoning was successful after only three hours of work, smoke billowed out of the summoning circle, threatening to choke the mages out before finally receding and revealed a cave mouth. Giger told Maxwell he needed to enter alone to pass the trial. The cave turned quickly into a perfect square shaped hallway covered in High Speech, with curtains having negative space that hurt Maxwell to look at for too long. He started to walk through the hallway but triggered a trap and took an arrow to his leg <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;no, not to his knee&gt;</span> and decided to levitate across instead. Then he came to a doorway that was covered in more runes and images of dragons and gold. Above the door, in High Speech, read \u201cI am a dragon's distant cousin, small, bright and true\u201d. Instead of trying to answer the riddle he used his Prime magic in the door, forcing it to open enough to get in. Once inside he saw the God-Killer Sword, a silver-blue great sword. Around the corners of the room were other artifacts and piles of gold. He took the sword, which was surprisingly light, and then went to look at another artifact, a helmet-crown that gave off an aura of authority. His Prime magic revealed that the artifact had Mind and Fate magic associated with it, and he decided to take it also. Once he left the treasure room the entire hall started shaking and he heard a roar come from somewhere deep within, \u201cTHIEF! YOU STEAL WHAT IS NOT YOURS!.\u201d He got out as quickly as he could, the helmet vanishing once he left the cave and the sword growing heavy in his hand and stabbing through the floor of Giger's apartment.<br /> <br /> Giger and Eye of God were able to hear the roar of the dragon as well, and even after the ritual ended, both mages were able to see a dragon coiled around Maxwell in their mage sights. Eye of God\u2019s Space sight showed him many new eyes <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Sympathetic connections&gt;</span> staring at Maxwell with hatred and fear, and Giger saw golden threads spew from the sword and weave themselves into a thick rope around Maxwell's neck, wrists and ankles. Giger also suddenly felt uneasy with Maxwell in his apartment and decided they should get the sword back to Maxwell's sanctum. Maxwell used gravity magic on the sword and they drove to his apartment, where the three mages worked together to cast a Prime veiling spell to hide the Supernal nature of the artifact for the time being.<br /> <br /> The final moment of the session had each of our mages hit with a shockwave of magic and Eye of God saw the world around him change, becoming dark and falling apart. When he heard Maxwell groan from the overwhelming magic it sounded like a far off whisper and bitch Maxwell and Giger seemed to be almost invisible to him. When he looked down at himself he was in black robes that were bound to him with a chain. All three of them saw Mark Slim III was overflowing with Supernal energies, and Eye of God realized that his apprentice was awakening and that he had been pulled into the Mystery play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T15:35:23-08:00","id":1545969,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 40</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/11/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This chapter happened before Giger returned in Chapter 39, and was a solo session with me and Giger.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;In order to understand the gravity of this chapter for Giger, we need to understand Giger\u2019s history that has not been revealed to the cabal. In 1999, Giger was still a child of 10, obviously unawakened, when his mother and father were killed brutally in an art deal gone wrong. This eventually inspired him to become The Shadow That Walks, as he decided that no one should be killed over priceless items, because no one should have that much to begin with, so he began stealing from the ultra wealthy, those who flaunt it. In addition, Leopold has always been in his family's service as a butler, although Giger would learn of his time in the British Intelligence Forces until he was older, he was a member of it until his father asked him to leave to serve the Murphy family as he had, convincing Leopold to stop being a spy and start acting as a butler for at least the past thirty years.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> This chapter begins with Giger leaving the Dragon\u2019s Hoard after successfully summoning and completing the trial of The Thief King\u2019s Cloak, an artifact he knew would give him the capabilities not just of a master thief, but of a thief that would lead other thiefs, he was also aware of the doom that came along with the destiny; betrayed. He watched as golden threads erupted out of the cloak and became a rope that bound his arms, legs, and neck. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I pointed out to him that there were no accusations of being called a thief like what had happened in Chapter 39 with Maxwell, but Giger currently has no context for that. There was also no smoking or roaring chasing him out. When Giger stole from the hoard the Dragon remained asleep.&gt; </span>As he recovered from this he heard congratulations coming from the doorway to his apartment. Gyges, the mage he and Eye of God had sworn to help reclaim truths from the Abyss, stood in his apartment, clearly pleased.<br /> <br /> Naturally, Giger was curious as to why Gyges was here. Gyges told Giger <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I am regretting my naming choice&gt;</span> that he has been waiting for Giger to retrieve this artifact from the Dragon's Hoard so that he could continue shaping him to his purpose, needing his Gnosis to be the correct shape in order to be able to steal from the Abyss as he needs it to be. In order to work towards this, he had a job he needed him to do. Twenty-three years ago, in 1996, a mage known as \u201cThe Clockmaster,\u201d was arrested for practicing Abyssal magic, specifically, trying to pull alternate timelines from the Abyss. He was eventually excommunicated, as his grimoire went missing, which was the strongest evidence for his intent. No one knows if he hid it or destroyed it himself, but it was never found. Gyges wanted Giger to return to his life in 1996 and retrieve the grimoire before it went missing. While it isn't exactly what Gyges is trying to do, it is adjacent, and therefore might prove insightful.<br /> <br /> Giger agreed, so Gyges cast some spells on him, transforming himself into his seven year old form, warning him that he'd need to hide the unmaking effect on himself to not draw attention, and swearing an oath that he'd lose his limbs if he didn't allow Giger to dispel the unmaking effect so he could return to the present, before finally sending Giger to the past.<br /> <br /> In the past Giger found himself in Beverly Hills, in his family's home there. He could hear the shower running, and saw his mom, reading not far from him. He ran to her to hug her, which she was pleased with. Giger made her promise to take him to play at the park later before running to his room to hide and cry. Once he had his cry he cast Time veiling to hide that he was displaced in time and noticed his spell did not trigger his peripheral mage sight, somehow Gyges had blocked it, so no one would notice Giger using spells.<br /> <br /> Giger went to find his father, who was freshly showered and visiting with his wife. Giger ran to him, told him he loved him and announced that they were going to the park later to play and that his dad should come. His father agreed and looked sadly at Giger, but Giger couldn't figure out why, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;0 Empathy&gt;</span> but his Time sight showed that Time around his father seemed to be chewed at the edges somehow. He would investigate later.<br /> <br /> Giger eventually got to himself and used Fate magic to dial a random number to bring him closer to The Clockmaster. On the other end of the phone a familiar voice answered, after talking for a bit he realized it was Blood. He told Blood he was investigating The Clockmaster and wanted to exchange information. Blood agreed and they met at a cafe nearby. Giger used magic to make him look like his adult self and met with Blood, who was completely different from the Blood Giger knows from the present. They discussed what they knew, Giger revealing that he knew The Clockmaster was a mage of the Mysterium and Blood sharing that they knew he was active only within Los Angeles. Blood told him of another Thyrsus, Eternal Elm, that could perhaps get them into the Athenaeum. They met her, explained they were looking for an Acanthus of the Mysterium, and asked if she could help. She seemed to be friends with Blood, so she agreed. Together they went to the Getty.<br /> <br /> Beneath the Getty they were confronted by a mage who introduced himself as Adam. Giger explained what was going on, and that he was also a mystagogue, flashing the sign he had learned from the First Atlantean Mystery, and Adam responded by showing him the sign saying he was higher along that Giger was. Adam was happy to help them regardless, but insisted that he would be nearby to keep an eye on Giger, and that Blood was not allowed to touch anything.<br /> <br /> They went to the Spiral Room, where all the Arcadian/Acanthus lore was stored. A book rests outside this room, and when a mage writes what he is looking for he can hear the room rearrange itself so that whatever information he sought would be at the center of the spiral. Giger eventually found information on a battle between Adamantine Arrow and Guardian mages vs members of the Doomsday Clock. At first he thought nothing of it, but then realized that there was no mention of the Mysterium being involved in the battle, so the mage who wrote this must have been looking backwards in time to see it. The Abyssal monster the Scelesti were using could not be destroyed so instead they trapped it, killed two of the four Scelesti, one killed himself by accident when his paradox sprung out of control, and one escaped. The author of these notes was Chrono, and Giger decided to investigate this Chrono more. Adam said he knew Chrono, he was an Acanthus studying a specific Fae that could tap into all magic from the past, present, and future, and was trying to find a way to do this himself.<br /> <br /> He, Eternal Elm, and Blood went to where his sanctum was in Beverly Hills, in an apartment complex. Giger had the other stay behind and checked the room out. No one seemed to be home so he broke in to find the living area filled with books. Looking over them, they were on the topic Adam had said Chrono had been interested in.<br /> <br /> Looking further he found what would have been a bedroom filled with more books, a dozen ticking clocks, a grimoire, and some Abyssal symbols written along the wall. As he opened the door he felt a spell go off and a portal open next to the grimoire to a study somewhere else, a study he recognized, the study he wasn't allowed in, his father's study.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I forgot to mention this earlier, but Giger was constantly casting Time unveiling and knowing magic to try and find information on The Clockmaster, but kept losing the clash of wills.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> His Father, Chrono, The Clockmaster, stepped through the portal. He did not seem mad nor happy, more like he was resigned. Giger introduced himself and the two spent some time sizing each other up, his father told him that he assumed he was powerful, because he couldn't get through his defenses with his own Time magic, and Giger used Prime magic to discover his father was a second degree master of Time and Fate. Eventually of course, Giger revealed his true identity, allowing his spell to end and reverting to his seven year old self in front of his father. Chrono held \u201cTeddy\u201d, sobbing.<br /> <br /> Giger asked if he knew he and his mother would die, Chrono revealed he did, no matter what he did he couldn't seem to escape that path. Giger pushed, revealing he needed the grimoire, but also asking why he would do this in the first place if it would lead to Giger growing up without parents. \u201cI killed her,\u201d was his father's response. During his awakening, which happened right after Giger was born, he accidentally erased Giger's younger twin sister from existence. He had spent all his time since then trying to find a way to restore her, and had eventually turned to Abyssal magic.<br /> <br /> Giger told him that he would grow up without his mother and father because of this, to which his father replied that they were all living without his sister, but after a moment, agreed with Giger. He rose, cast a spell on the grimoire, and handed it to Giger. He would go back into his own past and not delve into the Abyssal magic, he would stay true to the Supernal so that Teddy would have his parents. Before he did though, Teddy, along with his parents, had a beautiful day in the park, playing catch, chasing each other, and otherwise having a day as a family.<br /> <br /> That evening, before dispelling the unmaking spell keeping him in the past, Giger went to see Leopold. He needed Leopold to take him to Paris to gather information on a rival he had in the present. He revealed to Leopold, who he knows is a sleepwalker, that he was from the future, to which Leopold responded, \u201cI know.\u201d Leopold, who had served his family Giger\u2019s entire life, Leopold, who looked exactly the same in 1996 as he would in 2019. With unveiling magic, Giger realized that there was a hidden spell in Leopold keeping him from aging. When Giger inquired about it, he simply said \u201cThat's a conversation for twenty -three years from now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Giger did make it to Paris and gathered some dirt in a future rival.<br /> <br /> Once back in the present Giger gained a second set of memories, memories of the new timeline where his parents lived, and his father was a hierophant and mentor to him. He now went as Chronos instead of Chrono, and it was a secret of their relationship to other mages of the Mysterium, both as mentor and student, and father and son. Gyges took the grimoire from Giger and told him he made an interesting choice, thanked him for his work, and left. Giger is now suspicious of Gyges, who is doing magic that is similar to what had gotten his father banished from the Golden Order.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger had spent XP and moved some merits around to purchase his father as a five dot merit, but until he takes infamous mentor, that relationship is a secret.&gt;</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-27-2024, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T12:14:50-08:00","id":1546005,"title":"","content":"I am surprised Giger didn't try a reflexive <i>Exceptional Luck</i> to see why his father looked sad, but that would have led him to ask a whole lot of questions.<br /> <br /> An Awakening where he killed his own unborn child, that is horrifying, its amazing he didn't become a Banisher. Still, two generations of mages from the same family, Awakening to the same Path and choosing the same Order. I wonder if either of them find that suspicious.<br /> <br /> Even more suspicious is that Leopold knew Giger was from the future when Chrono did not.<br /> <br /> I am getting some <i>Flashpoint Paradox</i> vibes here, but for now, good for Giger saving his family.<br /> <br /> Was the spiral path room an intelligent golem with an archivist field ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T17:40:26-08:00","id":1546011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1546005#post1546005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am surprised Giger didn't try a reflexive <i>Exceptional Luck</i> to see why his father looked sad, but that would have led him to ask a whole lot of questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did a poor job here of comunicating it, but in the conversation between them in Chrono/The Clockmaster's sanctum it was made clear that the look was because he knew Ted would be losing his parents in a few years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1546005#post1546005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Awakening where he killed his own unborn child, that is horrifying, its amazing he didn't become a Banisher. Still, two generations of mages from the same family, Awakening to the same Path and choosing the same Order. I wonder if either of them find that suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well <i>technically</i> he just stopped her from being born but yeah, if I was in his shoes I don't think it woulde matter to me. <br /> <br /> I did think about making Chrono a Banisher but I have another Banisher in the setting that they met last night in Chapter 41 who has a similar situation going on and didn't wanna over do it, also thought it would help to get Giger to be suspicious of Gyges, being Chrono got arrested and killed for what he was doing, and Gyges is doing similar work. That worked,, he isn't sure if he trusts Gyges anymore which is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1546005#post1546005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more suspicious is that Leopold knew Giger was from the future when Chrono did not.<br /> <br /> I am getting some <i>Flashpoint Paradox</i> vibes here, but for now, good for Giger saving his family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got some logic behind that but we'll see if it actually comes up or not, although Giger does wanna have a talk with Leopold so I've got a feeling it will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1546005#post1546005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was the spiral path room an intelligent golem with an archivist field ?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer your question;<br /> The Athenaeum is a temple of living stone made by the mages of Atlantis, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">so while calling it a golem is correct, its more than just a Matter 4 spell going opn in that room</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm really happy with that room though, its shown up a few times but hasn't gotten the attention it deserves. It houses all the Arcadian lore that Acanthus mages collect on their path/realm. The idea of it shifting around like it does came from <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/43263680-ninth-house\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Ninth House</i></a> by Leigh Bardugo, where the people there have a similar thing but its much smaller. Write what you wanna find in the book, close the door, the room will move it to the center, and then you just walk the spiral to it. Its a fun idea she came up with and I saw an opportunity to put it in my setting so I took it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T18:00:02-08:00","id":1546012,"title":"","content":"I think you conveyed it pretty well, when you described how Chrono felt sad, I got the feel that he knew more than he let on. It made me wonder why Giger didn't try to push a bit with <i>Exceptional Luck</i>. When they met in the Sanctum and that Chrono was walking a doomed road while trying everything to have both his children alive and well, it all came together very nicely.<br /> <br /> I never heard of <i>The Ninth House</i>, I will look into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T18:51:58-08:00","id":1546014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1546012#post1546012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never heard of <i>The Ninth House</i>, I will look into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a good book, the sequal is also good, but not as good, I hope you get to enjoy it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T14:30:00-08:00","id":1546259,"title":"","content":"This chapter was supposed to involve everyone but we ended up having two people missing, Ragnar and Maxwell both had family things come up right before so we decided to just go ahead with the Awakening session so we could be ready to stop before the holiday season interrupts our game mid story. So this is the final chapter of the year unless someone asks for a 1 on 1 game, which I did offer so we'll see if anyone has anything they might wanna do.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 41</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/15/2024</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This is just going to be a summary, followed by my thoughts on the session and why I feel like it didn't go well in another post when I get home tonight. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Eye of God saw himself in a prison made of brass, the God-Killer Sword seemed rusted over and covered in dry blood. Mark Slim III wanted out of the Prison as shades coming out of Eye of God seemed to torment him. He eventually escaped, but only after a ghoul like creature made from brass pulled itself out of him. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Mark realized he had chains wrapped around him, weighing him down. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">He faced his grandfather, freeing himself from the weight he felt tying him down. As he did, Eye of God noticed several ghosts stalking Mark. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">A man started following Mark, Eye of God confronted him, the man and ghosts attacked, but with the Pneuma he had gained from getting an exceptional success on an earlier roll he simply trapped the ghosts in a space that was an infinite distance between them and the street he was on facing them, the man ran. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Giger met up with them and followed Mark to Eye of God\u2019s apartment building, which appeared as a massive tower of onyx. Mark broke in, made his way to Eye of God's apartment room, where he started reading from books Giger couldn't see. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">The man appeared with more ghosts and tried to talk Giger and Eye of God into letting him interrupt Mark's awakening so he would suffer once he finished. They realized he was a Banisher and fought him. They won, forcing the Banisher to retreat by opening an Avernian Gate to the underworld and jumping through. During the battle however he cast a Death making spell twice in Eye of God, killing him two times, but neither time killed Eye of God, yes this is supposed to sound paradoxical. The Banisher\u2019s Shadowname was Eclipse. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Eye of God continued to follow Mark Slim through Stygia as he did his trials, eventually coming to a building that looked like a cathedral but with no Christian markings on it, a name in High Speech he could not read. Inside he found a shade dressed similar to a bishop, but again with no markings on his dress to signify which religion he was part of. The shade had him lay on an altar, removed his heart painlessly, laid it in a fire, prayed and placed the altered heart in Eye of God again. </span><span style=\"color:#999999\">Mark</span> <span style=\"color:#999999\">awakened.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-21-2024, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T18:28:09-08:00","id":1546270,"title":"","content":"Alright, I wanna express some thoughts and frustrations I'm having with myself over Chapter 41, you don't have to read this, this is for me. Usually early-mid December my group stops playing games due to people traveling for Christmas and such, so I had planned Mark's awakening to take 2-3 sessions so we'd be done with it before the holidays, which would be a nice time for us to take a break from MtAw. <br /> <br /> It ended up only being one session because Only half of the PCs made it, cutting out things I had assumed they would want to do and issues that would be caused by them doing those things. The Awakening ended up feeling rushed then, and by the time Giger and Eye of God dealt with Eclipse I was done. The session had been very awkward to run, I wasn't able to balance things in a way that made it so the PCs weren't the center of marks awakening, but also make it so the PCs weren't just watching Mark deal with things without any need for them to be around. It was just awkward. I don't hate myself or anything over this, this is the first time I ever ran an awakening in play, I knew it wouldn't be perfect. It definitely went worse than I had thought, but oh well, sometimes when you are trying new things it goes poorly. :shrug:<br /> <br /> However, the weird, awkward part of all of this for me now that carries over has to do with Eye of God, and why he didn't die, despite having two Death making spells cast in him; spoilers ahead for anyone who doesn't wanna be exposed to them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So, in character creation Eye of God took a 3 dot destiny with the doom &quot;murdered&quot; and gave me permission to kill him in the middle of the story, &quot;Don't feel like you need to wait till the end.&quot; I was excited about this because it was a fun tool he gave me. But then, in the second session of the game, he decided to fulfill his vice &quot;Risky&quot; and step through a portal to a lower depth that lacks the ability to die. Wow, now I have a character who is doomed to be murdered who can't die. I was even more excited by this.<br /> <br /> After a sat on this for a few months I finally decided to sit down with Eye of God and talk about what I had been thinking of. I told him we could play this a few ways, but he decided the most fun would be to have Eye of God &quot;die&quot;, and then play some solo sessions together where he explores what this immortality is all about, and then eventually return to the cabal. I asked if he wanted to play Jessie during that time and he said he didn't want to, so I offered to have Mark Slim III awakens before hand and then he could play him during the time that Eye of God was thought to be dead by the cabal. He picked his path (Moros) and his order (Mysterium) and I told him that if he awakened I had a legacy I'd want him to go, and we agreed. <br /> <br /> This also is where the heart transplant that happened at the very end of the awakening came into things. He needed an item that would allow him to scrutinize Death mysteries and we talked about how he'd want to go about that. He's not a fan of Death arcanum stuff really, so taking dots in it sounded like a poor option, so I came up with this Stygian artifact that could only be claimed by non-Moros mages who had somehow ended up inside a Stygian mystery play, which will allow him Stygian sight later on, allowing him to do Death focused mage sight.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, now it's unclear if this plan will even matter going forward, Giger saw the imago of the spell and knows it went off, he knows Eye of God <i>should</i> be dead, twice, but isn't. Who knows if these solo sessions are going to happen, and if Eye of God will ever need to play Mark Slim III at all. If he doesn't, then not only was this awakening rushed and awkward, it didn't even need to happen.<br /> <br /> Lots of mistakes on my part that led to this, imo.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, with all this said... I'm excited going forward. Lots of moving pieces are indeed finally set up to start crashing into each other. Maxwell has his God-Killer Sword and is ready to face down Clausius and Sag'Suga Isim, Ragnar has two mysterious characters offering him patronage, Eye of God found out he can't die, and Giger has his artifact and legacy going, and on top of all of this, when we come back from Christmas, I'll be flipping a leaver that I've had my hand in for a while, so good things will be happening in this game in 2025, just an awkward final session of the year.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T07:53:09-08:00","id":1547634,"title":"","content":"We start back up on the tenth! Decided to do a two week timeskip to get things rolling again, created a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cs8T8uaYVjEZxfrTccsa1EAXjX4wkCGjuMG-wO_zv_o/edit?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\">handout</a> to detail everything that has happened in the past two weeks. Each player has been asked to only read the front page and the page with their character's name on it. Here it is, excited to be playing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T09:46:52-08:00","id":1547933,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 42</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">1/10/2025</span><br /> <br /> Eye of God was summoned to the censorium urgently. When he arrived, every censor was present, along with both hierophants, Chronos and Moon's Reflection on Water\u2019s Surface. The censorium had been ransacked, artifacts, books, soul stones, all of them scattered around the floor. Moon\u2019s Reflection of Water\u2019s Surface was speaking with something Eye of God couldn't see, while Chronos was working powerful Time magic in the center of the room. One of the censors came over to Eye of God to ask if he had talked with Architect recently. He hadn't, and no one could get a hold of him. Eye of God began helping to clean up, but after about an hour of working Chronos stopped them. \u201cNothing was taken, whatever they were looking for wasn't here. Go home and rest, the Golden Council will be holding a meeting tomorrow. You can clean up after,\u201d and with that he left himself. Moon's Reflection on Water's Surface stayed a bit longer herself, finishing casting a binding spell on whatever she was talking to, and then left, instructing everyone else to do the same.<br /> <br /> The next morning a meeting was called by the Golden Council, and when the cabal arrived the room was filled, as if every mage in the Golden Order was present. The Golden Council was already sitting in their seats, except for Architect, who was missing. Giger found Blood to find out if he knew what was happening. Blood said it must be about the symbol that has been getting left on anyone who does. Giger realized that wasn't true, that there were no reports of this happening from combat deaths. When the meeting began, it was revealed that Blood was right. Giger shared what he realized, and speculation about the source of this urge was made, and eventually the Temenose was settled on the source. Erinyes noted that she has a mental shield spell that is constantly on her, and she felt no urge to make the dead with the symbol, other Mind mages confirmed this, reinforcing the idea that the Temenose is somehow involved. Cabals started being assigned missions, most being sent into the Temenose to try and discover what had happened, while others were sent to investigate the symbol itself. The Lantern Keepers were given a mission into the Underworld to investigate the humans who had been kidnapped by a ghost wolf and dragged below. The Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The name the players settled on for their cabal&gt;</span> would accompany them, citing they had an Arrow in their ranks, along with the fact they had defeated a rapt, and two of their members had fought off a banisher to protect a sleepwalker going through their own awakening. The Lantern Keepers are a cabal of three, Vulcan of the Adamantine Arrow, Crypt of the Guardians of the Veil, and Crown of Lead of the Silver Ladder, who are the foremost experts in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Maxwell found Uriel after the meeting and asked if she'd supervise him while he spent the day researching the Celestial Flange, learning more about the cabal from Chicago that had gathered the most information on it (and maybe even had discovered it), the Delphi cabal, who had been destroyed at the start of the war in 1987. He also learned that the true name of the artifact is closer to the \u201ccosmic unifying principle\u201d.<br /> <br /> Ragnar went to Maxwell's sanctum to study the grimoire they had found from Mark Slim III and discovered a Spirit rote that could bind Abyssal manifestations to it, and in return for letting him spend time there, Maxwell had Ragnar train him to wield the God Killer Sword, using Forces magic to mage the weapon lighter so he could use it.<br /> <br /> The two cabals met in a mausoleum, the Sanctum of The Lantern Keepers. Crypt kept a close eye on Maxwell while everyone went over the information they had about the Underworld and figured out where they wanted to investigate. The Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse were told not to eat food in the Underworld as it would fill their stomachs but not nourish them, causing them to starve to death on a full stomach. Eye of God was informed his Space magic would work fine in the Underworld, but that was without an understanding of Death he wouldn't be able to use Space to return to the world of the living. Eye of God was then given two enchanted lanterns. The first would provide five subjects with the Ghost Shield spell, and the other would trick the creatures that swam the rivers of the Underworld into thinking they had a ferryman with them. The two cabals agreed to go to the Dead Dominion known as Lowgate Prison, reasoning than the ghost wolf must be capturing people who had broken the Old Laws of the Underworld and taking them there. They agreed to meet the next morning in the same graveyard and enter the Underworld before sunrise.<br /> <br /> Maxwell was bothered by a security guard while shopping for supplies.<br /> <br /> The next morning Ragnar slit open his hand before two trees in the graveyard that had formed an arch, their branches twisted together, and the two cabals entered the Underworld. Ragnar used his familiar to scout ahead, and Maxwell controlled the light with his Forces magic to do the same. He was able to see a collapsed building, and Vulcan informed them that this was the first landmark on their path downward to the river town of Seguridad, a safe haven for ghosts and the living that travel the Underworld alike, and asked them not to cause problems there, as they had a good reputation with the ghosts there.<br /> <br /> As they approached the building and entered, Maxwell, Eye of God, and Giger noticed movement in the darkness, but the Lantern Keepers pressed forward. The movement followed them through the building, and as they stepped out onto the other side of the fallen structure, four ghost children ran at them, calling out to Crown of Lead and Vulcan, holding onto Crown of Lead\u2019s robes and crying. They were shocked to see these ghosts, as they were supposed to be in Seguridad, but the children told them that the city had been destroyed by a monster that was now roaming the caves on the way the cabal needed to go.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger used his Mentor Merit to get his mentor, Chronos, to spread the information on the LA mayor he had gathered, which is now in the LA Times.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 02-07-2025, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-25T03:40:28-08:00","id":1547945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1547933#post1547933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger used his Mentor Merit to get his mentor, Chronos, to spread the information on the LA mayor he had gathered, which is now in the LA Times.&gt;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Which chapter mentioned the LA mayor's plot thread? I don't remember it and can't find it by searching &quot;mayor&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-25T11:09:35-08:00","id":1547948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1547945#post1547945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which chapter mentioned the LA mayor's plot thread? I don't remember it and can't find it by searching &quot;mayor&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter 40, last few paragraphs it was briefly mentioned. The future rival of his is the mayor of LA. His Gnosis 3 obsession is to become Mayor of LA himself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T10:38:36-08:00","id":1548095,"title":"","content":"Really short and easy chapter.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 43</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">1/24/2025</span><br /> <br /> The two cabals talked with the children more, learning very little about the ghost that attacked the village but getting directions to the village.<br /> <br /> As the cabals thraveled towards the village they started to hear the wailing of ghosts calling out for help, for mercy, for an end, and for &quot;The Necromancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> They spotted the ghost floating along next to one of the rivers of the Underworld, both of which were wailing for help and sorrow and regret. The ghost looked like an amalgamation of dozens of ghosts that had been pushed together by an incredible pressure and turned into one monster, with dozens of faces and arms trying to pull themselves free of it, just to be pulled back in. Giger divined the future and learned that the ghost would focus on the ghosts that traveled with the cabal <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;not the ghost kids they were left at the building&gt;</span>, that combat was likely, that the ghost wolf would take their next living victim to his mistress in Hel, that Ragnar no longer had the choice to ally with the man from his dream, and the Hel would teach him to control the Abyss. They decided to battle the ghost. Ragnar used Death magic to weaken the ghost and then the cabals went to battle. The fight was monstly one sided, with Maxwell taking control of a flame breath from Ragnar's familiar and enhancing it to burn the ghost away, Crypt using his Death magic to simply rot the ghost away, and Eye of God crushing it with manipulations of Space. Things started to sway in the ghosts favor when it managed to send both Ragnar and Vulcan into a state of insanity, attatcking the rest of the mages. Ragnar's attacks were deflected by Maxwell's magic, but Vulcan nearly killed Crown of Lead in a single blow. The ghost did burn up in Maxwell's fire, but it took Giger using Time magic on the two Arrows to end the battle. Maxwell then found the ghost reforming down the river and summoned the Spernal concept of Order to burn the creature up before it could reform, the ghosts going with it, along with a stain of Abyssal corruption at its core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T21:22:51-08:00","id":1548652,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 44 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">2/07/2025</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar and Vulcan spent some time apologizing while Crypt used Life magic to heal Crown of Lead after he had been hurt. Then Vulcan and Crypt used Death magic to open a wall next to the River of Woe and produced a small riverboat to sail, placing the one of their lanterns on it. Ragnar used Matter magic to change the floor of the Underworld into their own boat, and they also used the lantern as instructed. Each lantern produced the image of a ghost that was manning their ship, a boatman Vulcan explained, so that the creatures of the Underworld would believe the mages had paid a boatman to ferry them down the river.<br /> <br /> They sailed down the river to Seguridad, where the Lantern Keepers beached their ship and started exploring. The <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;player&gt;</span> cabal found a statue that had been ground to ruble from its waist up near the beach, and a collection of plants that had been growing in a sort of small farm that had been trampled and destroyed. As they explored further they eventually heard a howl, followed by an angry shout. Bending the light to them, Maxwell allowed them to see around the ruined village. They saw Crypt, who was watching what appeared to be a man, with wolf legs and a wolf head, pulling at the head, as if he was trying to remove his own head, but underneath the Wolf head they could see the neck and jawline of a human. Ragnar recognized the wolf as the one he had battled in his apartment <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;way back in Chapter 25&gt;</span> and Eye of God teleported his cabal in and Ragnar began working to help the man. As he did, using Death magic to try and separate them, Maxwell spoke with Crypt about why ghosts never noticed him. Crypt revealed he was part of a legacy that summoned ghosts to use, but that ghosts hated the members of his legacy, so he kept a spell active on himself to hide his presence from them. Maxwell found this answer disappointing. Ragnar managed to help the ghost remove the head, which fell and became a mask. Ragnar scrutinized the mask and found it had been tainted by the Abyss. The ghost, who's name was Bjorn, explained that his mistress Hel gave him the mask so he could become her wolf and bring the dead to her realm, but that he didn't want to do it anymore because she had been forcing him to bring the living to her, starting a few days ago. He confirmed that the mark that people had begun leaving on the dead in the living world had appeared on Hel, which is when he was instructed to bring her living victims. He tried to remove the mask, something he was usually able to do, but it held on, making him stay as her wolf. The cabal decided it would be best to travel to the realm of Hel instead of Lowgate Prison with this new information. Bjorn told them that the fastest, but not safest, way to get to Hel was to continue down the River of Woe, switch to the River of Blood when they could, sneak through the Killing Fields, and then sail around the Junkyard. Hel use to have a protector, but it was removed by Hel a few days ago. When the cabal asked Bjorn to come with them he declined, saying he wanted to return to his mistress but not until she was better. Ragnar kept the mask, tying it to his belt.<br /> <br /> The Lantern Keepers agreed that traveling to Hel seemed like the best option and the two cabals sailed off, sailing for another hour on the River of Woe and passing a large gate, guarded by a teddy bear, they could hear crying babies beyond, before coming to a break in the wall of the tunnel and switching to the River of Blood. While the River of Woe was loud with the wailing of the dead, the River of Blood stank like rotting blood. They met a giant, fish-crocodile monster that paid them no mind, the illusion working. The Lantern Keepers sailed past the entrance to the Killing Fields, but the cabal sailed in. The guard tried to stop them, but using Space magic from Eye of God and Forces magic from Maxwell the cabal quickly destroyed the ghost.<span style=\"color:#999999\"> &lt;Eye of God actually was shot by the ghost, but Giger went back in time to push him out of the way.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Once inside Ragnar released the spell keeping the boat in its shape, it returned to the stone of the Underworld and sank into the River of Blood. Ragnar told the cabal he wanted to meet another ghost also named Ragnar, who had some sort of key, and they crossed the bridges into the Killing Fields. They knew that each of these Dead Dominions had laws they needed to follow, but they did not know what this one's were. The landscape was flat, covered in craters with no real terrain of points of interest to mention except for a single wall of an old building left standing. On the inside of the was a propaganda poster of soldiers in white clothes with the words, \u201cFEALTY SHALL BE SWORN; NO QUARTER SHALL BE OFFERED; THERE SHALL BE ORDER IN THE RANKS\u201d but didn't catch on that these were the old laws here. Instead Maxwell used Forces magic to call out for Ragnar, hoping he would come. Instead several ghosts in white approached. Maxwell sent them to the ceiling with Forces magic and Giger looked into the future to figure out the best way to find the ghost Ragnar. Learning that they would encounter him in a place called the \u201cBlood Gutters\u201d and that Ragnar would not be the only danger there, they set off, but not before Maxwell released the spell, causing the ghosts to crash into the ground of the Killing Fields and explode. Eye of God also remembered that the banished that he and Giger had faced whole trying to protect Mark Slim III's awakening had a pack of ghosts from this realm.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Sessions ended with two acts of hubris, the cabal working together to destroy the guardian ghost of this realm, and Maxwell killing several ghosts as well, but I forgot all about AoH rolls, so they'll happen at the start of the next session. Also, Giger is really wanting to see the Junkyard Dead Dominion, excited to see machines killing each other and such. It's mainly Giger's player and it leaking into his character, but we may end up seeing three Dead Dominions in this story instead of just my planned two, which would be fun.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 03-06-2025, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T15:22:52-08:00","id":1549055,"title":"","content":"Short session as we spent most of the session going over some other stuff together about a new note taking website we are using now so they can more easily take and share notes with each other, and getting everyone set up for that. <br /> <br /> I did have everyone roll a wisdom check for destroying the ghost guarding the Killing Fields from the last chapter. Giger and Ragnar both failed and now have the Megalomaniacal condition. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 45</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">2/28/2025</span><br /> <br /> The cabal trudged off across the Killings Fields, looking for Ragnar in the Blood Gutters. As they walked Ragnar used his Death arcanum to veil the cabal, making them appear as ghosts. They knew the direction they were supposed to head but without any knowledge on how to follow that direction the cabal veered off course, coming across two groups of ghosts locked in combat. One was filled with ghosts wearing red, which outnumbered the second group of ghosts in white, led by a ghost in Ancient Greek armor. Ragnar and Giger powered up Ragnar's Wyvern familiar using Death/Matter and Time respectively and sent it to capture the Greek ghost. The rest of the ghosts, at the sight of the now enhanced ghost, cowered in shock, but then overcame their own fear and charged the Wyvern, shouting \u201cFEALTY MUST BE SWORN!\u201d Ragnar used Death magic to make the ghosts fight themselves again while his Wyvern captured the Greek ghost. Maxwell and Giger tried interrogating it, but the ghost was uncooperative, insisting that they were in violation of the Old Laws and must swear fealty. Even torture didn't get him to stop, as Maxwell heated the armor he was wearing to get him to talk. When Maxwell asked who they were supposed to swear fealty to, the ghost told them, \u201cThe true ruler of the Killing Fields, Clockwork,\u201d and when the cabal learned that Clockwork was at war with a ghost named \u201cDominus,\u201d Eye of God swore fealty to Dominus, causing a slight red light to envelope him. He was shocked that it worked, meaning it to be a joke to annoy the ghost. The cabal left, now using Space magic to go the correct direction. <br /> <br /> They came to a series of trenches dug into the ground, blood sweeping from the walls into the earth and flowing down. The trenches eventually became tunnels as they went completely underground. Giger, trying to assert his dominance in the cabal, tried to lead them through the underground maze but quickly became lost. After being lost for about half an hour underground, Giger used Fate to help guide him, Eye of God asked him if he had gotten them lost. Giger denied it of course, but Eye of God pressed the issue. As the small argument continued, they all felt a surge of magic, and the air around them burst into flames.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T10:25:04-08:00","id":1549084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1549055#post1549055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of God swore fealty to Dominus, causing a slight red light to envelope him. He was shocked that it worked, meaning it to be a joke to annoy the ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages not thinking their actions through? That's terrible! <i>*Chews popcorn*</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T10:12:59-07:00","id":1549459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1549084#post1549084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages not thinking their actions through? That's terrible! <i>*Chews popcorn*</i></div> </div> </div> </div>yes they do very exciting things that have long lasting consequences, I love it. Still have things happening slowly to him that he has only started to notice from Chapter 2!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T13:41:56-07:00","id":1549501,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I'm burnt out from work but don't wanna let my memory of what happened here fade so quick summaries of the last two sessions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 46</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">3/07/2025</span><br /> <br /> The ghost mage Ragnar managed to surprise the cabal, doing massive damage, nearly knocking the living Ragnar out in the first round of combat with the help over several ghouls. Eye of God used some Space magic to make the cabal a safe place to hide out in, everyone followed, with Maxwell using Forces magic to throw all the ghosts down the tunnel of the trench, with the ghost Ragnar resisting and using his Death arcanum to keep the living Ragnar's familiar from following. Giger used his Time arcanum to alter the Living Ragnar's past, boosting his weaponry skill and also changing his past so he carried a weapon made of pine wood, the ghost\u2019s bane. After that point the cabal quickly defeated the ghost, grabbed something that fell from him, and left the trenches.<br /> <br /> The thing that dropped was a milky gray stone with a nerve hanging from it, clearly an eye. Ragnar scrutinized it and saw that it was a Supernal artifact from an emanation realm, with two separate raven symbols, and an Eye symbol, although not the Exarch. Giger cast some Prime magic on it and learned it has four powers, one of which would grant a familiar if the artifact replaced someone's eye.<br /> <br /> Ragnar cast a spell from the grimoire he's been carrying on the death mask he had, binding it to the grimoire. The mask was absorbed by the grimoire and the sound of writing followed. The mask was being described in the back of the book now and the cabal realized that the grimoire was not a bestiary but a prison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 47</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">3/14/2025</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar dreamed of a bronze fortress, inside he discovered it was an empty prison. Inside her found cells with their doors wide open and eventually found a small room with a stool in it, the walls covered in Supernal runes. He studied these runes and used them to reshape his gnosis, joining a legacy that would allow him to bind Abyssal monsters to the grimoire. As he was waking up someone came down the hall, an old man of Middle Eastern descent, dressed like an old Catholic monk, bounding in chains dragging on the floor. He spoke a language Ragnar didn't understand and Ragnar woke up.<br /> <br /> The cabal sailed down the river of blood, then the river of fire to arrive at the Junkyard. Once they heard the pounding coming from the Junkyard, the ghost of Victoria Adams that had been following Ragnar for months changed, became more machine-like, but kept her humanoid appearance. They entered the Junkyard and she went straight to the massive crushers, where they read the Old Laws of the realm; \u201cThe Design Must Be Tested, The Design Must Evolve, The Crushers are Sacrosanct, The Smith Shall Retain His Tools\u201d and watched as broken machines were placed beneath the crushers and broken, ectoplasm being sprayed out into the river of fire while the crushed metal was taken further in. They followed the belts that left the crushers, and watched two ghosts fight. A humanoid wolf machine defeated an armored machine on legs that ended with wheels. The Wolf took a hand that could reshape itself as a blade and left. The cabal took the other hand and the armor from the defeated ghost and helped Victoria Adams arm herself with them. Maxwell found a hyena looking ghost machine, which agreed to help them find a ghost Victoria Adams could face in exchange for the wheel feet of the ghost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T12:51:44-07:00","id":1550279,"title":"","content":"Chapter 48 was kinda a meme session. One player was traveling and the rest of us spent the time planning our own trip to meet up, so with the last time we had left we did some battle bot stuff for fun and moved on. For Chapter 49 Maxwell wasn't around sadly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 48</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">3/28/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Victoria Adams was led by the hyena ghost past mountains of ghost scrap to a canyon with a small stream of oil coming from a cave. Inside the cave was a ghost with a flame arm attached. Victoria Adams beat it and took a piece from it to make her a bit stronger. Then the hyena made a new deal with her, to take her to another opponent but the Hyena would get first choice of the spoils of victory. She agreed and she battled a ghost that took the form of a robot spider, beating it by holding on and stabbing until it fell. Once the Hyena made its choice of scrap, Victoria attached four of the spider's legs to her back, Doctor Octopus style. The cabal then left her behind to continue testing herself and sailed down the River of Fire to Hel.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 49</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">4/11/2025</span><br /> <br /> As predicted by the ghost that sent them in the direction of Hel, there was no guard blocking their way. They entered and looked over the frost covered land. The ceiling was covered in roots as if the entire dominion existed beneath a large tree. Pockets of farmland existed within a forest that covered a large portion of the landscape with a massive citadel-like structure sitting at the center, a crimson light came from the highest tower, bathing the entire landscape with its light. Ragnar and Eye of God both recalled that this land was tainted by the Abyss, although neither knew in what way specifically. Ragnar, with his Death Sight, also took in the fact that the crimson light was Abyssal in some way, and that high above them in the roots was a massive cocoon that something within was writhing, pushing out against the cocoon.<br /> <br /> The cabal began walking through the dead forest that greeted them when Ragnar spotted a cracked and toppled standing stone with words inscribed on it, four lines that read:<ul><li>\u201cThe Dead Shall Be Honored</li> <li>The Dead Shall Serve</li> <li>The Living Shall Observe</li> <li>The Dead Shall Be Desecrated\u201d</li> </ul>With more words written along the spot where the stone was broken, regardless of the damage though Ragnar was able to make out what was written; \u201cThe Living Shall Be Devoured.\u201d<br /> <br /> The cabal traveled down a path through the dead woods where they came to a small farmstead with medieval Nordic appearance. They ectoplasmic crops were withered and inside the house it was completely empty, devoid of places to sleep, a fireplace, or any pleasantries aside from a table and chair. Right inside the door was a splatter of ectoplasm and some old farming tools. While searching the interior Eye of God discovered the strange rune that those in the living world have been compelled to inscribe on the bodies of the dead carved into the bottom of the table.<br /> <br /> They left the farm and continued down the road until it split, one path going deeper into the woods, and one going seemingly around the woods. The cabal traveled down the path that would take them deeper into the woods and quickly the frost covered landscape became covered in an inch of soft snow. While traveling along the path they noticed fresh red snow coming from behind a thick, but dead, bush. They realized a wounded, <i>living</i> person was hiding in the bush, but they were preparing to run when the cabal started to approach. Ragnar used Matter patterning to change the snow to ice and trap the person, but the spell also caused a strong paradox, breaking down the rules of action and consequence following each other logically. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Three paradox that he tried and failed to contain so I used those to create an environmental tilt. I used Inconsequentiality from <i>Nameless and Accursed</i> page 102 if you want to see the exact rules, but I thought it would be funny\u2026you'll see though.&gt;</span> Naturally the person freaked out, but Eye of God used Mind magic to calm him down and they got information from him. They learned that he and other living people were kept in a barn, and people were taking them from the barn to somewhere else one at a time. Two others were still in the barn, but he had escaped, not before being clawed by a zombie, which a small hoard of was guarding the barn. The cabal wanted him to come with him but we're unable to convince him to follow them, so instead they told him about the farm they had found and sent him there.<br /> <br /> Ragnar led the cabal through the woods, following the trail of blood in the snow back to the barn. The building itself was once a two story building but was now caved in, with a hoard of about twenty zombies blocking the front door, which was sealed. Ragnar cast a powerful Death spell to shrink the zombies and they quickly stomped them all, realizing as they did that the zombies were in fact ghosts! Either way, the barn was no longer guarded and they opened the door, finding a man in his 50s and a woman in her 30s, scared but safe. Before they could glean too much information they heard someone say from the tree-lined, \u201cRight on time!\u201d A man in a perfectly presented black tux stepped out of the woods and approached. The man seemed put together and confident, but his eyes were replaced with analog clocks that bith told a different time and clicked at different paces. He informed them that he had already killed the cabal several times and didn't want to again, so asked them to surrender. Noting how undamaged he looked, and how Time around him seemed to be wrong somehow, Eye of God and Ragnar agreed not to fight him, Giger resisted the idea and threw a fake punch at Eye of God, who counter punched. They locked the two living back into the barn, giving them a wink, and agreed to take the man, Abraham de Moivre was his shadowname, to find the man who had escaped and pointed the cabal to the barn in the first place. Their real planned, <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;concealed by some lucky roles,&gt;</span> is to lure him back to the Abyssal Environment to try and overwhelm him there through sheer luck.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T12:29:31-07:00","id":1550912,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 50</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/09/2025</span><br /> <br /> The cabal lured Abraham de Moivre back into the woods under the false pretense of taking him to the escaped sleeper, but once they entered the Abyssal environmental tilt he understood their plan. Combat was very pathetic on all fronts, with Ragnar getting himself grappled and Guger missing several point blank shots and eventually jamming his gun. Eventually Eye of God ran from the tilt and used Space magic to make sure that Abraham de Moivre couldn't follow, and Maxwell and Giger followed, with Ragnar remaining to go toe-to-toe with him. Maxwell managed to stun their opponent multiple times and before Eye of God could land a finishing blow, Abraham vanished. Giger realized he had vanished with a spell that had triggered once he took enough damage, pulling him out of time. Maxwell used Prime to bring him back, where they knocked him unconscious to decide what to do with him. Ragnar checked his body and found a solid black dagger with a red hand guard. With mage sight he realized that the dagger was the result of a Matter patterning spell, with Time also being involved. Giger used Time and realized that the dagger was the Abyssal manifestation that he had accidentally summoned during his first attempt to summon the God-Killer Sword, patterned into a dagger now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T15:47:40-07:00","id":1550947,"title":"","content":"I hope Giger used <i>Constant Presence </i>on that dagger, and on the cabal, because if Abraham de Moivre didn't bother to rewind, it means either he has other priorities or things went exactly as planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T07:37:37-07:00","id":1550954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1550947#post1550947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope Giger used <i>Constant Presence </i>on that dagger, and on the cabal, because if Abraham de Moivre didn't bother to rewind, it means either he has other priorities or things went exactly as planned.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fight went for a while, everyone rolling chance dice for so long meant no one was making much progress in a pretty silly way, so we ended with them still deciding how to move forward and kinda tired, so there will be time in the next session for them to regroup, but currently they have not done any Time magic to protect themselves, the dagger, or Abraham de Moivre which leaves so many possibilities open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T20:56:32-07:00","id":1551169,"title":"","content":"Maxwell was not present of this session.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 51</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/16/2025</span><br /> <br /> The cabal had many choices to make over the unconscious body of Abraham de Moivre. They started by gathering some information. They already knew he was a Master of Time, so Maxwell dove deeper, learning he was an adept of both Matter and Death, and also that he was on the path of the Moros, but it was broken in a strange way he didn't understand. Giger looked into his past and saw him creating pipe bombs enhanced with magic, although he couldn't tell exactly how. He met with people who had clock-like eyes similar to him, and in Hel he spoke with two others, saying that a war had been started in Los Angeles, that Giger had been used to destroy the Assembly, and as he was leaving the castle they were in the face the cabal he stated \u201cThis will be the last time we see each other as I am.\u201d Throughout looking through his past he would vanish out of Time and reappear, resulting in blank parts of his own timeline. Eye of God delved deep into his mind to learn what he was like when not acting as a mage, but learned that he spent all his time chasing his obsessions and working towards his legacy's goals. He also uncovered his memories of Giger, who Abraham de Moivre knew would play a role in his eventual death, but also \u201cGiger\u201d had been summoned out of the Abyss, an Abyssal manifestation that his legacy was using for their own purposes.<br /> <br /> While the others were looking over the defeated mage, Ragnar decided to do something about the Shadow That Walks Abyssal manifestation. Abraham de Moivre's nimbus was on it, and Giger had seen that he used Time/Matter Patterning to make it into a knife before turning to someone invisible to Giger and saying \u201cLet's go retrieve it then, shall we?\u201d Ragnar used Matter/Death Patterning to transform the knife into an ephemeral knife and then bound it to the Codex he carried. It started filling out the pages but he closed it instead of reading it.<br /> <br /> The cabal decided they couldn't allow him to live, but also didn't want to risk their own wisdom in killing him. Eye of God enhanced Giger's manipulation attribute and Giger convinced one of the two sleepers still trapped in the barn that they needed to do something about Abraham de Moivre. He trapped and tortured them, and who knew how many others before them. So it was their responsibility and right to make sure he doesn't harm anyone else. It worked, and the man agreed to do it. He shot him several times in the head and then slumped down, exhausted, and said he wanted to go home. The cabal realized that what they had just done, convince a sleeper to commit murder on their behalf, was no more than committing murder themselves using the man as the murder weapon, and all learned something from this act of hubris. Upon his death, the cabal felt a surge of magic but decided not to investigate.<br /> <br /> The cabal agreed to travel to the citadel in the center of Hel to find the other two mages and Hel herself before leaving, but first Ragnar decided he wanted to replace his eye with the artifact they had taken from the Ragnar of the Killing Fields. In order to facilitate this, Giger used Time magic on Eye of God, altering his past life to change him from a Manga store clerk into a world class surgeon who had finished college before the age of eighteen. They then put Ragnar under and Eye of God removed his right eye to replace it with the artifact. This time Ragnar did not learn from this act of hubris, but while he was unconscious he did have a dream.<br /> <br /> He found himself standing on a rocky shore, with snow and ice covering it. The sky was gray and the ocean rough. An old man with an eyepatch over his right eye and a long beard stood before him, the same man as before. This time Ragnar recognized him, realizing he was speaking with Odin. Odin was pleased that Ragnar had decided to bind himself to him. He then told him of a Scelestus named J\u00f6tunn who had almost destroyed Asgard, throwing it to the abyss, hundreds of years ago. He failed, but managed to capture Odin's Supernal sister Hel, and corrupted her with Abyssal magic before entering a sort of hibernation. Ragnar's awakening caused what was left of Hel's Supernal self to awaken, which in turn caused J\u00f6tunn to awaken. Odin also revealed that all doors to Asgard had been sealed shut by him at the end of his conflict with J\u00f6tunn, but his eye would open a door left deep in the Shadow when Ragnar was ready to learn from Odin. Odin told Ragnar not to face J\u00f6tunn until he was stronger and had spent time with Odin, but also warned him that J\u00f6tunn would seek to bring Ragnarok to Asgard once the door was opened again. Ragnar asked if there was any point of seeking out Hel but Odin admitted he did not know. Hel lost to the Abyssal manifestation that J\u00f6tunn had bound her to, so nothing left of her likely remains. Odin rode off on his eight legged horse and Ragnar awoke to see two ravens, made of both Death and Spirit ephemera, resting on his shoulders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The artifact now in Ragnar's eye hole;&gt;</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><b>Eye of Odin (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b></b></span><br /> <br /> Gnosis: 4 Death: 4 Life: 1 Spirit: 4 Mana: 12<br /> <br /> The Eye of Odin is an artifact from the Emanation Realm Asgard. A Paragon of that Realm, Odin, tore out one of his eyes during the near consumption of the realm by the Abyss and gave it to one of his mage servants, Ragnar. The Eye is a milky gray and replaces one of the eyes of the mage.<br /> <br /> Odin can look through this eye whenever he wishes, so long as the eye has replaced an eye. The artifact has a connected sympathy to Odin, and also serves as a universal key to all Irises that lead to Asgard, regardless of if someone has replaced their eye with it or not.<br /> <br /> The Eye grants the ability to speak with any ravens, and the ravens are always willing to share any information they have. This effect only works if the artifact has replaced the eye of a mortal.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if the artifact has replaced someone's eye, they are always able to see into both death and Spirit twilight at all times, passively.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if a mage has replaced their eye with this artifact, they gain a familiar. The stat block of the familiar is given below (see The Twin Ravens) but some special notes about it are provided here;<ul><li>The familiar takes the form of two ravens, these ravens share a sight with each other and can exist separate from each other. Each body of the familiar has half of the corpus of the full Spirit, and both bodies must be destroyed for the familiar to die. If only one body is destroyed it will reform after a day within the artifact and can be released by the mage as they see fit. If both bodies are destroyed it takes a week for them to reform in the eye.</li> <li>The familiar is both a spirit and a ghost for the purposes of which twilight it exists in, which mage sights can see it, and which arcana can interact with it.</li> <li>The familiar is never detected by peripheral mage sight as if it is constantly veiled. Using manifestations or numina trigger peripheral mage sight as normal.</li> <li>The mage (and Odin) can at any time see through the eye of either part of the familiar.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Twin Ravens</span><br /> <b>Rank</b>: 2<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 15<br /> <b>Power</b>: 2<br /> <b>Finesse</b>: 7<br /> <b>Resistance</b>: 5<br /> <b>Corpus</b>: 8 total, 4 per body<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: +12<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 2<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 20<br /> <b>Size</b>: 3<br /> <b>Influence</b>: Death 2, Secrets 2<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Pathfinder, Speed, Sign<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Discirporate, Materialize<br /> <b>Ban</b>: At the end of the day The Twin Ravens must return to rest on the shoulders of the mage they are bound to<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Weapons dipped in wine</div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T06:15:37-07:00","id":1551189,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do you know me, Ragnar ? Do you know what I am ? Do you want to know <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9x8-1MAAB44?si=0Y4chcsD8ZfRNvKh\" target=\"_blank\">my name</a> ?&quot;<br /> <br /> I also like that the nature of Huginn and Muninn made a subtle reference to Odin being the patron of shamans nd necromancers. Ragnar sacrificing an eye but not drinking from the Well of Wisdom is pretty poetic.<br /> <br /> Wonder if they will read about the knife in a safe place. Did they search Abraham de Moivre and found the timepiece ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T21:44:44-07:00","id":1551221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1551189#post1551189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like that the nature of Huginn and Muninn made a subtle reference to Odin being the patron of shamans nd necromancers. Ragnar sacrificing an eye but not drinking from the Well of Wisdom is pretty poetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty happy with this artifact, I had a lot of friends who know a lot more than me about Norse mythology help me with some of Ragnar's story beats, and this artifact was among those. It turned out really well and I have them to thank for all the inspiration and literal hours they've spent (and likely will continue to spend) as I keep progressing this plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1551189#post1551189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if they will read about the knife in a safe place. Did they search Abraham de Moivre and found the timepiece ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows, they tend to forget things pretty quickly and I try to hold their hands a reasonable amount but not too much, and when I described the writing happening around the dagger they didn't seem to interested and closed the book, so I think they've decided not to care. <br /> <br /> I didn't elaborate very well I think, but once they defeated Abraham de Moivre in Chapter 50 they found a dagger, solid black with a red handgaurd, on his person with some magic on it. Ragnar looked with Matter sight and realized it was patterned into Matter by a spell, and was Abyssal in nature, and that Time was somehow involved, so Giger looked and realized that it is the Abyssal Manifestation of the Shadow That Walks, which he accidentally let into the fallen world a looooooong time ago, during their first attempt at summoning the God-Killer Sword. This Manifestation killed detective Gordan James and the GotV Detective as well, and then went silent back when Giger had to take personal time. So this is the first time it has been seen, reshaped by Abraham de Moivre with Time/Matter Patterning into a tool, and now shaped again by Ragnar into Death ephemera and sealed away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T17:30:27-07:00","id":1551353,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 52</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/23/2025</span><br /> <br /> The cabal now had the sleepers relatively safe with them but there were still several mysteries in Hel and around Hel that they were curious about, including the absence of the Lantern Keepers who they had descended with. First though, Maxwell used his Prime magic to cast a sort of a reverse Apocalypse spell, which allowed the entire cabal to view the world as Ragnar's magesight saw it. With this they saw the entire world on the edge of Ragnarok, volcanic ash filling the sky. Most importantly they all were able to see the massive, pulsing cocoon nestled into the roots protruding from the ceiling. Each of them agreed they needed to get a better look, but first they decided to find the Lantern Keepers. Eye of God used his Space magic to duplicate and borrow Ragnar's sympathetic connection to Vulcan and then used Co-Location to open a portal to her. It worked, with Eye of God feeling a subtle romantic impulse towards Vulcan upon seeing her. The Lantern Keepers were standing beside a wall of the citadel. They seemed shocked to see Eye of God. Ragnar let them know they had found the sleepers, which seemed to calm the Lantern Keepers, who stepped through the portal. They explained they believed the sleeper captives would be in the citadel and were preparing to storm it. A discussion followed about what should be done next. The Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse wanted to uncover what the cocoon Ragnar had seen with his Death sight was about, and they wanted to speak with Hel. The Lantern Keepers did not, reminding the cabal that their goal was the safe return of the sleepers, but agreed to return the sleepers to the land above and then return to investigate the cocoon. The Lantern Keepers did not want to leave a portal between Hel and the world of the living open though, for fear that some abyssal thing might slip through while they were away.<br /> <br /> They had sent one of the three remaining sleepers back towards the entrance of Hel, Ragnar, accompanied by Crypt, and went in search of him. They found him and brought him back, but Ragnar noted the body of Abraham de Moivre was missing. He alerted his cabal to this when they returned, and Eye of God reasoned he must have been pulled into the cocoon.<br /> <br /> Crown of Lead, the Mastigos of the Lantern Keepers, asked Eye of God to assist him in putting the sleepers to sleep and opening a portal. Eye of God sang a lullaby, which Crown of Lead joined in with, complimenting the use of that as a yantra, and then Crown of Lead opened a portal to their crypt sanctum in Los Angeles. Ragnar and Vulcan moved the sleeping sleepers through the portal. Before they mages could return there was a knock on the crypt door, which Vulcan opened. Outside was a guardian in pitch black robes, standing next to Chronos, one of the two Hierophants of the Mysterium. The Guardian went to Crypt and they discussed in hushed whispers, while Chronos asked where Giger was. Hearing his name Giger stepped through the portal. Chronos informed Giger that he had prepared to have him leave Los Angeles for Tokyo, revealing that a terrorist attack had happened while they cabals were in the Underworld by someone who looked like Giger. A video was shown to them where someone, clearly their companion Giger, entered a building where a large meeting was happening and blew them all up. It was revealed that this was the Free Council Assembly; one hundred mages died. Chronos wanted Giger to hide himself away in Japan until this was resolved and was ready to teleport him there immediately but Giger refused, saying he had more to do in the Underworld. Chronos agreed, clearly irritated, so long as Giger would come to Chronos's sanctum upon returning to be sent to Japan, Giger agreed. Maxwell inquired about Architect <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;who has been missing since the start of this story remember&gt;</span> and Chronos revealed a Supernal of Death had been summoned out of Stygia and revealed that Architect had been killed in the Athenaeum when it had been ransacked <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;again at the start of the story&gt;</span>. It told the summoners there was no body to recover. Undeterred, the cabals returned to the Underworld to finish poking at their mysteries, except for Crypt, who remained behind with the second Guardian.<br /> <br /> With Maxwell's Forces magic the mages flew up to the cacoon where Ragnar scrutinized it, discovering it was an Abyssal manifestation that was, somehow, created Abyssal Old Laws, but for what purpose he didn't know. He didn't give it a chance to show them and bound it to the grimoire he carried. The cabals split up, with Vulcan and Crown of Lead returning to the world of the living, but first Eye of God handed over his cell phone to Crown of Lead, who agreed to leave it just past the entrance they had come through so that Eye of God could open a portal to it and leave the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse then flew to the citadel, finding it eerily empty, no ghosts, nor the mages Giger had seen mingling with Abraham de Moivre were to be found, just Hel, sitting on a massive stone throne. She seemed amused that Ragnar had finally answered the call of her other half. They spared a bit back and forth verbally before Hel finally offered Ragnar to make him into a warrior. When Ragnar asked what that meant and what he needed to give up, she told him she could make the impossible possible if he gave her the Codex. He refused, instead trying to bind her, but even with a potent version of the spell casting, she was not bound. She sighed and dismissed him, seemingly uninterested in him after that. Asking him to wait just long enough to look into his new right eye and ask \u201cOdin, is this the best you could find?\u201d Giger approached next and asked about Abraham de Moivre. Hel said that if he had met Adam that Giger had most likely given him what he wanted. Giger said that Abraham de Moivre was dead, and Hel agreed, \u201cYou did exactly as he had hoped then.\u201d Giger tried to learn more as to why, but Hel refused to give anymore information unless Giger traded her the cloak he carried in his pack, which he also refused. Maxwell and Eye of God did not entertain a conversation with her at all, and they all left, returning to the surface.<br /> <br /> Giger and Chronos:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Giger went to see his father at his sanctum. Chronos urged him to go to Japan but Giger did not want to, reminding Chronos that he had ambitions in Los Angeles, becoming Mayor. Chronos informed him that it wasn't possible with the people of California believing him to be a terrorist and a murderer and then removed to help smooth this over for him so that he could pursue his obsession later. Giger eventually relented and stepped through the portal into Japan that Chronos opened, but planned to return to his cabal and his obsessions as soon as he could.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T15:08:40-07:00","id":1551666,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 53</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">5/30/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Not a lot happened so no narration for Chapter 53. With Architect\u2019s death the censors, so Eye of God, went through his magical belongings to ensure none of it needed to be censored. Giger returned from Japan with Eye of God\u2019s help, he placed a Time veiling spell on himself so anyone divining his future will see him doing things in Japan. It was confirmed that the Assembly was destroyed, Boltzmann was killed, Dante is MIA. Maxwell called Blood to ask about the Weave of Entropy but nothing has come out, just people being dragged in, according to spirits. Maxwell managed to talk Uriel into letting him into the Athenaeum, she didn\u2019t want to because of all the chaos around the attack on the Free Council and the death of Architect, but a lucky roll got him in to research the Dragon\u2019s Hoard. A journal from an English mage talked about the same Mark of the Dragon he is dealing with, they didn\u2019t find a way to rid themselves of it, but they did plan to summon The Dragon that ruled over the Aedes, no follow up on how that went. Ragnar returned in his sleep to the Temenose realm of the Gaolers of Idaobaoth and gained the second attainment, conversing with the goetia guarding the place but the language barrier meant no conversation actually happened, they did embrace and the goetia kissed both sides of his face. Giger cast a spell on Maxwell to rewrite his history so he didn\u2019t take the Tyrant\u2019s Crown when he stole the God-Killer Sword, and heard the Dragon\u2019s voice say \u201cYou\u2019ll need to be more clever than that.\u201d The mark remained. Giger returned him to normal and they called Moon\u2019s Tears, time to hunt Sag\u2019Suga Isim and Clausius. The werewolf was nearby already and performed a ritual, mock wrestling with Ragnar while the others stomped in rhythm, empowering them all in a way they didn't understand.&gt;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 06-20-2025, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T15:53:09-07:00","id":1551808,"title":"","content":"Its impressive that Clausius has escalated his threat level to the point where he had a Sacred Hunt called on him, at the same time, its quite an honor that the cabal were asked to participate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T17:45:25-07:00","id":1551887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1551808#post1551808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its impressive that Clausius has escalated his threat level to the point where he had a Sacred Hunt called on him, at the same time, its quite an honor that the cabal were asked to participate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a reminder that Clausius and Sag'Suga Ism killed Moon's Tears' entire pack in San Fransisco, so having allies willing to help the old woman get her revenge is welcome for her. I was hoping to spend a little more time building him (Clausius) up but they were ready to go <i>now</i> as I think Maxwell is getting sick of the curse he is dealing with from taking more than just the God-Killer Sword during the summoning's trial. But as we are about to see...I'll probably have time to build the guy up a bit more.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 54</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">6/13/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;It should be noted, because this is gonna come up in Chapter 55, the cabal has made zero effort to heal the damage they've taken. Also somethingI forgot to include in the quick summary from Chapter 53 was that Ragnar cast a Spirit shielding spell on everyone combined with Heightened Senses.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> The cabal and Moon's Tears set out to find a locus that would take them to the Shadow, using Ragnar's Spirit arcanum to track the flow of resonance, they came to a spot in West Hollywood that had what they were looking for. A quick knowing spell informed Ragnar that the gate would open if an undrunk drink was spit in front of it. He went to a nearby bar, The Abby, got a drink and went back. Being new to Spirit magic he decided to test the key, drank the drink and spilled it; naturally nothing happened so he got himself another drink and spilled it before the locus without drinking any of it, opening it. They all stepped through. In the Shadow the part of Hollywood as a small, flowing layer of alcohol running over the surface of the street. The cabal tried to talk to some spirits for information but none would let them get close enough to talk with Moon\u2019s Tears with them, so instead Ragnar used Spirit Veiling to hide them and they started heading towards Anaheim, remembering that Boltzmann had told them the Weave of Entropy existed in the space between LA and Anaheim's Shadow reflections.<br /> <br /> They followed a Leyline but quickly realized they were being followed by someone. Maxwell redirected the light so they could see who it was; Abraham de Moivre, although now his head, the parts that had been blown apart by the pistol, was replaced by Clockwork gears. They told him to come out, and their mage sights told them something had changed beyond just his head. Giger\u2019s Time sight couldn't even detect him, and Ragnar saw him as a corpse. Maxwell's Prime sight indicated something was off about him, but most strangely to the cabal, Moon\u2019s Tears couldn't see him at all, nor hear him. Eye of God uses Mind magic to share what he was seeing with her, which did allow her to see him.<br /> <br /> The conversation to follow was strange, Abraham de Moivre seemed to have lost all control over his own voice's tone, volume and inflection, speaking without emotion. He thanked them, Giger specifically, for helping him reach this state and free himself from \u201cthe thing that binds us all; Time.\u201d It quickly became clear to the cabal that Abraham de Moivre's corpse had been possessed by some sort of Abyssal Manifestation, so Ragnar decided to try to bind it to the Codex. He was warned it wouldn't work and Abraham de Moivre counter spelled his first attempt, apologizing profusely that he did. The second attempt had Abraham de Moivre's body react the way Hel had, a slight shift to ectoplasm before retaking its form: \u201cIf you couldn't bind her why would you think you can bind me?\u201d Throughout the process Abraham de Moivre seemed to have no malice towards the cabal, while his words made him seem grateful for his death, he didn't sound grateful. Eventually the cabal decided they needed to destroy the manifestation, Abraham de Moivre asked them not too, \u201cI don't have any sleepers prisoner here, I'm just minding my business there is no reason to fight!\u201d Regardless, allowing an Abyssal manifestation to wander around clearly wasn't something they would allow. Ragnar activated an imbued ring, giving him the Kinetic Blow spell and Maxwell attempted to cut him with the God-Killer Sword, but it passed right through him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 55</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">6/20/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The day before this chapter I gave my players a warning here that this was going to be a hard combat and reminded them that when Giger had looked into Abraham de Moivre's past he had learned they had been planning for war. Again\u2026they had not healed and I hadn't noticed until it was too late so this became brutal fast.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Before the battle began two pings of mage sight went off, and two more mages appeared. One Giger recognized from when he looked into Abraham de Moivre's past, however now the man was in armor and wielding two blunt swords. The other was wrapped completely in metal armor with jagged shards of metal sticking out of the armored knuckles. The duel wielder congratulated Abraham de Moivre on bringing Ragnar to them and then gave Ragnar an option. The lives of his cabal for the Codex and then going to J\u00f6tunn. Obviously he didn't accept those terms and began casting a spell, but the duel wielder cut him down without moving, however Eye of God saw that one of his two swords attacked sympathetically at Ragnar. And thus the battle began.<br /> <br /> It didn't go well. Moon\u2019s Tears shifted into her war form and kept the duel wielder busy, but it was like trying to tear apart a corpse. Giger tried to assist with magic but Abraham de Moivre constantly counterspelled him. Maxwell and Eye of God managed to keep the metal mage away, the one blow that almost landed being charged with a Forces spell that split the ground where his punch landed. Abraham de Moivre caused Giger to blink out of time but Maxwell managed to dispel the effect quickly, bringing him back to the fight. However whenever the cabal would cast they would be attacked along sympathy by the duel wielder and this eventually knocked down Maxwell. Ragnar's familiar drug his unconscious body away and tried to return to the fight, but Abraham de Moivre lost control of a paradox and the result caused the familiar to blink out of time. Eye of God did enough damage to the metal man to see that there was nothing inside the armor, just metal twisting in on itself as the damage was done.<br /> <br /> The fight went on with both new enemies being killed, only to be resurrected by Abraham de Moivre. Giger tried to use his Time magic to bring Maxwell healthy from the past to the present but again Abraham de Moivre counterspelled him. At this point in the battle Eye of God had taken a lot of hits along his own sympathy and was near death <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;one hit point box without aggravated damage in it&gt;</span> and so threw up a spell to increase the distance between himself and the enemy, but the metal mage dispelled it. The duel wielder struck the werewolf with one blade and swung the other at Eye of God to finish him off and\u2026<br /> <br /> &lt;Literally as I was typing in the command to roll the 2 dice for this attack to find out if Eye of God would die here my power went out. Didn't get it back for 49 hours so we ended this session huddled in our basement with 90p mph winds and tornadoes not knowing what was going to happen to Eye of God. Session is in 20 minutes though, so I'll know soon enough.&gt;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 07-12-2025, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T17:47:54-07:00","id":1551888,"title":"","content":"So I've talked with Eye of God's player, we live together, a lot during this week about what he is okay with happening and what the different outcomes might mean, so....13 minutes till we find out what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T20:23:19-07:00","id":1551890,"title":"","content":"Now that is tense, that missing health made all the difference. The armored mage probably used <i>Possesion</i> on the exosuit, so a dispelation would probably aided with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T18:08:59-07:00","id":1552315,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 56</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">6/27/2025</span><br /> <br /> Ding Ding! This Chapter began with the ringing of shop bells as the door to Otakus Anonymous opened and Johnny <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Eye of God&gt;</span> and Brandon stepped through together for the first time. Brandon was proud of what he found, bragging to his friend about what a great place he found. Johnny was pulled in, to the fresh high school graduate, this place looked like heaven. A woman with a name badge that read \u201cHi! I\u2019m Jaquoline,\u201d approached them to see if they needed anything. They both said hello, while Brandon spoke to her Johnny explored, quickly finding Fullmetal Alchemist manga and looking through them. Brandon came over to tell him that the store was hiring, and the two friends resolved to work here together as a way of continuing their friendship forever into the future.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Then I rolled a one.&gt;</span> The sword of the mage sliced across Eye of God\u2019s chest, cutting deep and, while missing his heart, drew enough blood to end him. He fell into Giger\u2019s arms where they had only a moment to speak before Eye of God bled out; during this time they had Eye of God ask Giger to look after Jessie, to take care of her and make sure she doesn\u2019t fall into the \u201cdarker side\u201d of anime. With his last request finalized he bled out.<br /> <br /> Finally Giger was able to bring Maxwell back with Time, returning him to how he was before their trip into the Underworld. While he acted fast, using Gravity Supremacy in an attempt to pull the duel wielder back towards them, for he had started going after Ragnar once he finished Eye of God. it wasn't enough and Abraham de Moivre used Temporal Stutter to remove the living mages and Moon's Tears from time. Just before the spell ended, the mage who had killed Eye of God smiled at Giger, knowing.<br /> <br /> Ragnar woke up to find a man he did not recognize standing over him, an open portal behind him leading to a library he didn't recognize. The man is enraged, telling Ragnar to get his shit together and protect the Codex if he insisted on carrying it around, telling him he had protected him and it from the mages he faced, but he didn't have time to baby sit. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I probably should have let the mages get the Codex from Raganr, but Eye of God dying felt like enough consequences here.&gt;</span> A moment later two First Talons appeared, Paladin and Lacuna. They asked where his cabal was and he took them back to the fight. Several active spells were going on. The three warriors prepared themselves for a potential battle and Paladin dispelled the Time Stutter spell, bringing everyone back but Eye of God. Ragnar broke down when he learned of his cabal mate's death, and while the First Talons tried to get information about what had happened, Giger and Maxwell instead looked for their friend's body. Giger looked into the past to see his body vanish, a clear sign that someone veiled against Time magic also veiled the body before moving it. Maxwell discovered the body snatcher's nimbus to be a purple sun whose rays turned into a hypnotic circle around the sun, but none of the present mages knew who the nimbus belonged to. Moon\u2019s Tears wanted to continue the hunt but Maxwell talked her out of it, she wasn't happy though, citing consequences.<br /> <br /> The mages returned to the physical world and left to their different order headquarters to be healed. While there, Uriel offered her condolences to Maxwell and invited him to St. Leon Armenian Cathedral once he was ready. When he said he wasn't feeling religious, she insisted it was about what happened in the Shadow and what is happening in Los Angeles with the Abyss, not religion. Giger was found by Delver who asked about Eye of God. When he discovered he had been killed and his body missing, he asked for his permission to join the cabal to help uncover what happened and get revenge for Eye of God, Giger agreed and the mages all met at Delver's mansion. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;A reminder that Delver is Mark Slim III post Moros Awakening and is now being played by Eye of God's player.&gt;</span> The cabal played pickleball to try and distract at Delver's instance but it didn't help. After losing Ragnar called Vulcan, who offered her condolences, and asked about any Death masters she knew. Immediately she knew what this was about and warned against trying to resurrect Eye of God, but he insisted on talking to a Master. She promised to find him someone to talk to and sent him to see a Moros of the Silver Ladder, Alpha Centauri. He agreed to meet them that evening in his cabal's sanctum that evening which was hidden inside Griffith Observatory. He insisted that resurrection was risky being they wouldn't need a soul to fully restore himself, but Ragnar insisted on trying. Alpha Centauri told him he would look into potential Shades that could be summoned but that they would first need a body, which was missing.<br /> <br /> In order to find the body the cabal went to Eye of God's apartment to get his computer and find a Space mage to use the sympathy to him to find his body. While there, Jessie wanted to know what happened. Raganr explained to her that he failed to protect him and he was killed. This caused her to have a breakdown, where she claimed herself for not protecting him, sliding into self loathing in front of everyone and then discharged a blast of electricity that harmed the entire cabal before she fled.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Me and Eye of God\u2019s players spent the week talking about all possible outcomes. Does he want to die, live, or let the dice determine the outcome? If he doesn\u2019t die what consequences does he want from this scene (as there should be some no matter what, even if death isn\u2019t the end.) If he does die, who does he want to play? I think we came to some pretty good decisions along the way and I am excited to see where this goes. Ragnar spent most of the session reading through the core book looking for ways to resurrect Eye of God.&gt;<br /> </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T06:05:10-07:00","id":1552327,"title":"","content":"If its stil being brainstormed, some possible resurrection ideas that came to mind include:<br /> <br /> * Go to Yggdrasil and retrieve &quot;the eye of a god&quot; from Mimir's Well, by dropping a worthy sacrifice in its place.<br /> * Pass a Trial for the Angel of Hours Supernal Boon, sendimg them back before the fight to heal and jump them.<br /> * Quest for water from the River Anahita, as dangerous as that can be.<br /> * Revive him with <i>Deny the Reaper</i> (or the Endings Unwoven Boon), heal the Souless condition back to the lowest stage, suspend progress via <i>Veil of Moments</i> and start trying to figure out how to get a replacement soul.<br /> <br /> Some of them require them to retrieve him first, but all bring onboard some fun complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T21:22:10-07:00","id":1552344,"title":"","content":"Loved all of those examples and will pass that post on to them to give some more ideas if this is indeed where they want to go. I know Ragnar is pursuing it as a way to rectify a failure as he sees it, but when he asked Eye of God's player if he wanted him to try the response was &quot;If it is what Ragnar would do.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only thing that didn't register for me what this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1552327#post1552327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Quest for water from the River Anahita, as dangerous as that can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this referencing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T22:49:40-07:00","id":1552350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1552344#post1552344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this referencing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluebook/Geist supplement Book of the Dead introduces some additional example Rivers of the Underworld; Anahita is the extremely elusive River of Life that can supposedly heal all wounds and maybe even restore the dead, though the tradeoff for this (since there's always a catch when drinking from the Rivers) is according to myth the waters are finite and when they run dry the whole world will collapse into the Great Below.<br /> <br /> On a more general note, it's something of a recurring soft story hook in Geist that the Underworld takes poorly to attempts to take water from the Rivers beyond its bounds, to the point where Kerberoi supposedly get involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T04:20:17-07:00","id":1552362,"title":"","content":"To add to KaiserAfini's examples:<br /> <br /> * Ephemeral entities of Rank 4+ may possess a Resurrection Numen. If I recall correctly, using it wouldn't result in soul loss, but it <i>would</i> return Eye of God as a Sleepwalker.<br /> * The God-Machine has projects intended to resurrect people, one of them written up in the God-Machine book. I don't mean to say that Mages would even know about it, but a Fate or Time spell asking to find a way to bring Eye of God back from the dead could direct your PCs towards random weirdness of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T10:11:16-07:00","id":1552375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1552362#post1552362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to KaiserAfini's examples:<br /> <br /> * Ephemeral entities of Rank 4+ may possess a Resurrection Numen. If I recall correctly, using it wouldn't result in soul loss, but it <i>would</i> return Eye of God as a Sleepwalker.<br /> * The God-Machine has projects intended to resurrect people, one of them written up in the God-Machine book. I don't mean to say that Mages would even know about it, but a Fate or Time spell asking to find a way to bring Eye of God back from the dead could direct your PCs towards random weirdness of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be the <i>Wake the Dead</i> tale from page 214 and maybe <i>Do-Over</i> from page 199 of the CofD core book. Either of them could become a whole Mystery in itself, and help showcase some additional effects the Cult of the Doomday Clock is having.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:00:56-07:00","id":1552409,"title":"","content":"Wait... I might be bad at research, but I went back through the thread and couldn't find it...<br /> Did Eye of God lose his immortality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T12:30:25-07:00","id":1552457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1552409#post1552409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... I might be bad at research, but I went back through the thread and couldn't find it...<br /> Did Eye of God lose his immortality?</div> </div> </div> </div>A question yet to be answered in game but they'll need his body to find out, and also never even investigated his immortality to know its rules.<br /> <br /> We are on hiatus right now too so probably won't be playing until next week, so might be a bit before they discover that answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T12:31:35-07:00","id":1552458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1552350#post1552350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluebook/Geist supplement Book of the Dead introduces some additional example Rivers of the Underworld; Anahita is the extremely elusive River of Life that can supposedly heal all wounds and maybe even restore the dead, though the tradeoff for this (since there's always a catch when drinking from the Rivers) is according to myth the waters are finite and when they run dry the whole world will collapse into the Great Below.<br /> <br /> On a more general note, it's something of a recurring soft story hook in Geist that the Underworld takes poorly to attempts to take water from the Rivers beyond its bounds, to the point where Kerberoi supposedly get involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. That could be fun, I am not sure right now how interested they are in returning to the Underworld but I suspect they would if they could bring EoG back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T15:19:32-07:00","id":1552813,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 57</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">7/25/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Very Short session that basically revolved around Maxwell trying to find out how to track down Abraham.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Ragnar got a phone call from Vulcan, asking him to meet her at her sanctum. Once there she told him about Mictlan, a Dead Dominion that her cabal was trying to find. If they did, they might find a way to bring Eye of God back that way, according to the legends. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;I had forgotten this was the entire point of the Lantern Keepers as a cabal, but forgot to bring it up when Ragnar asked Vulcan about resurrection in the last session.&gt;</span> Ragnar then did some research in the Adamantine Arrow library and discovered the Aeons, specifically Typhon, who may be able to grant the ability for a true resurrection if Ragnar made it to his dominion. Ragnar placed two different soul jars at two different retirement homes.<br /> <br /> Maxwell tried to do his own research but no one in the Mysterium was willing to babysit him, so instead he went to the St Leon Cathedral in Glendale to see what Uriel had offered to show him. She was there waiting and his peripheral mage sight started aching. He opened his sight to see the cathedral change into a massive golden cathedral that disappeared into the clouds above, and he felt certain that the structure went all the way to the Aether. Angels dressed in white robes came and went, carrying scrolls with them, sealed as they went, and open as they returned. Some had trumpets. Uriel welcomed him, apparently knowing via Time magic he would be arriving today, and took him inside. Inside the building normal mortals went about their business, saying prayers in corners of the building or working, while smaller angels floated through the halls singing. Uriel explained that this was an Aedes known as The Cathedral and existed to help Obrimos like themselves to understand their own paths in life. The angels that could be summoned from here could help a mage understand their own fate and destiny. Inside the chapel there was an angel of pure gold sitting atop a throne with a golden staff in hand. Behind the chapel were two more mages, Paladin the Arrow that had arrived to save them in the Shadow, and a Guardian of the Veil. A Hallow existed in this space as well, and a curtain hung from the wall, blocking something off from view that Uriel explained as \u201can artifact that assists the Choir. Paladin and Uriel explained to Maxwell they had learned of him through this artifact and the aedes, and wanted to invite him to join the Choir of Hashmallim, a legacy of Obrimos that specializes in the destruction of the Abyss. When he asked how they did this Paladin gave a nod to Uriel, who summoned an angel, which they called an avatar. The angel wished to battle Abyssal manifestations on the spot, and Uriel apologized that there were none to face, allowing it to return to the Supernal. Maxwell agreed to join and Paladin explained that he would need to locate an Abyssal manifestation to destroy and then Uriel would assist him in summoning his own avatar, together Maxwell and the avatar would destroy the manifestation and then the avatar itself would induct Maxwell into the legacy. Maxwell decided he would summon an angel from the aedes that evening with his cabal to learn about Abraham and where he would have him.<br /> <br /> The summoning was successful and each mage had to give mana to the angel in order to read from a scroll she had in her hand; Maxwell had to steal mana from the Choir's hallow to have enough, but once ten mana was given the scroll was offered and Maxwell took it. He wanted to know where he would find Eye of God, and the scroll showed him his cabal maye surrounded by demons and their allies <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Abyssal manifestation and scelesti&gt;</span>. When he asked where he'd find Abraham he saw him in three locations, beneath the Redondo Pier with the mages he had been with in the Shadow, in the Underworld next to Hel, and again next to Hel in the Astral. He saw the same locations when he asked where he'd kill Abraham. Then he asked about the God-Killer Sword and how he'd use it and learned it had three abilities; striking anything in Twilight, it could grant him information about gods <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Rank 4-5 ephemeral entities and Supernals&gt;</span> and granted him heightened defenses against their magic while also allowing him to strike their magic with the sword to dispel it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;We ended kinda abruptly here because everyone had had a long week and it felt like a good place to end. It is important to note that when Maxwell saw Hel in the Astral and the Underworld he realized it was the same entity in both places. Also, I forgot when it happened in the timeline but Delver used Mind magic to help Ragnar recall the conversation he had in the Astral with the creature living in the Realm of the legacy he has joined; \u201cFinally someone has come after all this time, now the master's work can continue.\u201d&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-01-2025, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-15T16:28:19-07:00","id":1553214,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 58</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/01/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar was not present for this chapter. Therefore some things happened I was planning on waiting to do for a bit longer for - so that Maxwell could control Abraham - but without Ragnar they didn't want to go down that path right now.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> The cabal had information on Eye of God, and had his computer in order to pursue the sympathetic connections to their old cabal mate. They gathered in Giger's apartment and contacted Blood, who agreed to help them. Blood arrived quickly and worked his Space magic to connect a portal to Eye of God, who was laying, arms folded over his chest, on an altar in a church. Maxwell expected a trap or a fight due to what he learned from the Angel but after investing through the portal, and then stepping through said portal and investigating more, nothing seemed off other than the body being laid out in public the way it was. Still not fully trusting it, Maxwell used Gravity Supremacy to pull the body through the portal. Blood apologized for the loss of their friend and left, leaving the cabal to hide Eye of God's corpse in Giger's apartment.<br /> <br /> As the cabal discussed what to do next a new portal opened, this time a man in pure white armor with ruby trim that came together to make a rose stepped through, wielding a large shield and a halberd, both made of the same white metal his armor was. The man braved himself to charge, pointing the tip of the halberd at Giger and demanding Giger declare his allegiance. Giger declared he was a member of the Mysterium and made the sign of a member who had passed through the first mystery. This satisfied the man, who removed his helmet to reveal he was Giger <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;from this point on White Knight Giger&gt;</span>. White Knight Giger was relieved, as he did not want to have to kill another Giger, but was certain that the Giger of this timeline would have become a Scelestus, given the appearance of the Clocktower in the sky and the fact Time was ending here. White Knight Giger told Giger a third would reach out to him in the near future to help direct the effort to save Time here and left through the portal he had come through. Delver and Giger both noticed that the other side of the portal seemed to be in a desert with giant bronze hourglasses resting in it.<br /> <br /> While Giger was excited to meet other versions of himself he recalled Eye of God and the promise he made before he died, so being they did not have a soul yet, he used his Fate magic to cause him to find Jessie so he could help protect her. As he and the others wandered Los Angeles they came across her in an alley, being handed a slip of paper by a man they had never seen, who then transformed into a dove to fly away. They approached cautiously, remembering her electrical burst she had given off last time, but she seemed more like her old self, although angrier. Maxwell asked who the man was but at first she refused to tell them. Maxwell and Giger explained they had Eye of God\u2019s body and were close to resurrecting him, revealing they had hid the body in Giger's apartment. Jessie had no interest in seeing it. When confronted on this she admitted that the slip she had been given was the location of someone like her, a promethean, who could teach her to be stronger, and until she was strong enough to have been able to protect Eye of God she couldn't bring herself to see him, dead or alive. The cabal understood and let her go.<br /> <br /> The final scene saw Giger and Maxwell drinking in Eye of God's honor. Giger paid the bar owner to make a drink named after his friend and together they drank till past midnight. As they were leaving with Leopold driving away, a homeless man knocked on the window. Giger gave the man some water and money and then noticed an old man standing across the street. The man approached and told him he wanted to speak, but not until Giger was sober. Giger rolled up the window and used his Time magic to bring up the version of himself who had not yet gone drinking and used Prime magic to learn the man was a mage, with mastery over Time and Fate, adepthood over Matter Life as well as his weakest arcana. Giger invited him in where Maxwell accused him of being another Giger. The man seemed sad looking at Maxwell, and confirmed he had once used that shadow name but not for a long time. Giger asked what he went by now and he just said \u201cTed.\u201d Ted confirmed that he was here trying to save all of Time from the Clocktower and needed Giger\u2019s help, that this was more important than resurrecting Eye of God. Giger asked if Eye of God had died in his timeline but he hadn't, it had been Maxwell who was executed for falling to rapture while hunting Clausius who had died, and he tried to save him but failed. Giger agreed to help Ted, and was given a task. He needed to find the Seer known as Conquest. She was a servant of the General who had already been hunting Scelesti in Los Angeles but Ted believed she would get in the way of his efforts, so told Giger and Maxwell to direct her focus to J\u00f6tunn, who was the mage hunting Ragnar. He further revealed that she had no sleeper name or past, having burnt it up upon awakening, she was now just a tool for the will of the General. The cabal agreed and asked how to contact him to confirm they had succeeded but Ted didn't believe it would be necessary, saying he would know.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;For fun, <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/FullmetalAlchemist/comments/rnxdyu/the_flame_alchemist_3_parts_rum_chata_1_part/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a link to Reddit so you can see what the Eye of God drink is.&gt;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-15-2025, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T07:26:36-07:00","id":1553215,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If he went from Giger, who measured nuclear energy, to &quot;Ted&quot; Taylor, who developed nuclear weapons in Los Alamos, then that has all sorts of symbolic implications. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-17-2025, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T17:16:58-07:00","id":1553549,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 59</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/15/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Ragnar was not around for this chapter.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> The cabal began their search for Conquest by researching her lord, The General. Maxwell was not allowed into the Athenaeum but Delver and Giger where they learned the general <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;lol&gt;</span> information about the Exarch of Forces. Once they had their information Giger cast a Fate spell to cause him to meet Conquest, but it was dispelled after it had been cast. He cast it again, hiding it this time by combining it with Prime magic and this time it was not dispelled. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger got an exceptional success on this second roll, and I allowed him to put the charmed condition on Conquest for when they would meet, which will come up later.&gt;</span> Leopold then drove the three mages around Los Angeles in no meaningful direction. The spell ended after an hour. Looking around them they were in an old warehouse district. They decided to search the nearest warehouse but found nothing of interest.<br /> <br /> It was the second building where Delver heard the sounds of footsteps on a higher floor, along with voices and something that sounded violent. They crept together to the higher floor where they witnessed a woman using her fists on a man\u2019s skull, destroying everything from the jaw up. She seemed to take no pleasure or displeasure from it. When the work was done she calmly walked to a nearby skink to wash the blood off of her hands, and a robed figure provided a towel to dry her hands on. Only after her hands were dried did she acknowledge the cabal, opening the conversation with a question, \u201cAre you Scelesti?\u201d When they answered that they were not she asked if they were the ones looking for her, and Giger confirmed they were. Giger immediately opened with the threat of J\u00f6tunn and told Conquest that he thought he would be a worthy adversary. She was uninterested in that though. Giger tried several angles but she took no interest in hunting a powerful Scelestus on behalf of the cabal. Giger then asked who she had killed, but Conquest didn\u2019t know, just a Scelesti. Giger used Time magic to watch her kill the man. He realized this wasn\u2019t an interrogation, she didn\u2019t ask questions or use magic to learn about him, she just tied him to the chair and killed him. Delver used Mind magic on her to learn her aspirations and obsessions during the conversation; \u201cMystery Command (Kill Scelesti), Martial Arts, Enforcing the Symbols of the General, Life Patterning to Mana,\u201d were her obsessions, with \u201cMaintain her position in the Iron Pyramid\u201d and \u201cfind an apprentice,\u201d being her aspirations. Delver asked if they could have a moment to talk, which Conquest was fine giving. Before she let Giger go she asked if the cabal needed the corpse, Giger said he\u2019d take it, but as he went to his cabal she used Forces magic to turn the body to ash, dusted off the chair, and sat waiting. Delver passed on the information he gained and Giger went back to talk to her.<br /> <br /> Even with the new information, especially using the fact she wanted to keep her position in the Iron Pyramid, he couldn\u2019t convince her. Finally she announced she had no interest in running errands for the Pentacle and killed the robed man she had with her. His body split in two at his death, which opened a portal that she stepped through. Giger, with his cabal, followed her to a land that was covered with supernatural darkness, streams of blood ran over the ground. There was some torchlight that lit where they arrived, but beyond that was pitch black. The portal closed behind them and Conquest was pissed, showing emotion for the first time, to see them. She used magic and then told Giger to use his Time arcana to return before they were killed. He refused until she agreed to help them with J\u00f6tunn, so she asked Giger who he cared for more, and then broke Maxwell\u2019s nose with a punch. Giger agreed, and went back a few moments, just in time to see her murder the robed man and open the portal again. Once back Giger lied to her, telling her he had just come from a future where J\u00f6tunn had destroyed her and the entire Pyramid and while she seemed reluctant, he could tell she believed him, but to his frustration, she left before agreeing to help them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Technically I think she should have killed them all for following, it made more sense to me given where they followed her to, but I decided to let them live because I wanted to game to go on, and the Charmed condition seemed like a good reason to justify her not ending them on the spot.&gt;<br /> </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T12:43:47-07:00","id":1553556,"title":"","content":"I think that fell perfectly into Charmed's description, and a timely use too. However, I can also understand the cabal's reasoning. She didn't show interest in defeating the Scelestus, meaning she will follow her Mystery Command to the letter, without questioning or going a step beyond.<br /> <br /> She was completely unbothered by being scrutinized by Pentacle mages, meaning she is not paranoid, and even overconfident. She disintegrated the body, meaning either she has a grudge against the Pentacle, one that she does not bother to reign in, or it was her petty revenge for their investigation.<br /> <br /> So based on that, and that she opened a un-Keyed portal in front of them, they might have gotten the impression that she has stuff to do and would continue the discussion if they were not squeamish about her teleportation method. It wasn't the case, though.<br /> <br /> The greatest win in this encounter, I think, is laying the groundwork so that Mind spells concealed with a <i>Supernal Veil</i> might be used next time to convince her to be more helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-30-2025, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T20:32:43-07:00","id":1553633,"title":"","content":"Yes, true. I also think that because Ted told tehm to do it they assumed it was just a matter of finding her and asking her, so Giger decided if he was persistent enough she'd eventually agree. They do seem to have plans but have other things they delt with last chapter and this coming chapter. I should get the recap from last week up tomorrow it was a short one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T08:45:37-07:00","id":1553669,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 60</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">8/29/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Full session was a short chapter this last week. Lots of prep.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> With Conquest gone the cabal decided to turn to other things, Abraham de Moivre. Maxwell contacted Uriel and asked to meet outside the Athenaeum where he informed her he had an Abyssal manifestation he wanted to kill. She cast a spell and sighed but agreed to help. He wanted to go immediately but she said no, they would meet that night at the Cathedral and summon his avatar, and then gave Abraham de Moivre that morning.<br /> <br /> That evening the cabal met but before beginning the summoning they all prepared themselves for the upcoming fight. Once they had finished their spells, some ritually cast they completed the summoning of Maxwell's avatar. It took the form of an angel with nebula-like wings, stars for eyes, and a golden God-Killer Sword in hand. It asked only one answer of Maxwell; \u201cWhere is the demon?\u201d<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The following spells were cast:</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Maxwell used Prime shielding to give any attempts at counterspelling any of the present mages a -9 to the attempt.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Giger cast \u201cControl Chaos\u201d with three potency.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Giger cast \u201cHungspell\u201d and Maxwell stored a potency six \u201cCelestialfire\u201d.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Ragnar granted everyone a +3 to perception.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Ragnar cast \u201cGhost Armor\u201d on all mages present.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#999999\">Ragnar and Delver worked together to grant everyone a +4 general armor rating.</span></li> </ol><span style=\"color:#999999\">Also, Maxwell is now Gnosis 5.&gt;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T08:47:10-07:00","id":1553670,"title":"","content":"It took hours to get all this prep done, but I really don't blame them, someone died last time they went up against these guys and it really did give them an opportuniy to see how much prep can let you walk in with, so maybe we'll start dedicating more time to preping magic like this before we go on big adventures. Usually they each will cast a single spell on everyone and roll out, so this is a big change in the MO of the cabal, one I approve of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T16:15:49-07:00","id":1554028,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 61</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">9/13/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yJBLzWvCK-g\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a link to the playlist we used during this battle. I can\u2019t describe how many close calls this battle had, multiple times a turn one of the enemy mages would roll 4 successes to counterspell a player, just to have that player roll a 5. Very insane fight and the soundtrack definitely contributed to that.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> This Chapter started with the cabal and Uriel already under the Redondo Beach Pier where the sand had been hardened by Matter magic and shaped into a tunnel. They traveled through the tunnel to a spot where the walls had symbols carved into the wall, symbols of Time and Death. A quick look over the place allowed the cabal to understand that the entire location had been turned into an environmental yantra for any magic that would reinforce Death or weaken Time. Ragnar used this to his advantage to enhance his familiar's attributes. Only another couple of minutes of walking and the cabal found Abraham de Moivre and the others. Abraham stood before a gateway to the Underworld that was flanked by two of the zombie-like ghosts that had been encountered in Hel. The other two mages that had been present during the battle in the Shadow were present as well, as was a large wolf-like creature with a skull instead of a standard head and some abyssal tainted coming off of it. Abraham welcomed the cabal and then looked around confused before asking, \u201cWhere is Eye of God,\u201d which enraged Maxwell who had Giger release the Celestial Fire spell on the duel wielding mage, beginning the battle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The battle itself was chaotic and instead of recounting it turn by turn, I'll describe everyone's contributions.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Maxwell's preparations for the battle paid off, namely with the Prime shielding spell that penalized anyone trying to counterspell as Abraham de Moivre had done in their last battle. In fact not a single member of the cabal had their spells countered during this engagement. In addition to this Maxwell unleashed powerful Celestial Fire spells on the resurrected mages and Abraham, causing massive damage. Abraham was so wounded from this in fact that after only a few moments in the combat he retreated through the portal into the Underworld. The Angel that Maxwell had summoned flew after Abraham and by the time it finally caught up to him Abraham had already entered the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Delver, being the newest mage, struggled at first to contribute much to the battle. However he did end up trapped the mage covered in metal by transforming the sand beneath him into \u201ccartoonish quicksand,\u201d trapped him for several turns.<br /> <br /> The metal mage unleashed his own Celestial Fire, causing massive damage to Maxwell, Ragnar, and Giger, which Giger reversed by using Time magic. The duel wielder also tried speeding himself up with the Accelerate spell, but Giger countered each attempt. On top of that Giger used his Control Chaos spell he had already cast to hamper their opponents attempts at using their weapons, while boosting his cabal's attempts.<br /> <br /> Ragnar had his wyvern familiar lock the wolf down using the Awe ability, while forcing the ghosts flanking the gate to the Underworld to pursue and fight Abraham de Moivre. When Abraham retreated into the Underworld he also sent the Twin Ravens to spy on him. He dueled the mage that used the two swords, but wasn't able to deal much damage to him. Instead he decided to disarm him. Delver had been trying to alter the integrity of the mage\u2019s swords throughout the battle to no avail, so Ragnar, remembering that the swords were Abyssal in nature, used a Death and Matter spell combined with a binding spell to bind the Abyssal swords to the Codex.<br /> <br /> Uriel summoned her own avatar, which helped Ragnar battle the sword mage, and then spent the battle casting shielding spells on those who needed it and counterspelling whenever she could.<br /> <br /> Finally Maxwell cast a powerful Supernal Dispellation spell, ending the spell that had resurrected the two warrior mages in the Shadow during the last battle, and ending the spell on the wolf creature which caused it to vanish. Ragnar could see a large group of ghosts marching out of Hel through the portal to attack them through the eyes of his ravens, along with the summoned Angel battling Abraham in the Underworld. As the ghosts marched through Delver managed to, somehow, take control of one of the ghosts away from Abraham, and Ragnar used Matter and Death to pattern the remaining ghosts into gunpowder, which his wyvern then exploded with Firestarter.<br /> <br /> Maxwell used his Forces magic to speed himself up and rushed through the portal to engage Abraham alongside the Angel. Once in the Underworld Abraham asked Maxwell if this was before or after Eye of God, and Maxwell answered that it was after, to which Abraham responded, \u201cThen why do you look so angry with me?\u201d which enraged Maxwell further. Abraham tried to kill Maxwell with Death making magic but he and his cabal managed to keep it countered as Maxwell burned Abraham using Celestial Fire, with his Angel delivering the killing blow. As Abraham burned up he said \u201cI think this was the first time, so I'll see you soon.\u201d Upon killing Abraham Maxwell found that he had changed in his own mage sight, he now had a sheath for his own God-Killer Sword, and a scroll filled with knowledge, as he took on a more angelic form; slaying this Abyssal Intrusion alongside the Angel had changed his Gnosis and he became a member of the Choir of Hashmalim.<br /> <br /> <br /> The chapter ended with a few flashes of things happening after this. Maxwell burned up the bodies of the mages who had been resurrected and then sent the ashes into space with his Forces magic. Ragnar discovered that one of the water bottles he had turn into a soul jar had been filled with the soul of someone who had died. The giant clock that exists in everyone's mage sight rung loud, and lastly Abraham de Moivre stood next to Hel in the Underworld, badly burned but grinning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 09-26-2025, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-27T19:00:45-07:00","id":1554037,"title":"","content":"The ghost to gunpowder spell is really cool, but also something ghosts would be terrified about. The fact that Abraham seems to be experiencing time in a non-linear manner is concerning. The scabbard as a proof of joining the Choir of the Hashmallim was a cool touch. Binding the Abyssal blades to the book was pretty clever, I wonder if they will be described as clock hands. The battle sounds like it was the best kind of chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T17:58:37-07:00","id":1554114,"title":"","content":"Ragnar binding the swords was so cleaver. I had thought of it, but as something he could do <i>after</i> the mage had been killed and the weapons captured, not as a way to disarm his enemy mid battle, it was cool and I was proud of him. And his gunpowder spell was explosive, super cool. I was really happy with the entire battle, it was really charged due to their last encounter with Abraham and the others, probably the best reoccuring villian I've ran and I got DMs after it from the players about things they wanna do in response which was fun, so now things will be happening going forward as a result of these three battles they've had with Abraham, which is fun and exciting. It also feels good having Maxwell in the Chior, that has been a long time coming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T13:43:03-07:00","id":1554869,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 62</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">9/26/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Before I started writing this session report up I traveled and forgot to, so here instead is a summary of what happened. Ragnar did a Supernal summoning where he battled a version of himself that was a weapon wielder instead of a martial artist. He defeated him and became that version of himself, he now wields an Artifact Axe that will be shared later. This was a Supernal Boon that cast a lasting Rewrite History spell on him. Giger traded a vial of blood to Blood to be healed and then asked him to teleport him back to Tokyo but Blood refused. Maxwell did more research on the General to hopefully gain some leverage on Conquest. Giger spoke with Chronos who wondered why he hadn't been interacting with any of the Tokyo Mysterium, Giger lied and said he had been shopping for real estate. Giger asked Chronos to do research on the Praetorian Ministry and pass the information on to Maxwell. Giger called his mom and told her she was in Japan and she said his father was stressed but she didn't know why and decided maybe they should visit him in Japan to help his father relax. Information was passed on to Maxwell which will be shared as a hangout later. Together the mages decided to target Conquest's subordinates in hopes that they could create a political dilemma for her with the only way to resolve it being to defeat J\u00f6tunn. Maxwell used his Prime magic on Giger so he could see Fate Sight for the first time, to him it looked like Entropy slowly happening.&gt;<br /> </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T13:08:54-08:00","id":1555173,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15fH9Jo38gB81yb27WhPJ8xIdC9zBfx3YFrYOf0fO6cw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a link to a google doc I made today for my players with some information on three different Seers that they could potentially use against Conquest. The information was gathered by Chronos on behalf of Giger using his Mentor merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T14:37:39-08:00","id":1555178,"title":"","content":"All 3 are really interesting. Abea has something to prove, to the Exarch and to the other Seers, and might be the easiest to convince to help.<br /> <br /> Beria is someone Conquest will personally go out of their way to undermine, making him great bait.<br /> <br /> Blankley had the same kind of &quot;vanished to a revelatory journey and came back a traitor&quot; vibe that Veritas did....well that's not good, he is probably the most dangerous of the three. Even if they choose not to approach him, he is probably not someone you leave to his own devices.<br /> <br /> I am really curious what they choose to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-06-2025, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T15:11:20-08:00","id":1555182,"title":"","content":"I'm excited to see their choice here too. I am pretty happy with this cast of characters, got a lot of good ideas from the discord and decided these would be the three I use, but I got a bank of Praetorians now if I ever need more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T15:47:42-08:00","id":1555221,"title":"","content":"In Chapter 62 Ragnar underwent a Supernal trial to take on the history of a different timeline of himself. Part of that in a metagame sense was changing up his merit and skill dots, and in doing so he gained an artifact. Here is my offical write up on it after we figured out exactly what he wants it to be like.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Vapen\u00e4ra (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> Gnosis: 5 Death: 2 Fate: 3 Mind: 2 Prime: 2 Spirit: 2 Mana: 10<br /> <br /> Vapen\u00e4ra is an Arcadian artifact that has been handed down through the ranks Adamantine Arrow for fourty-seven generations, each mage that wields it is meant to become a duelist. Vapen\u00e4ra does not assist these mages in becoming duelists, instead it simply gives them the opportunity. The mages of the past who wield it have always taken on a shadowname that ties them to warriors from the Viking Age, although not always from the cultures of the Vikings. Many mages took on the names of English, French, and other European mages, all that is important to Vapen\u00e4ra is that they embrace this era of human history. MAges that have acquired the axe have changed their shadownames if they did not already fit its symbology in order to wield it. Vapen\u00e4ra takes the form of a hatchet (Size 1, +1 Damage, -2 initiative, Strength 1) that appears normal to the eye. A historian of the Middle Ages might mistake it as a well preserved historic relic from that era.<br /> <br /> Vapen\u00e4ra witnesses oaths sword by its wielder, enforcing and protecting them. If the mage wielding Vapen\u00e4ra swears to battle a single enemy the artifact activates, casing the Fate spell Sworn Oaths (MtAw 137), although it casts both the mage and their enemy in the role of duelist. For the duration of the duel each participant gain access to a numbers of boons equal to the highest of their Fate arcana, including the Fate of Vapen\u00e4ra. The winner of this duel gains the rote quality on all physical actions for one month, while the loser suffers as all their physical actions become a chance dice.<br /> <br /> Legend around Vapen\u00e4ra says that it is not concerned with the legacy or status of its wielder but of itself, and will not witness the oaths of battle against targets that are weaker than the mage swearing the oath, only mages that are equal in strength or stronger than the mage with it witness. Rumors also exist of powerful mages swearing to do battle against the mage who wields Vapen\u00e4ra and the axe witnessing that oath, although these are not confirmed. Temporal Sympathy can be used to witness the past battles of Vapen\u00e4ra, which is used as evidence that the weapon has some sort of intentions of its own to forge a legacy for itself.<br /> <br /> Vapen\u00e4ra also shields both duelists against interference. This effect functions as a universal counterspell that automatically succeeds to stop any spell that would directly affect either participant, and as a Fate shielding effect to keep others from physically interfering with the duel. Participants can be talked out of the duel, however Vapen\u00e4ra considers anyone talked out of the duel to be the loser and inflicts its hex.<br /> <br /> A strange effect of Vapen\u00e4ra that scholars have not fully worked out is its interactions with ephemeral entities. If the duel is sworn against an ephemeral entity that entity becomes manifested, seemingly of its own intent, for the duel. If that entity loses all of its corpus it does not vanish, but instead appears next to the mage wielding Vapen\u00e4ra at their mercy.<br /> <br /> One final note on the history of Vapen\u00e4ra; in the modern age only mages are capable of using Vapen\u00e4ra, along with some Proximi families, but during the Middle Ages Vapen\u00e4ra was wielded by mages, sleepwalkers, and sleepers alike. This ended in 1065 A.D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-07-2025, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T13:30:37-08:00","id":1555477,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 63</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/10/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This chapter is a solo session for Giger to become a Guardian of the Veil. The little mini story was meant to be played between two different chapters, so the second half of this story will be Chapter 65. This story begins once the mages returned from the Hel in the Underworld. Giger, seeing the dangers of left-handed and Abyssal magics confided in Blood that he wanted to help the Guardians track and deal either these mages, and thus was introduced to another Guardian to train him in the orders methods and philosophy, Arachnid.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Giger met Arachnid in her sanctum, a place full of webs and spiders that seems to crawl in patterns that whispered of some sort of secret that Giger has never been able to piece together while being here. She is the one who has been training Giger, teaching him the Exoteric Tenets. Today she informed him of a series of sleepers who have gone seemingly catatonic in a town several hours North of Los Angeles, Salinas. Specifically, these sleepers are exhibiting the signs of having lost their souls. Salinas is outside of the range of the Golden Order, and the Awakened of San Francisco rarely travel that far South, so the Guardians have decided to send Giger to investigate and deal with any problems he may come across the way a Guardian should. He was given the name of the most recent victim, an Ethan Jose, along with his address and the intel that all of the victims were at the Salinas Regional Hospital psych ward as they were conscious but unable to feed or clean themselves. Giger was also given a pair of glasses imbued with the Soul Marks spell so he could discover if these sleepers really were soulless or if something else had happened.<br /> <br /> Before leaving Giger cast a Fool's Rush In spell and Exceptional Luck to ensure things would go in his direction on this mission.<br /> <br /> Leopold had driven Giger to Ethan Jose\u2019s small house, which had several newspapers out front. Before entering Giger looked through the papers to get a sense of what might be happening in Salinas and found an interview with the doctor that is treating the four patients. While none of the information shared in the article was new, Giger learned the name of the doctor who was treating them, Elijah Cullings. Elijah was a friend of his growing up as their parents were friends. Elijah\u2019s father owned a pharmaceutical company but instead of taking it over Elijah went to medical school to try and directly help the sick. They were friends when they were children but had grown apart as life causes adults to do.<br /> <br /> Inside Jose\u2019s apartment Giger checked with Mage Sight and felt a powerful signature nimbus, one of the sensations of drowning in despair. Using Time magic he looked into the past to see that four days ago Ethan was moved by stretcher and ambulance to the hospital in a catatonic state, no spell was on him. Two women, one older than Ethan and one closer to his age, cried as it happened. The day before Ethan spent the day on his couch doing nothing, no T.V., no phone time, nothing, while the two women yelled and pleaded with him. Giger learned this was his girlfriend and mother. The day before that Ethan came home drunk with another whiskey bottle ready to go, wearing his work uniform. He got into a fight with his girlfriend and started drinking on the couch after she left. This time he was under the effects of a spell. Giger then took the liberty of looking around the apartment. It was clear Ethan's girlfriend had not been living here the past few days. Nothing interesting was found except for some medical bills for a check up that Ethan had at the Salinas Hospital's clinic a month before.<br /> <br /> Giger went to his place of work next, a nearby gas station, and looked into the past again. Nothing odd happened over the month he looked through. The only thing was that a spell was cast on Ethan while at work, but Giger couldn't see anyone who would have cast it. He came to the conclusion that it must have been either cast remotely on him, or a Space mage was involved.<br /> <br /> After the gas station Giger decided it was time to see Ethan and the other victims so he went to the hospital, convinced the receptionist he was a cousin of Ethan's, and got past the security into the psych ward. He found Ethan and barricaded the door to make sure no one would disturb what he was about to do. Using the glasses he saw that Ethan did in fact have no soul, and neither did the other man in the bed next to Ethan. In addition to this, neither man had any Fate about them, as if it had been taken. Ethan didn't respond to any of his questions, which he expected, so Giger used Temporal Summons to bring the version of Ethan he had seen in the past, when he had returned from work drunk. The spell worked and Ethan quickly became agitated by being in a hospital all of a sudden with a stranger. Giger managed to calm him down by having Leopold bring up an expensive bottle of whiskey and offering it to him. Leopold got it past security using some sort of magical effect Giger wasn't able to identify before letting Leopold into the room, which ended the effect.<br /> <br /> Bribed with whiskey Ethan talked. Unfortunately not much information was gained. Giger convinced him that he had been taken to the hospital because of an act of biological terrorism and Giger was trying to find the terrorists. Leopold was able to identify the other two victims but Ethan didn't recognize his roommate at the hospital nor the other male victim. He did recognize the woman without a soul as a bartender at a classy bar, but didn't know her beyond that. He hadn't gotten in any fights either. Before the conversation could go further there was a knock at the door and a nurse tried to enter, calling for help when she realized the door was barricaded. Giger ended the Temporal Summons and reverted time one turn in order to keep his whiskey bottle from shattering. When he moved the chair away from the door two nurses, two guards, and Elijah entered the room. Elijah instructed the guards to get the police here, but Giger quickly cast a Chaos Mastery and the hospital was struck by a random lightning bolt, causing power to be lost and patients in the psych ward began panicking. He then used this distraction to leap out the window, making it to his car and raising a glass as a toast to Elijah before driving away.<br /> <br /> In the car driving away Giger used Divination to peak into the future for some extra insight into this situation.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Q. Is this linked to the alternate timeline Gigers or another Fate mage? A. Another Fate mage.</li> <li>Q. How will this Fate mage destroy the Fate of future victims? A. They won't.</li> <li>Q. Will this Fate mage have future victims? A. If they are not stopped.</li> <li>Q. Where is this mage taking the souls of his victims? A. To their sanctum by the sea <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;he also gained the address.&gt;</span></li> <li>Q. Where will this mage and I first meet? A. You already have.</li> <li>Q. What name will this mage go by in a day? A. Elijah Cullings.</li> <li>Q. What does Elijah accomplish with the devoured souls? A. He steals their Fate and luck.</li> </ol><br /> Giger had Leopold drive them close to the cabin that Elijah had turned into his sanctum and donned the Thief King's Cloak, the artifact he had stolen from the Dragon\u2019s Hoard Aedes in his apartment building. He cast a potent Chaos Mastery spell in himself and entered the building. The inside was dark except for a fire coming from the lower floor. Using Chaos Mastery he put the fire out and stalked into the darkness. With his mage sight active he could see a book glowing on the mantle and see a figure hunched over the fire trying to restart it, their body glowing as a mage armor protects it. Giger reignited the fire with a second use of Chaos Mastery and spoke with Elijah. Elijah told him he knew he was coming and was curious why, \u201cCertainly you don't care about those at the hospital?\u201d The conversation continued and Giger learned that Elijah was convinced God himself had given him dominion over other humans to use as he saw fit and if anyone got in his way he'd destroy them. He pointed his fingers at Giger, ready to snap them together, and offered to let Giger go. Giger shot Elijah, blowing his fingers off of his hand without any blood, confirming to Giger he was using Death armor, and used his last chaos mastery charge to make it dark again. The battle was one sided, with Giger clearly being the more powerful mage, he countered every spell Elijah tried to cast while shooting him from different angles. It took three bullets to make Elijah begin begging for his life while stumbling towards the fireplace again, he offered the book he had, and to teach Giger what he knew of the book. Giger told Elijah to bring the book to him, with the intent of knocking him unconscious and bringing him back to the Guardians. When Elijah pulled the book from the shelf and presented it to Giger, Giger punched him and the blow ended up killing Elijah, whose body had suffered damage from the earlier bullets. A quick look through the book revealed that Elijah\u2019s awakening had convinced him that he was God reincarnated on Earth. Giger also recognized it was a grimoire as well. Giger felt sorry for Elijah, who had undergone his awakening away from the reach of the orders and fell into this sort of madness. He took the body back to Los Angeles with him.<br /> <br /> The book he hid in his apartment and the body he offered to Arachnid, who covered it in her spiders as Giger explained what had happened. Arachnid told him he did well, Elijah had tasted the power of the soul not once, but four times, and was beyond saving. She told Giger now his soul had a chance to reincarnate and provide stability to the Diamond Wheel instead of harming it. Giger asked about his victims\u2019 souls, but Arachnid said she could not help with that, encouraging him to ask the Mysterium for help there if he cared about the sleepers. Then he admitted he felt as if he couldn't control his magic well, and Arachnid told him he must become more wise if he wished to have more control over his own magic.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T17:39:10-08:00","id":1555483,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused, did Giger use <i>Chaos Mastery</i> or <i>Miracle</i> ? Because <i>Chaos Mastery</i> only affects whatever subject is targeted, while <i>Miracle</i> is around the subject.<br /> <br /> Did he consider <i>Shifting Sands</i> and try to capture him with <i>Temporal Stutter</i> until he got someone else there, or did he make a deliberate choice for the greater good ?<br /> <br /> Leaving the soul recovery quest an open possibility is pretty cool. A possible way he could recover the soul would be if the Mysterium pointed him to the Dominion of Mictlan, which would make him undertake a Guardian style trial by fire, which includes choosing which soul to bring back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T18:55:48-08:00","id":1555487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1555483#post1555483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused, did Giger use <i>Chaos Mastery</i> or <i>Miracle</i> ? Because <i>Chaos Mastery</i> only affects whatever subject is targeted, while <i>Miracle</i> is around the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Chaos Mastery, but you are right, that was just a slip up I made running the session. Good catch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1555483#post1555483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did he consider <i>Shifting Sands</i> and try to capture him with <i>Temporal Stutter</i> until he got someone else there, or did he make a deliberate choice for the greater good ?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was trying to knock him out so he could take him back to the Guardians, but then when he did kill him he wasn't super worried about it because he was a guy willing to steal Fate, luck and souls from sleepers and then his conversation with Archnid confirmed to him he might the right choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play?p=1555483#post1555483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving the soul recovery quest an open possibility is pretty cool. A possible way he could recover the soul would be if the Mysterium pointed him to the Dominion of Mictlan, which would make him undertake a Guardian style trial by fire, which includes choosing which soul to bring back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not think of Mictlan, that is a cool idea! We will see if he is willing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-21-2025, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T10:20:07-08:00","id":1556169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 64</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/14/2025</span><br /> The Cabal had made a decision; Beria would be the Praetorian they tried to leverage against Conquest. He would be easy enough to find at town hall, but one problem did present itself. Giger had been seen on T.V. not too long ago acting as a terrorist. To try and get around the problem being a wanted terrorist in town hall would bring, Giger rewrote his own history so that he had plastic surgery a decade ago, altering his face. This spell released a powerful Abyssal manifestation in the form of an Abyssal Revision environmental tilt <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Nameless and Accursed page 101&gt;</span> that covered his entire apartment. The cabal decided to leave and cast any more spells they needed to before meeting Beria on the drive over. This rewritten version of Giger had driven Leopold off however with his obsessive need to perfect his appearance, and so the cabal had to drive themselves. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Likely the first and last time Giger will be behind a wheel due to his own will.&gt;</span> On the drive Maxwell reached out to Alpha Centauri, who had previously agreed to give them information on resurrection that would be deemed ethical by the Golden Order to let him know they were ready. Alpha Centauri suggested they meet that evening and Maxwell agreed, giving him the address to Eye of God's apartment.<br /> <br /> Once the Cabal arrived at city hall all of their peripheral mage sights detected something, and opening their eyes they saw that town hall had been replaced by a massive pyramid with an angel looking down over it. They realized that this was an Exarchal Aedes known as the Omni-Caste, details on this within the Golden Order are limited, but Giger was told about it, if he wants to progress within the ranks of the Egregore he must unravel the secrets of this Aedes and present his findings to the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> Once inside the cabal made it past a security checkpoint that had been set up, except for Giger who was immediately recognized as the terrorists who had bombed downtown Los Angeles. He did manage to escape and use Shifting Sands to return to his apartment before he cast the Rewrite History spell. He cast it again, and changed nothing except for when he had gotten the plastic surgery on his face, changing the timeline one week ago instead of years ago.<br /> <br /> Beria was easy to find once inside town hall. His real name was found online and through the research Chronos did on Giger\u2019s behalf and the office was labeled. The cabal lingered outside his office, listening in to a phone call he was having where he encouraged whoever was on the other side of the phone to engage in an undescribed behavior against the residence of Korea Town, telling them no one would care, that any repercussions wouldn't hurt their career, and any if anything did happen to them it would be more like a paid vacation than punishment. Once the call was over the cabal entered. Beria was completely alone, and wasn't happy to see them. He looked over the computer at the reception desk to find they had no appointment and told them to call his office to make one once his secretary had returned. Giger told them why they were there and Maxwell, noticing cameras, created a small, localized EMP blast to shut them and any recording devices down. Beria didn't seem bothered by this, sitting back in the chair and enjoying some coffee and a donut while informing the cabal he'd be sending them a bill for the damaged property.<br /> <br /> The cabal tried negotiations with Beria, starting with lying to him about the threat J\u00f6tunn posed to his ministry and telling him Conquest didn\u2019t care. Beria laughed and said neither did he, that he had determined J\u00f6tunn was only a threat to the Golden Order, cast a spell quickly, and determined that was still the case. In fact he did this mockingly several times throughout the conversation. So, the cabal shifted tactics, trying to convince him that he could convince Conquest his visions had changed, but Beria wasn't interested in this, calling it \u201ctheir dirty work\u201d. The conversation went in circles for a bit before a plan was laid out that Beria accepted; it was revealed that Beria did not think Conquest would be able to defeat J\u00f6tunn unscathed, but he also did not think he could dethrone her and take her place at the top of the Ministry even if she was wounded due to Abea's influence. Therefore, once Abea's power had been destabilized by the Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse, Beria would act, revealing that his Time magic reveals a new future where the local Praetorians are destroyed by J\u00f6tunn, forcing Conquest to act or look cowardly. However Beria said he would not act until after he was sure Abea was dealt with. Giger also struck a personal deal with Beria much easier, telling him he wanted him to not support the current mayor of Los Angeles in the future. Beria said he already knew how \u201cthat\u201d was going to play out and knew which side he'd be on.<br /> <br /> The final scene took place at Eye of God's apartment with Alpha Centauri, but before he was willing to hand over any information on resurrections he had the cabal confirm how they had acquired a soul. When they revealed that they had set up soul jars around nursing homes he seemed slightly uncomfortable but admitted it didn't violate any sort of laws, so he told them of four paths he had found to bring Eye of God back. The first was simple, a master of Death could resurrect him, but the spell would be vulnerable to being dispelled. Second, he had discovered a Supernal Entity, a Shade, that would resurrect someone for the price of a life. Third was traveling to the Aeons and petitioning Typhon for the power to permanently resurrect their friend. His final option was to attempt to discover Mictlan, although he didn't point out that the Lantern Keepers cabal had been trying and failing to do this, and that it might not even exist.<br /> <br /> The Cabal debated over two things. First, which path should they take. No one wanted to risk a spell that could be dispelled, while Giger thought a Supernal summoning and then the murder of someone predetermined as worth killing by the tenants of the Guardians of the Veil could kill two birds with one stone. Maxwell and Ragnar were against this, seeing Mictlan as a better solution. The second point of debate, brought up by Ragnar, was if Eye of God even wanted to be resurrected. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;This was also a meta game question for Eye of God/Delver's player, who answered that the Cabal should move forward with what they thought their characters would want to do.&gt;</span> They decided to perform a Supernal summoning to ask a Shade what Eye of God wants, and then if he did want to be resurrected they would attempt to find Mictlan first, resorting to killing someone only if it came down to that as a last resort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 65</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">11/17/2025</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger's solo session to finish joining the Guardians of the Veil&gt;</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For Giger\u2019s next test to prove he'd be a good fit for the Guardians of the Veil he was sent to Hollywood to meet with Vulcan of the Adamantine Arrow. Her order had become aware of a ritual site that had resulted in three deaths and wanted the Guardians to investigate. They decided to send Giger with the instructions to handle this as a Guardian, not a mystagogue. He arrived at the ritual site, an out of business bar that was now mainly used as storage. Vulcan showed him to the cellar where the ritual had taken place. Three corpses lay around a summoning circle, and the walls were covered in runes. Giger recognized the ruins as similar in intent to the ruins on the walls of the location where the Arcane Luminaries of the Expanse battled Abraham de Moivre; strengthening Death while weakening Time. Each corpse had killed themselves it seemed. A closer look at the summoning circle revealed Abyssal anti-symbols and Giger realized that they had been summoning an Abyssal manifestation. He was able to look back in time and learned that the three mages here had been planning this summoning for two weeks, somehow convincing people to clear the cellar out and then setting up the ritual site while referencing a book that Giger recognized as The Eater Codex, a grimoire filled with Abyssal knowledge on how to consume magic on behalf of a powerful Abyssal manifestation known as The Eater. It also became clear that someone had discovered this ritual site and was investigating it but was invisible to Giger's view of the past. Whoever they were, they discovered The Eater Codex, dropped it and quickly returned it to its hiding place, and then returned the next morning to retrieve it. Then, that night, the cabal that was using the grimoire returned and found it missing.<br /> <br /> An argument happened with one mage saying they should call off the summoning until they found the grimoire and could complete the preparations, but the side that wanted to attempt the summoning with the current preparations won out. The summoning failed, with the presence of The Eater leaking through just enough to drive each mage to suicide, ending the summoning before the manifestation could fully come into the Fallen World. Then, the following morning he and Vulcan arrived. Giger informed Vulcan of what he saw and then used Prophecy to ask questions of the future.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>When will I first encounter this book? When you find the sanctum of the mage who took it.</li> <li>What is this mage's name? Virgil, but you know him as Dante.</li> <li>What will I learn about Virgil's plan for the book? That he currently has no plan. He is unsure if he should destroy the book, turn it in to some greater authority, or hide it away. He has no intention of using the book though, but if he does hold on to it he will be tempted by the knowledge in the book like any mage would be in that situation.</li> <li>What would The Eater gain by influencing the summoners to kill themselves before it had been fully summoned? Nothing.</li> </ol>With this information he called Virgil, who seemed tired over the phone. Giger asked if they could meet to discuss an investigation he was leading and Virgil agreed, telling him he could meet him in thirty minutes and giving him the address of his sanctum. Giger filled Vulcan in on what was going in and she left. With no immediate threats and just an interview of a mage who wasn't part of the Golden Order to begin with she had no reason to stay and plenty of reasons to go investigate other threats. She shook Giger\u2019s hand and they went their own ways.<br /> <br /> Giger arrived at Virgil's sanctum with time to spare but decided not to break into the sanctum. He did arm himself with his pistols, but waited for Virgil. Virgil seemed shocked to learn how rich Giger was, as evident by the limousine he was waiting in. In turn, Giger was shocked by Virgil's sanctum, as it was much larger and more filled with tombs and magical items than he had expected. Virgil revealed that it has been tradition for a century for Virgil to pick a Dante, train him, and pass all the lore they had acquired down to their Dante upon their death. The Dante would then take the Shadowname of Virgil and continue the process. When Thread-Cutter had been brought to justice, the then Dante got all of the stolen lore that was taken from his Virgil and finally felt he could take on his master's Shadowname. While he described this he closed and covered a book that had been left open, but Giger didn't push yet.<br /> <br /> Giger caught Virgil up on what had happened with the Eater Codex, and to his surprise, Virgil admitted he had it and turned it over to Giger. Touching the book made Giger feel like he was being bitten over and over again at the points of contact by millions of small mouths and it was no shock to him that Virgil was so ready to hand it off to anyone else. However Giger wasn't sure if just retrieving the grimoire was enough and so he questioned Virgil more. Virgil admitted he had found the book and was shocked by its contents, and that he had stolen it in hopes that it would dissuade the owners from completing the summoning. Giger confirmed that he hadn't read it by looking at the book's past, seeing he hadn't opened it in the past day, and also checked Virgil's past, who hadn't hidden himself from Time since returning with the book and instead went into the Astral looking for something, but failing to find it.<br /> <br /> It was at this point two things happened. Giger noticed there was a large spider on the ceiling of Virgil's sanctum and at the same time he received a text from an unknown number telling him Virgil must die. He tried calling them back but the line was dead, so he used Fate magic to text a random number to contact them, asking them who they were. They did not answer, instead they just said \u201cThis order comes from higher up than either of us.\u201d Virgil asked what was happening but Giger told him not to worry, again casting Prophecy.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If I keep the Eater Codex will I use it? You'll have the same temptations to use it that Virgil would have, but it is not guaranteed.</li> <li>What will happen if I don\u2019t kill Virgil? This question was blocked, hidden by powerful Time magic and he didn't get an answer.</li> <li>Who is giving the order to Kill Virgil? Epopt. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Giger recognized this as a rank, not a name.&gt;</span></li> </ol>After much agonizing, Giger decided not to kill Virgil. He had stolen the Eater Codex, and not studied it at all, in an attempt to stop the previous owners from summoning the Eater. He was not looking to use the book and would only be tempted by its secrets if he had held onto it, but he had already handed it over to Giger. So, he thanked him and decided that the Guardians were not the order for him. Still, he received a text saying to meet at the Wiltern the next morning to inform Arachnid of what had happened, and he decided he would go to try to save Virgil\u2019s life.<br /> <br /> At his apartment he cast a indefinite duration Time veiling spell to hide the inside of his secret vault from Time magic, so everything inside would be hidden, and then cast a second indefinite Time spell on the living room of his apartment to make it look like the Shadow That Walks had broken in and stolen the Eater Codex the same night Giger had returned with it, foolishly leaving it on his shelf. Both spells were safely relinquished.<br /> <br /> The next morning Giger went to the Wiltern and met with Arachnid. She was with two others, a robed figure, whose face was hidden by a mask, he was chained to the ground. The second was an unremarkable woman in street clothes. Giger informed them of the ritual, the fate of the Eater Codex, and why he had spared Virgil. Archanid and the other woman were obviously upset that the Codex had been stolen, but Arachnid praised his willingness to not kill Virgil, \u201cThe Guardians need mages who hold to their morals, not attack dogs.\u201d Giger was welcomed as a member of the Guardians of the Veil and Arachnid left. The woman told Giger that the masked and chained man was a Goetia who would help Giger learn the secret of making his own Masque.<br /> <br /> Giger meditated into the Astral and was standing on top of a skyscraper, looking down over an egg shaped realm. A river split the egg down the middle before splitting again at both ends, making four sections; the section he was in, a far section, and a middle section that had been split in two. He did not explore his Oneiros and instead, with the help of the goetia, created his first Masque.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-12-2025, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T11:13:47-08:00","id":1556171,"title":"","content":"I forgot to add <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Art/comments/lqgnv6/goddess_and_protector_me_digital_2020/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, the art that inspired the Omni-Caste","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T16:32:29-08:00","id":1556207,"title":"","content":"Entering into an Exarchal Verge was very bold, the Beria conversation sounded tricky, glad it worked out. I wonder if <i>Influence</i> <i>Electricity</i> could have saved them a camera repair bill. The Omni-Castle looks cool and ominous, hope it returns at some point.<br /> <br /> Asking a summon on the posthumous wishes of the dead is cool, and very thematic. I wonder if the summon can be bargained with for the location of Mictlan.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> <br /> The idea of a Vergil and Dante cycle of inheritance is pretty cool, with knowledge being passed down the generations. Reminds me of a less deadly Rule of Two.<br /> <br /> &quot;Giger didn't kill Vergil, he didn't cross the Black Veil, but for good reason<i> nods approvingly</i> &quot;<br /> &quot;He also turned in forbidden knowledge&quot;<br /> &quot;That's true&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Giger thanking his lucky stars they didn\u2019t hear about the Paradox he released in his apartment. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T16:41:07-08:00","id":1556579,"title":"","content":"Last chapter of 2025!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chapter 66</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">12/12/2025</span><br /> <br /> Upon waking Maxwell, Ragnar, and Delver each learned through the news that The Shadow That Walks had returned, and they had struck Giger's apartment. They all learned he was okay, but that a book he had stolen on behalf of the Guardians of the Veil had been taken by the Shadow That Walks the previous night before he could hand it over. Leopold spoke with the police, as Giger was supposed to have committed suicide in the bombing before. Special Agent Olivia Miller was on sight and seemed suspicious of this but without any sight of Giger she didn\u2019t push Leopold, instead she instructed him to find a new place to stay for a few nights while her people conducted their investigation. <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;Good thing the cabal had moved Eye of God's body to his apartment to meet with Alpha Centauri.&gt;</span> Giger got himself a cheap hotel to lay low in and contacted Chronos. They discussed what happened and Chronos asked if Giger planned to return to Los Angeles for this, but Giger told him he'd still be in Japan. Chronos then reminded him that his mother wanted to come visit and that he should make sure he is in Japan when she does, implying something that Giger was unable to pick up on. When the rest of the cabal arrived at Giger's hotel he talked them out of investigating this theft as he was much more interested in bringing Eye of God back. So the cabal agreed to meet at an old rural cemetery that night to summon the Mausoleum, a Shade that Ragnar knew about that could create a ghost and compel it to answer questions to the summoner in exchange for the summoner being willing to be haunted.<br /> <br /> During the day Giger and Raganr both took mana from their hallows while Maxwell, starved for mana since his hallow had stopped producing mana, went to Otakus Anonymous to draw on the mana from Eye of God's old Hallow. He drained it all by reading from the full collection of Fullmetal Alchemist and then purchased some heat up ramen which the tass had settled in. He left without asking the woman behind that counter, who was an old friend of Eye of God, why she seemed so exhausted.<br /> <br /> In the Graveyard that night the summoning was simple. Maxwell used Forces magic to hide the ritual, which only took three hours to complete with Ragnar leading. The Mausoleum rose from the earth, a fifteen foot tall structure of black marble. With it came a slab of the same marble, which Ragnar wrote Eye of God's name on. The stone started to fall off, like ice melting and sliding away, until a human form was made from the stone. Then the sound of a chisel could be heard as details were carved into the stone. The whole ordeal took nearly twenty minutes, but at the end a black marble statue of Eye of God stood before the cabal. Ragnar asked his question; \u201cDo you want to return to the living?\u201d Eye of God responded with, \u201cSure, why not?\u201d With the question asked, the Mausoleum returned to the Supernal and Eye of God remained, a ghost, haunting Ragnar.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\">&lt;The rest of the session was research on Typhon and Mictlan, with Ragnar discovering a path to the Whorl and Giger making contact with Crypt to learn about Mictlan. Legends were given about Mictlan and a recent discovery made by Crown of Lead was shared, but Crypt informed the cabal that the Lantern Keepers were trying to find the way to Mictlan to protect it from Seers, so if they discovered it that had to swear not to tell anyone about it. In the end though only Maxwell wanted to return to the Underworld for over a month, and the cabal decided to seek out Typhon instead.&gt;</span><br /> <br /> Before splitting up Maxwell decided to help teach Delver magic by exposing him, forcefully, to the Aether with an Apocalypse spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T21:54:51-08:00","id":1558522,"title":"","content":"We've been busy and only got on session in, and honestly not enough happened in it for me to take the time to write up a whole summary, so this coming session on Friday will have a quick summary for chapter 67 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}